lt0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The installation program will present you with an up-to-date list of video adapters\line supported by the version of the software you have.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb317\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 The Installation Program}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri4\sb202\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To install \b Smalltalk/V, \b0 make sure that the directory currently logged on the screen is\line your directory containing the \b Smalitalk/V \b0 files.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi-385\ri0\sb25\sa0\sl-400\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Now enter the following command:\line \b\expndtw-4 install}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb119\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 When you hit \b return \b0 or \b enter, \b0 the installation program displays a list of supported video\line \expndtw-1 adapters. Enter the number corresponding to your hardware configuration followed by\line the \b return \b0 or \b enter \b0 key.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri4\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The installation program performs two functions. First \i it \i0 records your hardware\line \expndtw-2 configuration in the file go in the current directory. Second, it decompresses all of the\line \b\expndtw-1 Smalltalk/V \b0 files from the distribution archives. Then the archive files are deleted.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri4\sb148\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 If your hardward configuration changes, you can run the installation program again. Since\line \expndtw0 the archive files have been deleted, only the first function is performed.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb364\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Starting Up Smalltalk/V}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri4\sb220\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Do not try to run \b Smalltalk/V \b0 unless you have already installed the \b Smalltalk/V\line \b0\expndtw-5 program.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri4\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To start up \b Smalltalk/V, \b0 make sure that the current directory displayed on the screen is\line \expndtw0 the directory holding \b Smalltalk/V \b0 programs.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb133\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Now enter the following command and hit \b return \b0 or \b enter:}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1208\margrsxn1946\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-126\shptop1613\shpright-126\shpbottom4702\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-32\shptop3017\shpright-32\shpbottom4515\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1156\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 24    Chapter 2: Introduction to the Smalltalk/ V286 Environment}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1148\fi0\ri0\sb706\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Smalltalk/V \b0 then loads. When \b Smalltalk/V \b0 is ready to run, it will display the start-up\line \expndtw-4 screen below:}\par \pard \plain \li2178\ri2725\sb389\sa0{\pict\picw6794\pich838\picwgoal3852\pichgoal475\jpegblip
}\par\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1548\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 I-beam}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1537\fi0\ri0\sb54\sa0\sl-472\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 window-\line \expndtw-2 cursor\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\f2\cchs0 \'97}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1544\fi0\ri0\sb227\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 background}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1552\fi0\ri0\sb950\sa482\sl-223\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Figure 2.1\line \expndtw3 Start Up Screen}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1208\margrsxn1946\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw720\colsr421\colno2\colw7614\linebetcol \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb734\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex58\expndtw11\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 : i}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Exiting Smalltalk/V}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb220\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To exit \b Smalltalk/V \b0 and return to DOS, move the cursor to the background and click\line \expndtw-2 the right mouse button to bring up the \b system menu. \b0 Select the \b exit Smalltalk \b0 item by\line \expndtw0 moving the cursor down the menu and clicking the left mouse button when the cursor\line \expndtw1 is over your choice on the menu. The menu shown below will pop up on the screen:}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2759\margrsxn3134\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\pard\plain \sb616\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2759\margrsxn3134\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw867\colsr4428\colno2\colw720 \pard \plain \li0\ri0\sb0\sa0\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx1879\posnegy0\absw0\absh3305\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\pict\picw4686\pich5829\picwgoal2656\pichgoal3304\jpegblip
}\par\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb2894\sa0\sl-223\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 2.2\line \expndtw-8 Exit Menu}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb882\sa0\sl-130\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 continue\line \expndtw-7 mawe iaage}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2435\margrsxn1867\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 2: Introduction to the Smalltalk/ V286 Environment    25}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li14\fi0\ri0\sb310\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 This menu asks you whether or not to save your changes. For now, choose \b forget image;\line \b0 since you haven't done any programming yet, you don't have anything you need to save.\line \expndtw-2 Later, when you are actually programming in \b Smalltalk/V, \b0 you'll want to save your\line \expndtw-1 changes after each \b Smalltalk/V \b0 session.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb378\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Getting Around}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri4\sb227\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To get around the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 environment, you must open up and close windows,\line \expndtw-2 make selections from popped-up menus and move the cursor using a mouse or your\line \expndtw-4 keyboard.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb346\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-12\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 The Cursor}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri4\sb202\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The cursor is your pointer on the screen. It tells \b Smalltalk/V \b0 where you are going to do\line \expndtw-4 something like pop-up a menu. You can move the cursor by dragging your mouse in the\line \expndtw-3 direction you want it to move or by using the cursor keys on the numeric keypad. When\line using the keypad, you can move the cursor in larger amounts by holding down the \b shift\line \b0\expndtw-1 key while pressing down on a cursor key.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb342\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 The I-beam}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri11\sb202\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The insertion point or I-beam is a special text marker that is used when editing text\line \expndtw-3 strings. It appears in a text window or pane and marks the spot where new text will be\line \expndtw-1 inserted or deleted.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb385\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Working with Your Mouse}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri11\sb223\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Using a mouse is the easiest way to get around the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 environment. With your\line \expndtw-3 mouse you can quickly move between windows and background, text and menus by\line \expndtw1 dragging the mouse and clicking the correct button.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb346\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-16\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 Mouse Buttons}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri7\sb205\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Your mouse has two buttons. The right button "administrates" your way around the\line \expndtw1 environment. Use the right button to bring up menus for selection and for scrolling\line \expndtw-3 within a window pane. The left button "selects" things for \b Smalltalk/V \b0 to execute. Use\line \expndtw-1 the \b left \b0 button to choose specific menu items, text or text lines, and objects from \b a \b0 list.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2297\margrsxn2002\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 26    Chapter 2: Introduction to the Smalltalk/ V286 Environment}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb356\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Mouse-key Equivalents}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb191\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 If you do not want to use a mouse, you can use your keyboard keys to get around the\line \expndtw-3 Smalltalk/V environment. Throughout this chapter you will find specific instructions for\line \expndtw0 using the keyboard. For more keyboard instructions, refer to Chapter 15.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb378\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Windows and Menus}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri4\sb209\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Smalltalk/V \b0 is a menu-driven system. You give commands to the environment by\line \expndtw1 selecting things from a menu of possible things to do. There are several different\line \expndtw-1 windows and menus available in the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 environment.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri0\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 This section of the chapter introduces the windows and menus of the \b Smalltalk/V\line \b0\expndtw-3 standard window set. You will first learn some general information about windows and\line \expndtw0 menus and then you will take a \b Quick \b0 Tour of the main \b Smalltalk/V \b0 windows and\line menus. For more detailed reading, see Chapters 15 and 16 in \b Part \b0 3 of this manual.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb389\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Windows}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri4\sb220\sa986\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A window is an object with a border, label bar, window buttons and one or more panes\line \expndtw0 and pop-up menus as shown in Figure 2.3. A window can be active or non-active.\line Windows can be opened, closed, collapsed, resized and moved around on the screen.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2297\margrsxn2002\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720 \pard \plain \li0\ri0\sb0\sa0\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx331\posnegy0\absw0\absh3327\nowrap\dfrmtxtx10080\dfrmtxty0 {\pict\picw11709\pich5867\picwgoal6638\pichgoal3326\jpegblip
}\par\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx331\posnegy2689\absw1527\absh-655\nowrap\dfrmtxtx10080\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 2.3\line \expndtw-2 Workspace and\line \expndtw-4 Popped Up Menu}\par {\pard\plain \sb0\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2444\margrsxn1840\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 2: Introduction to the Smalltalk/ V286 Environment    21}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li22\fi0\ri0\sb349\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Label Bar}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri0\sb216\sa533\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Each window has its own label bar and menu. We will say more about menus a little\line \expndtw-2 further on. The window title is displayed on the label bar along with one or more small\line \expndtw-1 buttons, depending on which \b Smalltalk/V \b0 window is open. The buttons provide quick\line \expndtw-2 access to specific window activities.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn5616\margrsxn2632\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1515\colsr1170\colno2\colw975 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-1775\shptop-101\shpright-1775\shpbottom605\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 13970}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-1660\shptop-22\shpright-1660\shpbottom489\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 15875}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-1177\shptop-22\shpright-1177\shpbottom489\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 15875}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2639\shptop-14\shpright2639\shpbottom497\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 15875}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft3726\shptop-14\shpright3726\shpbottom497\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 15875}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft3848\shptop-14\shpright3848\shpbottom497\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 15875}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft4324\shptop-14\shpright4324\shpbottom504\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 18415}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs38 Label Bar}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb54\sa0\sl-374\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex121\expndtw-29\dn7\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs58 Z \dbch\af2\loch\af0\hich\f0\cchs0 \u9633\'3f}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn5238\margrsxn4266\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\pard\plain \sb396\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn5238\margrsxn4266\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw720\colsr965\colno2\colw720\linebetcol \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb7\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 close}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 zoom}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2444\margrsxn1840\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4810\fi0\ri0\sb230\sa29 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 collapse}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2804\margrsxn3092\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw3553\colsr1739\colno2\colw720\linebetcol \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 2.4}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Window Label Bar with Window Buttons}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb245\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 resize}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2444\margrsxn1840\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri4\sb400\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Close Button: \b0 When selected, the window closes and disappears from the screen. To\line \expndtw-2 close the window, place the cursor onto the close button and click the left mouse button\line \expndtw3 or use the numeric keypad \b + \b0 key.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri7\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Zoom Button: \b0 When selected, \b Smalltalk/V \b0 zooms in on the text pane so that it fills the\line \expndtw-2 whole screen. To select the zoom button, place the cursor onto the button and click the\line \expndtw-1 left mouse button or use the numeric keypad + key. To unzoom the text pane, click on\line \expndtw-2 the label bar and the window redraws to its original configuration. You can also use the\line \expndtw2 F8 function key to zoom a text pane.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri11\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Collapse Button: \b0 When selected, the window collapses to show only the label bar. If the\line window is already collapsed, selecting this button expands the window to its original size\line \expndtw1 and position on the screen. To select the collapse button, place the cursor onto the\line \expndtw3 button and click the left mouse button or use the numeric keypad \b + \b0 key.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri7\sb144\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Resize Button: \b0 Select this button and the system responds with a rectangle outline for\line \expndtw0 resizing the window. You can resize the window using either the mouse or keyboard.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li630\fi0\ri11\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 With a Mouse: \i0 Be sure that the cursor is on the resize button. Press and hold down\line \expndtw-3 the left mouse button while you move the mouse to drag the cursor and resize the\line \expndtw-2 rectangle outline. Release the mouse button and the window redraws to its new\line \expndtw-12 size.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2266\margrsxn2015\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 28    Chapter 2: Introduction to the Smalltalk/V286 Environment}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li644\fi0\ri0\sb313\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 With the Keypad; \i0 With the cursor on the resize button, press and release the\line \expndtw1 numeric keypad + key. Use the keyboard cursor keys to move the cursor and\line \expndtw-2 resize the rectangle outline. Once again, press and release the numeric keypad +\line \expndtw0 key and the window redraws \i to \i0 its new \i size.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb338\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-14\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 Pane}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri0\sb209\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Each window has one or more panes, depending upon which \b Smalltalk/V \b0 window is\line \expndtw-2 open. Each pane also has a menu. The \b pane \b0 is the workspace for programming in\line \b\expndtw-3 Smailtalk/V. \b0 Here you select items from lists using the left mouse button, insert and edit\line \expndtw-1 text strings using the I-beam, and select and evaluate \b Smallralk/V \b0 programming code.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri4\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Each pane also has a \b scroll bar \b0 and cursor available for scrolling through all the text\line \expndtw-4 contained in the pane as shown in Figure 2.5. You can bring up the scroll bar by pointing\line \expndtw-1 the cursor onto the pane and holding down the right mouse button. We will discuss\line \expndtw0 scrolling in greater detail a little further on.}\par \pard \plain \li1994\ri256\sb454\sa0{\pict\picw9486\pich1079\picwgoal5378\pichgoal612\jpegblip
}\par\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa97 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 reversed label bar}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2684\margrsxn3037\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw813\colsr1969\colno2\colw3405 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft1879\shptop-698\shpright1879\shpbottom2600\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 13970}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2477\shptop-324\shpright2477\shpbottom1987\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft6804\shptop-324\shpright6804\shpbottom2002\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 57150}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb374\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 scroll bar}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li133\fi-133\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-133\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 This is Map la text. It Mill scroll upward and out\line \expndtw-6 of sight as you click and drag the Mouse downward\line \expndtw-7 within this pans.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2266\margrsxn2015\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-785\shptop144\shpright-785\shpbottom871\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb191\sa623 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 scroll cursor}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2680\margrsxn2771\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1494\colsr1292\colno2\colw3672 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft1818\shptop-158\shpright1818\shpbottom893\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb184\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 2.5}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Pane}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 with Scroll Bar}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 and Scroll Cursor}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li137\fi-137\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-133\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 Scrolling Mill cause this text to Move upward in this\line \expndtw-6 pane, revealing the text which is below and currently}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2266\margrsxn2015\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb331\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-15\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Menus}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri7\sb223\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 There are many menus in the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 environment. A menu is an object containing\line a list of choices relevant to a particular window, pane or other object. Menus are hidden\line \expndtw-4 behind windows, panes and the system screen. You can make a menu visible by popping\line \expndtw2 up the menu using the mouse or keypad.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2363\margrsxn1931\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 2: Introduction to the Smalltalk! V286 Environment   29}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb349\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Popping up Menus}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri11\sb220\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To pop up a menu, position the cursor over the object hiding the menu. Then, click the\line \expndtw2 right mouse button or press the Del key on the keyboard. The menu pops up.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb346\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Selecting from a Menu}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri11\sb216\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To select an item from a menu, move the cursor over the item you wish to select. Click\line \expndtw3 the left mouse button or press the + key on the numeric keypad.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb353\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Hiding a Menu}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri11\sb212\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 If you are using a mouse, move the cursor outside of the menu and click either mouse\line \expndtw-4 button. The menu disappears. If you are using a keypad, use the cursor keys to move the\line \expndtw0 cursor out of the menu and the menu automatically disappears.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb349\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Finding Different Menus}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri11\sb216\sa875\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Smalltalk/V \b0 has many different kinds of menus some of which are shown in Figure 2.6.\line \expndtw-2 What kind of menu you get depends on where the cursor is when you pop it up. If the\line \expndtw-4 cursor is outside of every window, the system menu is popped up. When the cursor is on\line \expndtw-1 the window label bar, a window menu pops up. When the cursor is on a pane, a pane\line \expndtw1 menu specific to that pane pops up.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2774\margrsxn3019\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1238\colsr3949\colno2\colw928 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft4450\shptop50\shpright4450\shpbottom3326\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 13970}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft5162\shptop1094\shpright5162\shpbottom2361\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft6120\shptop1094\shpright6120\shpbottom2376\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 25400}}}}{\pard\plain \sb0\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\pard \plain \li0\ri0\sb0\sa0\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx1872\posnegy0\absw0\absh1944\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\pict\picw4546\pich3429\picwgoal2577\pichgoal1944\jpegblip
}\par\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb29\sa0\sl-544\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-12\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 window menu\line \expndtw-8 pane menu \b0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0 \'97}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb428\sa0\sl-202\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 secondary\line \expndtw-4 pane menu}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb187\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 system menu}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb1105\sa0\sl-133\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 dos shell\line speed/space\line \expndtw-7 exit Smalltalk}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-25\shptop0\shpright990\shpbottom0\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 8890}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-133\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 browse disk\line \expndtw-7 open workspace\line broMse classes\line \expndtw-5 redraw screen}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-25\shptop4\shpright976\shpbottom4\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-133\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 save iMage\line run deMo}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2774\margrsxn4876\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\pard\plain \sb155\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2774\margrsxn4876\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1299\colsr630\colno2\colw2329 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft5141\shptop-180\shpright6178\shpbottom-180\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 22860}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft1894\shptop-2376\shpright1894\shpbottom821\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 13970}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft1872\shptop-2254\shpright1872\shpbottom439\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb216\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 2.6\line \expndtw-7 Different Kinds\line \expndtw-6 of Menus}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li198\fi-198\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-133\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 Sane "^Q have choices which lead\line \expndtw-6 to additional pop up Menus\line offering More selections such as\line \expndtw-8 the ' next aenu' iteM in the\line \expndtw-7 Transcript pane Menu above.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2313\margrsxn1979\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li22\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 30    Chapter 2: Introduction to the Smalltalk/ V286 Environment}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li22\fi0\ri0\sb378\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 The System Menu}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri4\sb209\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The system menu lets you open new windows and perform system level functions, such\line \expndtw0 as exiting \b Smalltalk/V \b0 or redrawing the screen.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri7\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To find this menu, place the cursor outside any window onto the screen background.\line \expndtw2 Then click the right mouse button or press the \b Del \b0 key.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb335\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 The Window Menu}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri0\sb205\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The window menu lets you manipulate the window as a whole. For example, you can\line \expndtw-3 resize the window by selecting \b frame \b0 from the menu. Or you can deactivate the active\line \expndtw1 window and activate the window behind it by selecting \b cycle \b0 from the menu.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri4\sb144\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To quickly find this menu from any part of the window, press the \b Ins \b0 key. Or, you can\line \expndtw-3 place the cursor over the window label bar, and click the right mouse button or press the\line \b\expndtw-1 Del \b0 key.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb342\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 The Pane Menu}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri11\sb205\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The pane menu lets you manipulate the contents of the window pane. For example you\line \expndtw0 can evaluate selected \b Smalltalk/V \b0 code by choosing \b show it \b0 or \b do it \b0 from the pane\line \expndtw1 menu. Or, you can edit selected \b Smalltalk/V \b0 code by choosing \b copy, cut or paste.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri11\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To find this menu, place the cursor anywhere inside the window pane and click the right\line \expndtw2 mouse button or press the \b Del \b0 key.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb320\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex83\expndtw-2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Using Menus: Running the Demonstration Program}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri7\sb212\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To get you started, we've included a demonstration program, showing you how to use\line \expndtw2 menus and \i move \i0 the cursor. To start the demonstration program, move the cursor\line \expndtw1 outside of all of the windows, and pop up the menu. You should see the following\line \expndtw-8 screen:}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2484\margrsxn1797\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3182\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa346 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 2: Introduction to the Smalltalk/ V286 Environment    31}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2841\margrsxn2949\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1551\colsr3636\colno2\colw932 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2023\shptop-29\shpright2477\shpbottom-29\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft3060\shptop-14\shpright4241\shpbottom-14\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 2540}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft5162\shptop1001\shpright5162\shpbottom2167\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 8890}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft6120\shptop1001\shpright6120\shpbottom2167\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 22860}}}}{\pard\plain \sb0\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\pard \plain \li0\ri0\sb0\sa0\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx1958\posnegy0\absw0\absh3290\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\pict\picw4699\pich5803\picwgoal2664\pichgoal3290\jpegblip
}\par\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx2419\posnegy47\absw0\absh-141\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 S\loch\af16\hich\af16\dbch\f17\cchs0 \'bb\hich\af16\dbch\af17\loch\f16\cchs0 alltalk/V Transcript     [Z]tLI}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb2923\sa0\sl-212\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 2.7\line Starting the Demo}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb1008\sa0\sl-133\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 dos shell\line speed/space\line \expndtw-2 exit Smlltalk}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-40\shptop11\shpright990\shpbottom11\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-137\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 browse disk\line \expndtw-7 open workspace\line browse classes\line \expndtw-6 redraw screen}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-32\shptop4\shpright976\shpbottom4\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 8890}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 save iwage}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2484\margrsxn1797\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li18\fi0\ri0\sb421\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Now select the item \b run demo \b0 from the menu. (If \b run \b0 demo is not on the menu, you\line \expndtw-2 didn't have the cursor outside of all the windows when you popped up the menu. Try\line \expndtw-1 again.) When you select \b run demo, \b0 you'll see a special menu:}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2484\margrsxn1807\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \li0\ri0\sb0\sa0\pvpara\phcol\posnegx2308\posnegy277\absw0\absh3362\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\pict\picw9448\pich5930\picwgoal5356\pichgoal3362\jpegblip
}\par\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li364\fi0\ri0\sb3280\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 2.8\line Running the Demo}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb248\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 When you select any item from this menu, the demonstration program draws a\line \expndtw0 corresponding picture. For example, select \b mandala \b0 and a mandala is drawn on the\line \expndtw-3 screen. Select \b ball \b0 and you'll see a little greater program complexity. As you move the\line \expndtw-1 cursor, the ball moves differently. The ball moves faster when you move the cursor\line \expndtw2 towards the bottom of the screen, and slower when the cursor is near the top.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb130\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To leave the demo, select the exit item from the demo menu.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1438\margrsxn1942\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw720\colsr169\colno2\colw7639\linebetcol \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb11858\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-21\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Ill.}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li25\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 32    Chapter 2: Introduction to the Smalltalk/ V286 Environment}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb346\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Working with Windows}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri22\sb227\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Windows provide the main interface between Smalltalk/V and you. For example, you\line \expndtw-2 use the \b Class Hierarchy Browser \b0 window to enter programs into the system and the\line \b\expndtw-4 Disk Browser \b0 window to browse and manipulate files. A window can be opened, closed,\line \expndtw0 collapsed, resized and moved about on the screen.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb353\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Opening a Window}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri22\sb209\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A window must be open before it can be activated. When you first start up \b Smalltalk/V,\line \b0\expndtw-1 the \b System Transcript Window \b0 is opened. To open other \b Smalltalk/V \b0 windows you\line \expndtw-2 make selections from specific menus.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 For example when you select \b browse disk \b0 from the \b System Menu \b0 the \b Disk Browser\line \expndtw1 Window \b0\i is \i0 opened. Or select \b browse classes \b0 from the same menu and the \b Class\line \expndtw-2 Hierarchy Browser \b0 window opens at a default size appropriate to the window type. If\line \expndtw2 you want to change the size of a window, use the resize button on the label bar.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb356\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Activating a Window}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri22\sb216\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Although there may be many windows visible on the screen at one time, only one of them\line \expndtw1 can be active. To use a window, you need to activate it.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri22\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To activate a window, move the cursor over some portion \i of \i0 the window and click the\line left mouse button or press the + key on the numeric keypad. \b Smalltalk/V \b0 reverses the\line \expndtw2 color of the label bar to show that the window is active and ready for use.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb360\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Deactivating a Window}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri18\sb212\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 You can deactivate a window by selecting another window on the screen. Click on the\line inactive window and its label bar reverses color to show it is active as the old window\line \expndtw-3 becomes deactivated.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri29\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 If there are no other windows visible on the screen, move the cursor outside the window.\line \expndtw-2 Then click either the left mouse button or press the + key on the numeric keypad. This\line \expndtw0 deactivates the window on the screen.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2492\margrsxn1791\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 2: Introduction to the Smalltalk/ V286 Environment    33}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li25\fi0\ri0\sb310\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex83\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Resizing a Window}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li14\fi0\ri0\sb212\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 An active window can be resized to your own taste or to allow you to view more than\line \expndtw-2 one window at a time on the screen. You can resize a window by selecting the \b resize\line button \b0 from the label bar and dragging the cursor to resize the window, or by selecting\line \b\expndtw0 frame \b0 from the window menu and following the same procedure.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li22\fi0\ri0\sb313\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex83\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Closing a Window}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li18\fi0\ri4\sb205\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 When you are finished with a window, you may close it. To close a window you can\line \expndtw1 either select the \b close window button \b0 on the window label bar, or \b close \b0 from the\line \expndtw-2 window menu.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li22\fi0\ri0\sb324\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex83\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Moving a Window}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li18\fi0\ri14\sb202\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 You can move windows. This is useful when you have collapsed or resized windows and\line \expndtw1 you want to reposition them on the screen.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri7\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 You can move a window in three ways. 1) Select move from the window menu. Then\line drag the cursor and its attached window outline, to its new position and click the left\line \expndtw-2 mouse button. The window is redrawn in its new location. 2) Place the cursor on the\line \expndtw-4 window label bar then press and hold the left mouse button. Drag the mouse and relocate\line \expndtw-1 the window on the screen. 3) Select \b move \b0 from the window menu using the 4- key on\line the numeric keypad. After the cursor grabs the window frame, use the cursor keys to\line \expndtw0 move and reposition the window. Press the + key again and the window is redrawn in\line \expndtw-1 its new location.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb374\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Quick-Tour-Windows and Menus}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri14\sb216\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Part of the enjoyment of programming in \b Smalltalk\b0 /V is that you have lots of freedom\line \expndtw0 to experiment. To whet your appetite, a \b Quick Tour \b0 of the main windows and menus\line \expndtw-2 of the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 environment can be found on the following pages. You can use \b the\line Quick Tour \b0 to preview the environment or as a roadmap in case you get lost. Detailed\line \expndtw-1 information on the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 windows and menus is found in Chapter 15 in \b Part \b0 3\line of this manual.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2300\margrsxn1977\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li68\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa500 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 34    Chapter 2: Introduction to the Smalltalk/ V286 Environment}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn5032\margrsxn4637\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1461\colsr58\colno2\colw720\linebetcol \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 Smalltalk/U Transcript}\par \column {\pard\plain \sb0\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-187\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx187\posnegy25\absw0\absh-191\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-12\dn4\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs42 zm}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri425\sb0\sa0\sl-130\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 cole\line \expndtw-10 cycl\line \expndtw1 fram\line \expndtw-6 Move}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn5479\margrsxn3017\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\pard\plain \sb677\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn5479\margrsxn3017\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw720\colsr1757\colno2\colw936\linebetcol {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft1051\shptop-662\shpright1447\shpbottom-662\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 20320}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-22\