\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 Snoopy run inside kennel}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1150\margrsxn1845\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\pard\plain \sb342\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1150\margrsxn1845\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw720\colsr558\colno2\colw7635 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li25\fi0\ri0\sb5209\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex49\expndtw16\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 !  i}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb2153\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex69\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs38 k}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Try composing your own scripts in the input pane, and then select either all or a portion\line \expndtw2 of it to play.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb367\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 What YouVe Now Learned}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri4\sb227\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 By the end of this tutorial, you should be familiar with prompters, single pane windows,\line \expndtw-4 and multi-pane windows. You've seen a complex interactive application, which provides\line \expndtw0 many of Smalltalk's most important building blocks.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri4\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 As always, if you want to review any of the topics covered in this tutorial, you can either\line \expndtw0 repeat the corresponding section of the tutorial, or refer to the detailed description in\line \b\expndtw-5 Part \b0 3.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri11\sb166\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 If you are going to exit \b Smalltalk/ V \b0 before proceeding on to the next tutorial, be sure\line \expndtw0 to save the image.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1993\margrsxn2295\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li25\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs30 11 OBJECT-ORIENTED DEVELOPMENT}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb454\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The tutorials so far have shown you many strengths of the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 language and\line programming environment. Chapters 11 and 12 are about \b Smalltalk/V \b0 application\line \expndtw-3 development\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0 \'97\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0 the "how" rather than the "what" of OOPS. In Chapter 11, you will learn\line \expndtw0 the OOPS application development cycle, a methodology which will guide you in\line designing and implementing your own \b Smalltalk/V \b0 applications. The process is\line demonstrated through a simple but complete example.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 After working through the phone book example in this chapter, you will be ready for the\line more complex application in Chapter 12. There, a multi-window, multi-pane application\line \expndtw-1 involving state-transition data management is developed using \b Smalltalk/V \b0 in a case\line \expndtw0 study of the development of an office information system.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb378\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 The Smalltalk/V Application Development Cycle}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri4\sb223\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Smalltalk/V \b0 application development involves defining objects, their interrelationships\line and their behavior. Together with the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 environment, these problem solving\line \expndtw-2 techniques support an incremental and evolutionary approach to software development.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri7\sb140\sa0\sl-245\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The \b Smalltalk/V \b0 application development process can be generally divided into six\line \expndtw-7 phases:}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx623 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx623 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent220\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 State the Problem}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx623 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx623 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent220\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Draw the Window}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx623 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx623 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent220\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Identify the Classes}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx623 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx623 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent220\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Describe Object States}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx623 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx623 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent220\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 List the Object Interfaces}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx623 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx623 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent220\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Implement the Methods}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb353\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 State the Problem}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri7\sb212\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Begin your \b Smalltalk/V \b0 application development project by making as explicit and\line \expndtw0 cogent a problem statement as possible, describing what you are trying to get your\line \expndtw-1 software to do. For example:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi0\ri403\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Problem Statement: There are many people I call regularly on the phone, so I\line \expndtw0 will create a window application which maintains a list of people and their\line \expndtw1 phone numbers. The phone book list will be sorted in alphabetical order.\line \expndtw-3 Selecting a name will retrieve the associated phone number. Names and phone\line \expndtw2 numbers can be added to and deleted from the list.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2290\margrsxn1977\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li47\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex79\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 156    Chapter \expndtw31 11:\expndtw6  Object-Oriented Development}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li18\fi0\ri22\sb324\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 As you think through and learn more about your problem, you can return to the problem\line statement to qualify or extend it, refining application goals as you go along. The purpose\line here is to have a short, understandable statement of the problem which points toward the\line \expndtw0 kind of software solution that will address your need.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li18\fi0\ri0\sb144\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Your problem statement, like your \b Smalltalk/V \b0 application, will evolve. The act of\line \expndtw0 bringing your initial design ideas to life will generate insights that enhance your\line \expndtw-1 appreciation for the original problem.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li22\fi0\ri0\sb353\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Draw the Window}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li14\fi0\ri22\sb216\sa439\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Armed with your problem statement, ask yourself what a new window that helps solve\line \expndtw-2 your problem looks like, then draw it. Don's worry about the internal workings of the\line \expndtw-3 application and data structures involved. Concentrate on the appearance and interaction.\line \expndtw-2 What does the application look like? How does it behave? What existing \b Smalltalk/V\line \b0\expndtw0 windows have you seen that suggest an approach?}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2635\margrsxn2405\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1328\colsr2984\colno2\colw2556 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft7254\shptop4\shpright7254\shpbottom2790\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 13970}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft7024\shptop1105\shpright7024\shpbottom2934\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 52705}}}}{\pard\plain \sb0\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx4021\posnegy0\absw0\absh-381\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex80\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs32 Mi/ ?hone Book}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx2416\posnegy1998\absw0\absh-388\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex80\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs32 Andy Jlwerson}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx6037\posnegy2524\absw0\absh-303\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex81\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 neyp menu}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2243\shptop25\shpright4266\shpbottom2228\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr5\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 75}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn pib}{\sv {\pict\picw3568\pich3886\picwgoal2023\pichgoal2203\jpegblip
}}}{\sp{\sn pictureGray}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn pWrapPolygonVertices}{\sv 8;17;(0,0);(0,4023);(0,4023);(0,19764);(0,19764);(0,19976);(0,19976);(0,21600);(2690,21600);(2690,19976);(2997,19976);(2997,19764);(21600,19764);(21600,4023);(2690,4023);(2690,0);(0,0)}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fIsBullet}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fAllowOverlap}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fEditedWrap}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fBehindDocument}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fPrint}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn dxWrapDistLeft}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn dxWrapDistRight}{\sv 0}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb2398\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 11.1\line \b\expndtw1 PhoneBook}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Window Model}\par \column {\pard\plain \sb0\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx1732\posnegy695\absw0\absh-277\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 restore}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb36\sa0\sl-299\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 125 Maple Street\line \expndtw13 tastWontuck MN'61222}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li29\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-281\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx1699\posnegy90\absw544\absh-882\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-17\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 copif}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li25\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-281\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx1699\posnegy90\absw544\absh-882\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 cut}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-281\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx1699\posnegy90\absw544\absh-882\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 paste}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx1717\posnegy943\absw0\absh-277\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 saw}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-562\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw16\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 612-555-4521\line \expndtw-11 friend of the fa/nilif}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2290\margrsxn1977\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri25\sb464\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 11.1 shows a proposed phone book window. Notice that it includes menu\line \expndtw-1 selections. Having an idea of the number, size and contents of the panes of the window\line \expndtw-3 in your application is obviously helpful, but it is through the menu selections that things\line come to life. Menu items are the means for you as user-object to send messages to your\line \expndtw0 application which is, after all, a \b Smalltalk/V \b0 object.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri32\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 You have now transformed your problem statement into a concrete window to be built.\line \expndtw-1 The drawing is a specification of the application user interface and is the starting point\line \expndtw0 for specifying the rest of the application.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1906\margrsxn2364\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 Chapter \expndtw51 II:\expndtw7  Object-Oriented Development    157}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri14\sb306\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The next three phases consist of identifying classes, object state and object interfaces,\line \expndtw-3 and are by nature interrelated. Although they are described sequentially, it may be more\line \expndtw-1 productive to perform them in parallel or iteratively.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li22\fi0\ri0\sb342\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Identify the Classes}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri14\sb209\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Knowing as much as you can about your problem and having a sketch of the application\line interface, you are ready to identify the classes of objects that implement the application.\line \expndtw-2 List both the new classes defined for the application and existing classes from the\line \b\expndtw0 Smalltalk/V \b0 class hierarchy to be used. New classes will be either self-standing (a\line \expndtw-3 subclass of class \b Object), \b0 or a subclass of an existing class that implements some of the\line \expndtw-1 behavior needed by the new class. Existing classes used will generally include user\line \expndtw-3 interface classes \b (Menu \b0 and subclasses of \b Pane) \b0 and subclasses of \b Collection, Magni-\line \expndtw-4 tude \b0 and \b Stream.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri11\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 In our example, we need a new class \b PhoneBook \b0 whose instances are the phone book\line \expndtw-3 window application. Menus and panes appear in your window sketch, so classes \b Menu,\line \expndtw-4 ListPane, TextPane \b0 and \b TopPane \b0 are needed. After some consideration, it seems that a\line \b\expndtw1 Dictionary \b0 is most appropriate for associating names with telephone numbers, and\line \expndtw0 names and telephone numbers will be represented as \b Strings.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The classes identified so far seem like a natural breakdown of the problem statement and\line \expndtw-1 the window picture. But what if the choices aren't so obvious? It's important to make\line \expndtw-3 some choice, even if it's not the best. You may be wrong, but with an environment that\line \expndtw-1 allows you to make changes easily, you can change to better ones later. Any kind of\line \expndtw-3 progress on the application will enhance your understanding of the appropriate classes to\line \expndtw-2 be used.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb364\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Describe the Object States}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri18\sb209\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Given the problem statement, the window drawing and the classes to be used, what\line \expndtw-3 instance variables are needed in the new classes you have defined? In this example, our\line only new class is \b PhoneBook, \b0 which is the window model. What state is appropriate to\line put in a phone book object? The standard dispatcher and pane classes already keep track\line \expndtw0 of most of the state associated with the window. The model, an instance of class\line \b\expndtw-3 PhoneBook, \b0 needs the application specific data, which in this case are (l) the dictionary\line \expndtw3 of phone numbers \b phones \b0 and (2) the name from the selected list pane entry\line \expndtw-1 selectedName. Look in file \b chapter. 11 \b0 to see the resulting class definition.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri18\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Are there general rules for deciding what instance variables to use? The best guide is to\line \expndtw-2 look ahead to the object interface. What kind of questions (messages) will the object be\line \expndtw0 asked? What will be the object's behavior?}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2340\margrsxn1923\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li29\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex79\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 138    Chapter \expndtw31 11:\expndtw6  Object-Oriented Development}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb371\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 List the Object Interfaces}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri22\sb198\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Object interfaces are the messages that the object responds to. List the messages that the\line \expndtw-2 new classes must implement. A good starting point for this is to augment the window\line \expndtw0 drawing with the messages that will be used for each pane.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2675\margrsxn7341\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft4558\shptop2498\shpright4558\shpbottom3132\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 2540}}}}{\pard\plain \sb0\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\pard \plain \li0\ri0\sb0\sa0\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx5429\posnegy871\absw0\absh2325\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\pict\picw3340\pich4102\picwgoal1893\pichgoal2325\jpegblip
}\par\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx3978\posnegy1012\absw2124\absh-1559\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 Mi/ Phone Book}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li223\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx3978\posnegy1012\absw2124\absh-1559\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 123 Maple Street\line \expndtw6 EastWontuck MN 61222}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li227\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-414\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx3978\posnegy1012\absw2124\absh-1559\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 612-555-4521\line \expndtw-8 friend of the fam'ty}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx5483\posnegy1800\absw0\absh-208\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 restore}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-205\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx5479\posnegy1998\absw299\absh-414\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-13\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 copif\line \expndtw1 cut}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft1922\shptop662\shpright4183\shpbottom3362\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr5\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 75}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn pib}{\sv {\pict\picw3987\pich4762\picwgoal2260\pichgoal2700\jpegblip
}}}{\sp{\sn pictureGray}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn pWrapPolygonVertices}{\sv 8;9;(0,0);(0,5241);(0,5241);(0,21600);(21600,21600);(21600,5241);(19536,5241);(19536,0);(0,0)}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fIsBullet}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fAllowOverlap}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fEditedWrap}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fBehindDocument}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fPrint}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn dxWrapDistLeft}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn dxWrapDistRight}{\sv 0}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb2765\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 11.2\line \b\expndtw-2 PhoneBook \b0 Window\line \expndtw-5 with Messages}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2340\margrsxn1923\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb551\sa155\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 In Figure 11.2, the message names are circled. In general, messages are used for (1)\line \expndtw-3 accessing non-standard menus defined by the application, (2) accessing the contents of\line \expndtw-2 panes for display purposes, (3) saving the contents of changed panes, (4) carrying out\line \expndtw0 menu selections, and (5) opening the window. In our example we have the following:}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2729\margrsxn2154\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw2055\colsr104\colno2\colw4867 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li25\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 Message}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 add}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 list}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 list: aString}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 listMenu}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 openOn: aDictionary}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 remove}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 text}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 text: aString}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 from: aDispatcher}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li29\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 Purpose}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Add a new name to phone book.\line \expndtw1 Answer the list of names of people in the phone book.\line \expndtw0 Display the phone number for aString.\line \expndtw-1 Answer the name list menu.\line \expndtw1 Open a phone book window for aDictionary.\line Remove selected name from phone book.\line Answer the phone number for the selected name.\line Enter aString in dictionary as phone number for\line \expndtw-3 selected name.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1915\margrsxn2355\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter \expndtw21 11:\expndtw-2  Object-Oriented Development    159}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb328\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex83\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Implement the Methods}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri7\sb198\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 All that remains to do is to implement the methods. A good starting point for a window\line \expndtw-1 application is to do the window opening message (in our case, \b openOn:). \b0 This method\line \expndtw1 is generally the largest in your application. Here it is for the phone book:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb137\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 openOn: aDictionary}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li428\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 "Open a phone book window on aDictionary. Define\line \expndtw-1 the pane sizes and behavior and schedule the window."\line \expndtw-7 I topPane I}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 phones := aDictionary.\line \expndtw0 topPane : = TopPane new.\line \expndtw-2 topPane label: 'Phone Book'.\line \expndtw-7 topPane addSubpane:\line \expndtw-4 (ListPane new}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1202\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 menu: #listMenu;}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1199\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 model: self;}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1199\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 name: #list;}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1202\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 change: #list:;}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi385\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 framingRatio: (0 @ 0 extent: 1/3 @ 1)).\line \expndtw-5 topPane add Subpane:\line \ex