ndtw-2 file. The following expression files in class \b PhoneBook.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb126\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 (File pathName: 'chapter.!!') fileln}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2402\margrsxn1871\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li50\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 160    Chapter 11; Object-Oriented Development}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb194\sa0\sl-396\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 You will find it as the first expression in file \b chapter. 11.\line \b0\expndtw0 To try it out, evaluate:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li418\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-396\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 PhoneBook new openOn: Dictionary new}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li32\fi0\ri0\sb356\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Knowing When to Stop}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li14\fi0\ri4\sb230\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 During the first round of a new application development project, you generally progress\line through the above six steps sequentially. Once you have your "first cut" at a proposed\line \expndtw-1 application, your increased understanding will generate new insights. You will find\line \expndtw-3 yourself jumping around the six steps in a non-sequential process. For instance, while\line \expndtw-4 writing a method you realize the need for a class instance variable which brings you back\line \expndtw0 to state considerations.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri0\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Smalltalk/V's \b0 incremental compiling capabilities promote dynamic movement among\line \expndtw-4 these development steps. In face, \b Smalltalk/V \b0 application development can be seductive.\line \expndtw-3 It is always easy to think about adding just a few more lines of code which will further\line \expndtw-1 polish the application's interface or performance. By design, \b Smalltalk/V \b0 is an open\line system, an application always has the potential for enhancement.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 That is why it is important to refresh your memory as to the original design goals of your\line \b\expndtw2 Smalltalk/V \b0 application development project. If the prototype meets your design\line \expndtw-2 criteria, then stop. Use the application for a while and let experience guide subsequent\line \expndtw-3 enhancement.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb385\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 What YouVe Now Learned}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri11\sb227\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 You have seen the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 application development cycle applied to a very simple\line example. You have seen that a \b Smalltalk/V \b0 application develops in a revolving process\line \expndtw-4 which addresses:}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent209\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 State the Problem}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent209\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Draw the Window}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent209\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Identify the Classes}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent209\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Describe Object States}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent209\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 List the Object Interfaces}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent209\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Implement the Methods}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri11\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The next chapter will showcase the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 application development cycle in a\line \expndtw-3 more involved case study. As always, if you want to review any of the topics covered in\line \expndtw0 this tutorial, you can either repeat the corresponding section of the tutorial, or refer to\line the relevant topics in \b Part 3.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1965\margrsxn2330\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li29\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs30 12 APPLICATION DEVELOPMENT: CASE STUDY}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb439\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 This chapter gives you a snapshot of the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 big picture...}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent205\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 How do you approach real world problems with Smalltalk solutions?}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent205\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 What tips and techniques help your application prototyping?}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li608\fi-205\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li608\fi-205\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent205\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Where are the "hot spots" in the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 manual that help you write\line \expndtw-2 your own applications?}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent205\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Where do you start?...How do you proceed?}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 We'll take a case study approach. A case of real world people, not whiz Smalltalk\line \expndtw-4 programmers. This chapter is intended for non-programmers, people with something they\line \expndtw1 want their computers to help them do.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb378\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 The Case Study: A State-Transition Perspective}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri4\sb227\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Our case involves the prototype development of an office automation system, a sales\line \expndtw-4 communication application. In the general scheme of things, the case study is an analysis\line involving \b state-transition models \b0 where physical objects pass through \b a \b0 series of states\line \expndtw1 according to a network of connections between the states.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri7\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The connections between states reflect the logical constraints and preconditions which\line order the transition from one state to another. The tokens which pass from node to node\line \expndtw0 along the constraint network are objects experiencing the state changes.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb133\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Objects going through state changes is a subject of broad interest. The objects might be:}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent205\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A molecule in a chemical reaction}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent205\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A widget on the widget assembly line}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent205\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A source code instruction processed by a compiler}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent205\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A ticket in an airline reservation system}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb144\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 State-transition models relevant to these objects include, respectively:}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li608\fi-205\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li608\fi-205\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent205\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A theory on the molecular interaction of the substances involved in the\line \expndtw-4 reaction}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li608\fi-205\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li608\fi-205\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent205\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A specification of the factory's numerical control tools and assembly line\line \expndtw-1 conveyors, including capacities and set-up time}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li608\fi-205\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li608\fi-205\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent205\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A graph grammar specifying the step-wise decomposition of a high-level\line \expndtw0 language instruction into a collection of machine instructions}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li608\fi-205\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li608\fi-205\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx608 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent205\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A diagram describing the paperwork flow involved in getting a ticket to \b a\line \b0\expndtw-6 traveler}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2356\margrsxn1921\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li36\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 162    Chapter 12: Application Development: Case Study}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri18\sb320\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Smalltalk/V \b0 is ideal for developing applications based on state-transition and other\line \expndtw-3 highly graphical and data intensive models. Its screen graphics and rich data abstracting\line capabilities allow you to produce working prototypes of complex models in record time.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri18\sb140\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Our case study shows how some self-starters in an optical disk drive sales office develop\line \expndtw-2 a \b Smalltalk/V \b0 application to track and facilitate their sales communications. Their\line state-transition network\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0 \'97\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0 though they didn't know or care to call it that\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0 \'97\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0 is a flowchart\line \expndtw1 of their company's approved sales strategy. The tokens coursing through this sales\line \expndtw-1 strategy network are their potential customers.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb360\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 The Case Study Problem as a Smalltalk/V Problem}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri18\sb227\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Where to begin? The Whizzard WORMS reps knew they had a sales communication\line \expndtw-4 problem. They knew they wanted to develop a \b Smalltalk/V \b0 application to facilitate these\line \expndtw-3 communications consistent with corporate marketing strategy. They had a sense of what\line \expndtw-4 the application interface would be like\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0 \'97\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0 inspired by things they'd seen, code they already\line \expndtw-1 had on hand. A lunchtime, napkin-based brainstorming session captured the problem.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb137\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 On the first napkin they drafted a preliminary objective, their problem statement:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li396\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To develop a Sales Communication application (SalesCom) that will allow a rep to\line \expndtw-3 sit down to its interactive display where he or she will quickly and easily see what\line \expndtw-2 communication events are required for the day and to see what the current load of\line their customers is for each of the steps in the sales strategy. Further, the prototype\line \expndtw-4 version will print letters on a case by case basis and will facilitate making telephone\line \expndtw-3 follow-up calls. The protoptype application will be built as much as possible from\line \expndtw-4\lang1031  \lang1033 reusable code taken from the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 tutorial examples and system source files.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri25\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Looking over the rep developers' shoulders with the eyes of a generalist, their problem\line \expndtw-1 statement can be restated:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li396\fi0\ri22\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To develop a \b Smalltalk/V \b0 application using state-transition models to manage the\line \expndtw-5 movement of objects through a process. This application will have a multi-pane main\line \expndtw-3 window where a database of tokens moving through the process can be singled out\line \expndtw-2 for state inspection and manipulation. The application keeps a token state change\line \expndtw-3 event schedule. When moving a token through the process, the application prompts\line \expndtw-4 the user for preconditions or the result of state transitions where the network exhibits\line \expndtw-2 multiple alternate branches.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri25\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The reps, as far as WORM disk sales are concerned, see a world of "us" and "them".\line \expndtw-3 Inside are the Whizzard reps and outside, a sea of current and potential customers. The\line rep's job consists of acting as an agent for Whizzard through a series of communication\line \expndtw0 events with a customer which hopefully lead to a sale.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1865\margrsxn2416\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 12: Application Development: Case Study    163}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri0\sb302\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 They sketched a diagram of their customer prospecting strategy as shown in Figure 12.1.\line \expndtw-1 It was a simple marketing strategy which involved a direct mail campaign, followed by\line \b\expndtw1 a \b0 telephone contact with an attempt to get interested folks to attend a sales seminar.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2243\margrsxn7539\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \li0\ri0\sb0\sa0\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx2912\posnegy461\absw0\absh3362\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\pict\picw7670\pich5930\picwgoal4348\pichgoal3362\jpegblip
}\par\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb3398\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 12.1}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 SalesCom \b0 Sales Strategy}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1865\margrsxn2416\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb281\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 A Window Model for the SalesCom Application}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri0\sb230\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The reps next sketched a rough picture of the ideal \b SalesCom \b0 application window as in\line \expndtw-5 Figure 12.2. Their objective was to take inspiration from the various tutorial examples and\line \expndtw0 system features to formalize their vision of the proposed application.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2257\margrsxn7089\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \li0\ri0\sb0\sa0\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx3632\posnegy576\absw0\absh3420\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\pict\picw6388\pich6032\picwgoal3621\pichgoal3420\jpegblip
}\par\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb3557\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 12.2}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Sketch of \b SalesCom \b0 Window}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2415\margrsxn1833\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li36\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 164    Chapter 12: Application Development: Case Study}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb295\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 There were two purposes for the display as far as they could see:}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li619\fi-209\ri0\sb144\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li619\fi-209\ri0\sb144\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent209\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 They want a basic facility to scan and manage the database of customers.\line \expndtw0 Once one is selected, they want to see the detailed record of that customer.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li619\fi-209\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li619\fi-209\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent209\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 They want to promote a visual connection between their real world \i activity\line \i0\expndtw6 and the formal corporate marketing strategy represented by the (state-\line \expndtw-2 transition) diagram in Figure 12.1.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri29\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The first requirement suggested the \b IistPane \b0 and \b TextPane \b0 views in the \b SalesCom\line \b0\expndtw-2 window model, the Master Customer List pane and Customer Detail text pane. The\line \expndtw1 inspiration was the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 browsers where a clicked selection in a scrolling\line \b\expndtw0 IistPane \b0 initiates a look-up of some associated detail information, the source code for\line \expndtw2 a method or the contents of a file for instance.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri32\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The second requirement begged for graphic representation based on an extension of the\line \expndtw-2 tutorial Network of Nodes example. The "hard" part of taking a network data structure\line and giving it a visual representation is done already. The reps needed only to give the\line nodes more representative names and new screen coordinates to transform the random\line \expndtw0 network of Figure 9.2 to that of Figure 12.1.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri11\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The \b GraphPane \b0 of the \b SalesCom \b0 application (inspired by the animation pane of the\line Animal Habitat tutorial example) facilitates the salesperson's visualization of the\line communication process and the flow of customers through the sales cycle. Numbers\line \expndtw-1 appended to the label of each communication event node indicate the total number of\line \expndtw-3 customers currently pooled at that step in the strategy as well as the year-to-date total of\line \expndtw0 customers having passed through the event node.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li25\fi0\ri0\sb367\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Menus Enrich the Window Model}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri32\sb223\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The reps next addressed what the application would have to do to move customers\line \expndtw-3 through the marketing strategy. What "messages" would the user rep want to send to the\line \b\expndtw0 SalesCom \b0 application object to control preparing letters and prompting phone calls?}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri29\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 They gravitated toward brainstorming about the menus of each of the \b SalesCom\line \b0\expndtw0 application subpanes. They found a pad of removable self-stick notes was useful for\line \expndtw-2 laying hypothetical menu pop-ups over each pane. After much debate, the reps decided\line \expndtw-1 on the configuration in Figure 12.3.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri29\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The reps were excited. They finished lunch with a clear sense of direction on their\line \expndtw0 development project. They were ready to start writing code.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Survival Tip \i0 # \i 1: Don't over-plan. Yes, you need a decent statement of your problem and some\line \expndtw1 sense of what the application's primary interface will look like. But you don't have to have all\line \expndtw0 the answers to get going. To determine when to start, ask yourself, "If 1 write as much code as}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1987\margrsxn2283\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3830\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 12: Application Development: Case Study    165}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft3391\shptop353\shpright7193\shpbottom353\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4378\fi0\ri0\sb450\sa43 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 SalesCom: Today's Date}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2318\margrsxn2859\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw2919\colsr2552\colno2\colw1260 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft3132\shptop-47\shpright6869\shpbottom-47\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft3060\shptop-284\shpright3060\shpbottom508\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 8890}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft3067\shptop1523\shpright3067\shpbottom3229\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft6847\shptop-371\shpright6847\shpbottom1933\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft7200\shptop1904\shpright7200\shpbottom3027\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 43180}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft6898\shptop2956\shpright6898\shpbottom3266\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\pard\plain \sb0\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx3132\posnegy25\absw0\absh-159\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 ABC li}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\