\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 0.5 arcSin}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-15\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 0.52359878}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li79\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Angle in radians}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-230 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2030 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3182 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5040 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx6905 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 0.75 arcCos}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-15\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 0.72273425}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-209 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2030 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3182 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5040 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx6905 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 0.25 arcTan}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-14\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 0.24497866}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2290\margrsxn1984\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb392\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Float}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri11\sb216\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 An 8-byte IEEE format is used for instances of class \b Float \b0 to approximate real numbers.\line This gives approximately 18 digits of precision and represents values in the range (+/\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0 \'97\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0 )\line \expndtw-5 4.19e-307 to (+/\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0 \'97\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0 )l.67e3O8. The 8087 or 80287 arithmetic co-processor, depending upon\line \expndtw-1 your computer, must be present to perform arithmetic operations on floating operands.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb349\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Fraction}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb220\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Instances of class \b Fraction \b0 are exact representations of rational numbers. A pair of\line \expndtw-4 integers (instance variables numerator and denominator) describes the fraction. Fractions\line \expndtw-1 are created by sending the slash (/) message to an integer with an integer argument\line \expndtw1 (provided that the answer does not reduce to an integer).}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb349\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Integer}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri22\sb216\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Integers are frequently used in counting and indexing. Three subclasses of class \b Integer\line \b0 are defined: \b LargeNegativelnteger, LargePositivelnteger \b0 and \b Smalllnteger. \b0 Instances\line \expndtw-5 of class \b Smalllnteger \b0 are in the range -32767 to 32767. These are highly efficient in both\line \expndtw-3 computing speed and memory occupation. Small integers are encoded in the reference to\line the object (the object pointer); they are not represented as objects in memory. The large\line \expndtw-2 integer classes can represent numbers with up to 64K bytes of precision. Conversion\line between integer classes is automatic.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1894\margrsxn2401\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri11\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 14: Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes    211}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb320\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-13\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Streams}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri4\sb223\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The \b stream \b0 classes are used for accessing files, devices, and internal objects as sequences\line \expndtw-2 of characters or other objects. Streams have an internal record of their current position.\line \expndtw1 Streams also have access messages which get or put the next object at the current\line \expndtw-4 position and advance the stream's position by one. Messages are defined for changing the\line \expndtw0 stream position so that random access is possible.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri7\sb144\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 This chapter presents the purposes of and the protocol shared among the stream\line \expndtw-3 hierarchy classes. For a complete specification of each class, refer to \b Part 4: Encyclo-\line \expndtw-4 pedia of Classes.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb130\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The \b Stream \b0 class hierarchy is as follows:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb133\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-13\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Stream}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 ReadStream\line \expndtw-8 WriteStream}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1591\fi-400\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 ReadWriteStream\line \expndtw-10 FileStream\line \expndtw-11 TerminalStream}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb162\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Streams are frequently used for scanning input and writing edited output. The example\line which follows sends the message \b printString \b0 to an instance of class \b String. \b0 The answer\line \expndtw-4 to this message is a new string composed of the initial string (the receiver of \b printString)\line \b0\expndtw0 surrounded by quotes with any internal quotes doubled. For example:}\par \pard\plain\fs2\sa230\sl-1\slmult0\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-223 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2167 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3369 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Expression}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li385\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-526 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2167 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3369 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 'hello' printString}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-13\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 'hello*}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-576 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2167 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3369 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri385\sb0\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 'hello' printString\line printString}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 '"hello"\super 1}\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri11\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The key to the following implementation of \b printString \b0 in class \b String \b0 is that an\line \expndtw-3 instance of class \b WriteStream \b0 automatically grows to contain all the characters written\line \expndtw-2 to it and responds to the message \b contents \b0 by returning a string containing all of its\line \expndtw-5 characters.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2432\margrsxn1864\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 212     Chapter 14: Smalltalk/ V 286 Ciasses}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb317\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 printString}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 I inputStream outputStream I\line \expndtw-3 inputStream := ReadStream on: self.\line \expndtw-1 outputStream := WriteStream on:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 (String new: self size + 2).\line \expndtw-3 outputStream nextPut: $'.\line \expndtw-6 [inputStream atEnd]\line \expndtw-2 whileFalse: [}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1588\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 character := inputStream next.\line \expndtw-6 outputStream nextPut: character,\line \expndtw6 character == $'}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi1192\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 ifTrue: [outputStream nextPut: $']].\line \expndtw-3 outputStream nextPut: $'.\line \b0\scaps\expndtw-6 a \scaps0\b outputStream contents}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb137\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 This example illustrates several stream messages.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Instances of classes \b ReadStream \b0 and \b WriteStream \b0 are created with the \b on: \b0 message with\line \expndtw-2 a string as the argument. Both streams are positioned at the first character. Note that in\line creating the \b WriteStream \b0 instance, space is provided for the containing quotes but not\line \expndtw-1 for interior paired quotes. If interior quotes exist, the string object affected by the\line \expndtw0 WriteStream will automatically be enlarged.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Characters are written to the \b WriteStream \b0 with the message \b nextPut:. \b0 The character to\line \expndtw-1 write is the argument.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri4\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The end of a \b ReadStream \b0 is detected with the \b atEnd \b0 message. If there is a character at\line \expndtw-1 the current position, \b atEnd \b0 answers false; otherwise it answers true.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri4\sb148\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A character is read from the \b ReadStream \b0 with the message \b next. \b0 Note that you cannot\line \expndtw0 send the message \b next \b0 to a \b ReadStream \b0 that is positioned at the end.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri7\sb155\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 All of the characters in a \b WriteStream \b0 are returned as a string in answer to the \b contents\line \b0\expndtw-8 message.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1953\margrsxn2332\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 14: Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes    213}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb353\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Accessing Protocol}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa169 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 We summarize the above information in the following protocol:}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2349\margrsxn2483\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1674\colsr1008\colno2\colw4395 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Protocol}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-4\shptop7\shpright802\shpbottom7\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 15875}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb176\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-13\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 atEnd}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb421\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 contents}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb421\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 next}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb414\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 nextPut: anObject}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb11\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Explanation}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb180\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer true if stream is at the end else answer\line \expndtw-9 false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb187\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer the collection of objects that is being\line \expndtw-3 streamed over.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb194\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer the next object in the receiver stream and\line \expndtw0 advance the position by one.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb184\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Write \b anObject \b0 at the current position. Answer\line \b\expndtw-7 anObject.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1953\margrsxn2332\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb360\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Positioning and Reading Protocol}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb198\sa29 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Some of the stream positioning protocol is as follows:}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2345\margrsxn2371\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1767\colsr922\colno2\colw4503 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Protocol\line \expndtw0 position}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb623\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 position: anlnteger}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb418\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 reset}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb176\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 skip: anlnteger}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb144\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Explanation}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb191\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer an integer representing the stream's\line \expndtw0 position. The position at the beginning of the\line \expndtw-3 stream is zero.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb194\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Set the stream position to \b anlnteger. \b0 Report an\line \expndtw1 error if \b anlnteger \b0 is beyond the end of the stream.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb180\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Set the stream's position to zero.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb191\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Add \b anlnteger \b0 (which may be negative) to the\line \expndtw-2 stream's position.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1953\margrsxn2332\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb137\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Some stream reading protocol follows:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb173\sa180\tx3082 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Protocol{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\ul\expndtw-7 Explanation}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2349\margrsxn2641\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw986\colsr1692\colno2\colw4240 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 do: aBlock}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb14\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Proceed through the stream from the current\line \expndtw0 position to the end evaluating \b aBlock \b0 with each\line \expndtw1 element of the stream as the block argument.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2449\margrsxn1849\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx4\posnegy-698\absw3017\absh-6390\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 214    Chapter 14: Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li382\fi0\ri0\sb371\sa0\sl-432\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx4\posnegy-698\absw3017\absh-6390\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Protocol\line \ul0\expndtw-6 isEmpty}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li385\fi0\ri0\sb382\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx4\posnegy-698\absw3017\absh-6390\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 next: anlnteger}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li385\fi0\ri0\sb648\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx4\posnegy-698\absw3017\absh-6390\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 peek}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li382\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-1159\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx4\posnegy-698\absw3017\absh-6390\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 peekFor: anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li385\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-1159\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx4\posnegy-698\absw3017\absh-6390\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 skipTo: anObject\line \expndtw-3 upTo: anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3071\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Explanation}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3074\fi0\ri0\sb184\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer true if the stream contains no elements;\line \expndtw-4 otherwise answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3067\fi0\ri0\sb191\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer a collection of the next \b anlnteger\line \b0\expndtw-1 elements of the stream. Advance the stream\line \expndtw0 position by \b anlnteger.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3071\fi0\ri0\sb194\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer the next element in the stream without\line \expndtw-1 advancing the stream position. Answer nil if at end\line \expndtw-3 of stream.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3074\fi0\ri0\sb194\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer true and advance the stream position if the\line \expndtw0 next object in the stream equals \b anObject.\line \b0\expndtw-2 Otherwise, answer false and leave the stream\line position unchanged.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3078\fi0\ri0\sb191\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Set the stream position beyond the next occurrence\line \expndtw1 of \b anObject \b0 in the stream or, if none, at the end\line \expndtw0 of the stream. Answer true if there was an\line \expndtw-3 occurrence; otherwise answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3074\fi0\ri0\sb194\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer a collection of objects starting at the\line \expndtw2 current stream position and up to but not\line \expndtw-1 including the next object that equals \b anObject \b0 and\line \expndtw0 advance the stream position beyond the object that\line \expndtw-1 equals \b anObject. If anObject \b0 is not in the stream,\line \expndtw3 answer up to the end of the stream and set the\line \expndtw1 stream position to the end.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The following example illustrates positioning and reading protocol using a stream on an\line array of symbols. First the stream is created and assigned to the variable \b Colors. \b0 Then a\line series of messages are sent to the stream \b Colors. \b0 The result of each message is shown\line \expndtw-6 below.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb137\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Colors := ReadStream on:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li821\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 #(red blue green yellow pink cyan magenta brown).}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1963\margrsxn2328\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4630\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 14: Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes    215}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2367\margrsxn4934\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx2678\posnegy443\absw0\absh-259\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb479\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Expression}\par \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-439 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2462 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4608 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Colors isEmpty}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li104\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 false}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-223 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2462 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4608 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Colors next}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li101\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 red}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-266 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2462 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4608 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Colors next: 3}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li90\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 (blue green yellow)}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-230 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2462 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4608 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Colors peek}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li97\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 pink}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-230 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2462 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4608 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Colors peekFor: #blue}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li104\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 false}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-252 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2462 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4608 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Colors upTo: # magenta}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li94\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 (pink cyan)}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-238 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2462 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4608 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Colors skip: -4}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-238 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2462 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4608 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Colors position}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li108\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 3}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-238 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2462 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4608 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Colors skipTo: #pink}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li97\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 true}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-245 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2462 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4608 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Colors upTo: #red}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li94\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 (cyan magenta brown)}\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1963\margrsxn2328\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb346\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Writing Protocol}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa169 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Some additional stream writing protocol follows.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2352\margrsxn2587\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1659\colsr1019\colno2\colw4291 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Protocol}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft7\shptop4\shpright806\shpbottom4\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 15875}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi-396\ri0\sb191\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 nextPutAU:\line \expndtw-5 aColiection}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi-392\ri0\sb187\sa0\sl-245\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 next: anlnteger\line \expndtw-5 put: anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb25\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 cr}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 tab}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 space}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb7\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Explanation}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb198\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Write the elements of \b aColiection \b0 to the stream.\line \expndtw-4 Answer \b aColiection.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb205\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Write \b anObject \b0 to the \b stream anlnteger \b0 times.\line \expndtw-6 Answer \b anObject.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb36\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Write a line-terminating character to the stream.\line \expndtw1 Write a tab character to the stream.\line \expndtw0 Write a space character to the stream.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2414\margrsxn1867\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li25\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 216    Chapter 14: Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li14\fi0\ri7\sb731\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 All objects understand the message \b printOn: \b0 with a stream as the argument. This\line \expndtw-3 message produces a character description of the receiver object on the argument stream.\line \expndtw0 For example, the implementation of \b printOn: \b0 for class \b Rectangle \b0 is:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb126\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 printOn: aStream}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi410\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 "Print the origin and corner points"\line \expndtw-3 origin printOn: aStream.\line aStream nextPutAll: ' corner: '.\line \expndtw-5 corner printOn: aStream}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri4\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 where the \b printOn: \b0 message is sent to the origin and corner points and the message\line \b\expndtw0 nextPutAll: \b0 to its stream argument. The implementation for class \b Point \b0 is:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb144\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 printOn: aStream}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi407\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 "Print the x and y coordinates"\line \expndtw-5 x printOn: aStream.\line \expndtw0 aStream nextPutAll: ' \i @ \i0 '.\line \expndtw-5 y printOn: aStream}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb133\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 An example of printing a Rectangle is:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb137\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Display boundingBox printOn: Transcript}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 which writes the following in the System Transcript window if you are running in EGA\line \expndtw-1 color mode:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb144\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 0 \b0 @ \b 0 corner: 640 \b0 @ \b 350}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li22\fi0\ri0\sb378\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Interface to DOS File System}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri7\sb227\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Class \b FileStream, \b0 a subclass of \b ReadWriteStream, \b0 provides the primary interface to the\line \b\expndtw-4 DOS \b0 file system. File streams respond to all of the stream protocol presented earlier. File\line \expndtw-5 streams use an instance of the class \b File \b0 to provide random page access to DOS files. Files\line \expndtw2 use an instance of class \b FileHandle \b0 to read and write DOS file pages. The class\line \b\expndtw0 Directory \b0 provides access to DOS disk directories.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri4\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 In this section we present an overview of these file system classes. For detailed\line information on all of the messages that they provide, please see the descriptions in\line \b\expndtw-5 Part 4.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1771\margrsxn2496\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 14: Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes    21\i0 7}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb338\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 File Streams}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri4\sb212\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 File streams are usually created with either a message to class \b File \b0 specifying a partial or\line complete path name or a message to an instance of class \b Directory \b0 specifying a particular\line \expndtw0 file to access in that directory. Here are some examples of messages to class \b File.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb144\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 File pathName: 'c:\\smaltalk\\chapter.r}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 File pathName: 'chapter. 1'}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 File pathName: '\\smaltalk\\chapter.l*}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri7\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The first expression above has a complete path name. The second example above is a\line partial path name. The directory object \b Disk, \b0 a global variable, is used to complete the\line \expndtw-3 path name. In this case the file \b 'chapter. 1' \b0 in the directory \b Disk \b0 is accessed. The final\line \expndtw-2 example is a complete path name without a disk drive specifier. The drive specifier used\line \expndtw2 is the same as that used by the directory \b Disk.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri11\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The other way to create a file stream is by sending one of the following messages to a\line \expndtw-1 directory object.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Disk file: 'chapter. 1'\line \expndtw-2 Disk newFile: 'junk.fil'}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri7\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The above two messages cannot have path names as arguments, only a file name. The\line \expndtw-4 difference between the two messages is that the second message will erase an existing file\line \expndtw-2 of the same name if one exists. They both will create the file if it does not already exist.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri7\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A word of caution about DOS files. DOS does not automatically update the directory\line entry on disk as you write to a file. There are two messages that you can send to file\line \expndtw1 streams to cause the directory entry to be updated on the disk. These are:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 stream close\line \expndtw-7 stream flush}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri4\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The difference between the two messages is that the first closes the file stream making\line \expndtw-1 further access to the DOS file using this object impossible. The second message also\line \expndtw-3 causes the directory entry to be updated but keeps the file stream object open for further\line access to the file. For consistency, all other streams support these two messages as well,\line \expndtw0 but they have no effect.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri4\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 File streams are buffered for efficiency. In addition, file streams recognize two different\line \expndtw0 formats for end of line, the DOS cr-lf pair, and the UNIX single If. When a file stream\line \expndtw-2 is opened, the beginning of the file is scanned to determine which format applies. New\line files are created using the DOS format. The following three messages let you test and\line \expndtw1 change the line ending format for a file.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2385\margrsxn1885\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li22\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 218    Chapter 14.- Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb256\sa0\sl-234\slmult0\tx2826 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 stream lineDelimiter{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-3 "Answers Lf or Cr"}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 stream lineDelimiter: Lf         "Change to Unix format"}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-234\slmult0\tx3190 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 stream lineDelimiter: Cr{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-1 "Change to DOS format"}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The fastest way to read a file stream is with the \b upTo: \b0 or the \b nextLine \b0 message. The fast\line \expndtw0 way to write a file stream is with the \b nextPutAll: \b0 message.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Putting all of the above together, here is a faster version of the program given in Chapter\line \expndtw2 7 of the tutorials which converts text files from DOS format to UNIX format.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li414\fi0\ri0\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 "Convert a file from DOS format to UNIX format"}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li432\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 I input output I}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 input *= Disk file: 'chapter.7'.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 output := Disk newFile: 'stripped.7'.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 output lineDelimiter: Lf.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li432\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 [input atEnd]}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi356\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 whileFalse: [output nextPutAll: input nextLine; cr].\line \expndtw0 output close}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb346\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 Directories}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri7\sb205\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The class \b Directory \b0 provides access to DOS file system directories. \b Smalltalk/V \b0 as\line \expndtw-1 delivered has the following global variables which contain directories.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Disk}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 DiskA}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 DiskB}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri7\sb162\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The variable \b Disk \b0 contains the directory in which you started \b Smalltalk/V. \b0 The variables\line \b DiskA \b0 and \b DiskB \b0 contain the root directories for the disk devices A: and B: respectively.\line \expndtw0 You can create new directory objects using the following messages:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb140\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 SampleDir := Directory pathName: 'a:\\dirname'\line DiskC := Directory new drive: $c; pathName: \b0 'V}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri11\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Note that creating a directory object is not the same as creating a directory on the disk\line \expndtw-3 drive itself. To create a new directory on the disk, send the message \b create \b0 to a directory\line \expndtw1 object with the proper drive and path name, as in:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb133\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 SampleDir create}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1874\margrsxn2403\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 14: Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes    219}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li29\fi0\ri4\sb306\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Directories understand messages for listing their subdirectories and files, for creating new\line \expndtw-1 files and subdirectories, and much more. See \b Part 4 \b0 for more details.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li32\fi0\ri0\sb335\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 Files and FileHandles}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li18\fi0\ri7\sb216\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Class \b File \b0 provides the logical support to file streams necessary for random page access\line \expndtw0 to DOS files. Class \b FileHandle \b0 provides the low level access to DOS files. \b Part 4\line \b0\expndtw-3 provides a detailed list of the messages implemented by these classes. Unless you are\line \expndtw-4 building some sort of new file access protocol separate from file streams, you will rarely\line \expndtw-2 have to deal with these classes. A few of the class messages for \b File \b0 are important: the\line \expndtw-1 ones for copying, renaming, and removing files.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li14\fi0\ri11\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 FileHandle \b0 is a subclass of \b ByteArray. \b0 A \b FileHandle \b0 instance has a size of exactly two\line \expndtw-2 bytes long which contains the DOS file handle number when the file is opened. DOS\line \expndtw-1 allows only a limited number of file handles. When you try to open a file and no more\line file handles are available, \b Smalltalk/V \b0 automatically checks that all file handles are\line \expndtw-2 indeed used by some objects. For example, you might have opened a file and forgot to\line \expndtw0 close it. As long as this handle is not pointed to by any object, \b Smalltalk/V \b0 will\line automatically reuse it to open a new file.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb378\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Terminal Input and Output}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri14\sb230\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Terminal input and output is accomplished through the cooperation of two classes:\line \b\expndtw-4 InputEvent \b0 and \b TerminalStream. InputEvent \b0 is a lower level interface whose method\line \b\expndtw-3 nextEvent \b0 uses a primitive to read a keyboard or mouse event and return the type of the\line \expndtw-4 event read. \b InputEvent \b0 is interrupt driven. It usually waits on the \b KeyboardSemaphore\line \b0\expndtw-2 (a global variable containing an instance of class \b Semaphore) \b0 until the semaphore is\line \expndtw0 signaled by a key stroke or mouse operation.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 CurrentEvent \b0 is the global variable used to read events. It contains an instance of\line \b\expndtw-4 InputEvent. \b0 The read primitive modifies the instance variables of \b CurrentEvent: type,\line \expndtw2 value, x, \b0 and y. The location of the mouse at the time of the event is placed in x and\line \expndtw-4 y. The following table describes the events returned from the read primitive (left column),\line \expndtw-5 the types returned by the \b InputEvent \b0 (middle column), and the values associated with the\line \expndtw-2 types (right column).}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2368\margrsxn1916\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li22\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa500 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 220    Chapter 14: Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2779\margrsxn2265\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw3610\colsr346\colno2\colw2908 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Primitive Type     nextEvent Type}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx202 \pvpara\phcol\posnegx25\posnegy198\absw1436\absh-1195\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  #\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx202 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx25\posnegy198\absw1436\absh-1195\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent202\pnf3{\pntxtb #}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 characterlnput}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx202 \pvpara\phcol\posnegx25\posnegy198\absw1436\absh-1195\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  #\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx202 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx25\posnegy198\absw1436\absh-1195\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent202\pnf3{\pntxtb #}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 functionlnput}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx202 \pvpara\phcol\posnegx25\posnegy198\absw1436\absh-1195\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  #\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx202 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx25\posnegy198\absw1436\absh-1195\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent202\pnf3{\pntxtb #}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 mouseMove}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb216\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx25\posnegy198\absw1436\absh-1195\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 #mouseButton}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1710\fi0\ri0\sb223\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx1912 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  #\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1710\fi0\ri0\sb223\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx1912 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent202\pnf3{\pntxtb #}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 characterlnput}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1710\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx1912 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  #\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1710\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx1912 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent202\pnf3{\pntxtb #}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 functionlnput}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1710\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx1912 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  #\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1710\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx1912 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent202\pnf3{\pntxtb #}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 mouseMove}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1710\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx1912 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  #\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1710\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx1912 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent202\pnf3{\pntxtb #}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 mouseStillDown}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1710\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx1912 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  #\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1710\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx1912 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent202\pnf3{\pntxtb #}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 mouseButtonDown}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1710\fi0\ri0\sb1170\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 # mouseButtonUp}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx25\posnegy1138\absw0\absh-259\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 #nullEvent}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1710\fi0\ri0\sb1177\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 #nullEvent}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb7\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Value}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb227\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 ASCII code\line \expndtw0 scan code}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb234\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 mouse button value}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx198 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  1\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx198 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent184\pnf3}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 = left button down}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx198 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  2\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx198 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent184\pnf3}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 = right button down}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx198 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  3\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx198 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent184\pnf3}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\super\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 =\nosupersub  middle button down}\par \pard\plain\fs2\par{\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx194 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  5\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx194 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart5\pnindent194\pnf3}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 = left button down shifted}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx194 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  6\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx194 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart5\pnindent194\pnf3}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 = right button down shifted}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx194 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  7\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx194 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart5\pnindent194\pnf3}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 = middle button down shifted}\par \pard\plain\fs2\par{\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx194 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  1\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx194 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent183\pnf3}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 = left button up}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx194 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  2\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx194 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent183\pnf3}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 = right button up}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx194 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  3\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx194 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent183\pnf3}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 \'97\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0  middle button up}\par \pard\plain\fs2\par{\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx194 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  5\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx194 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart5\pnindent194\pnf3}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 = left button up shifted}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx194 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  6\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx194 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart5\pnindent194\pnf3}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 = right button up shifted}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx194 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  7\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx194 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart5\pnindent194\pnf3}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 = middle button up shifted\line \expndtw-5 (none)}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2368\margrsxn1916\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb79\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The  scan  code  associated  with   # \b functionlnput  \b0 is   defined   by   DOS.  When  a}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tx220 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  #\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tx220 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent216\pnf3{\pntxtb #}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 mouseMove \b0 event is returned from the primitive, an \b InputEvent \b0 can generate either}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-241\slmult0\tx220 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  #\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-241\slmult0\tx220 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent216\pnf3{\pntxtb #}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 mouseMove \b0 or \b # mouseStillDown \b0 depending on whether a mouse button is being\line \expndtw-3 held down (if yes, the latter one is generated). When a \b #mouseButton \b0 event is returned,\line \expndtw4 an \b InputEvent \b0 further differentiates  it into two types,   # \b mouseButtonDown  \b0 or}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-241\slmult0\tx220 \b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  #\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-241\slmult0\tx220 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent216\pnf3{\pntxtb #}}\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 mouseButtonUp \b0 depending on whether it is a down or up action that has caused the\line \expndtw-6 event.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri4\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 TerminalStream \b0 is defined as a subclass of \b ReadWriteStream. \b0 It uses \b InputEvent \b0 to\line \expndtw-4 read from the keyboard or mouse and sends messages to \b CharacterScanner \b0 to write\line \expndtw0 characters to the terminal screen. The global variable \b Terminal, \b0 which contains an\line \expndtw-2 instance of class \b TerminalStream, \b0 is used throughout \b Smalltalk/V \b0 to handle terminal\line \b I/O.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri7\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 TerminalStream \b0 reimplements the method \b next \b0 defined in \b Stream \b0 with the method\line \b\expndtw-3 read. \b0 Method \b read \b0 is the major user interface for reading a single character (or function\line \expndtw-4 key) from the keyboard or an event from the mouse. Two global variables, \b FunctionKey\line \b0\expndtw-1 and \b MouseEvent, \b0 are set to true or false to indicate the source of the input before the\line \expndtw-3 input is returned. If a mouse event is read, the variable \b MouseEvent \b0 is set to true. If a\line \expndtw-2 function key is pressed, the variable \b FunctionKey \b0 is set to true. And non-function keys\line \expndtw0 set both variables to false.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1868\margrsxn2402\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 14: Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes    221}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri0\sb310\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Method nextPut: \b0 outputs a character to the terminal screen at the current cursor\line \expndtw-3 position. It is seldom used in the system since writing characters to the screen is usually\line \expndtw-5 done through instances of \b CharacterScanner \b0 which has more sophisticated masking and\line \expndtw-3 clipping capabilities.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb346\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Programming Function Keys}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb216\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 When a function key is processed outside of class \b Terminal-Stream, \b0 the \b read \b0 method in\line \expndtw-3 class \b TerminalStream \b0 is usually invoked by method \b processlnput \b0 in class \b Dispatcher.\line \b0 As soon as a function key is pressed, the \b read \b0 method returns the function code and sets\line \expndtw-1 the global variable FunctionKey to true and the global variable \b MouseEvent \b0 to false.\line Method \b processlnput \b0 then calls method \b processKey: \b0 in the receiver dispatcher class\line \expndtw0 (any of the dispatcher classes). The latter method checks the state of the two global\line \expndtw-3 Boolean variables, \b MouseEvent \b0 and \b FunctionKey. \b0 If either of the variables is true, then\line \b\expndtw-1 a \b0 function code must be processed. To do this, method \b processFunctionKey: \b0 in the\line \expndtw-3 receiver dispatcher is invoked to compare the function code to the values defined by the\line \expndtw-1 pool dictionary \b FunctionKeys. \b0 When a match is found, the appropriate action is taken.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb144\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw14\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Suppose you want to assign the move and \b frame window \b0 operations to Fl\line \expndtw-2 and F2. First, define names for them, for example \b MoveWindowFunction \b0 and\line \b\expndtw-3 FrameWindowFunction \b0 respectively. Then, enter these names into the pool dictionary\line \b\expndtw-2 FunctionKeys \b0 and associate them with the desired function key codes. You can do this\line \expndtw-1 by executing the following expression:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 FunctionKeys at: 'MoveWindowFunction'}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi349\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 put: 59 asCharacter.\line \expndtw-4 FunctionKeys at: 'FrameWindowFunction'}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li760\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 put: 60 asCharacter}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri7\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 This creates two new variables in pool dictionary \b FunctionKeys. \b0 Note that 59 and 60 are\line \expndtw1 the scan codes generated by Fl and F2 respectively.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri7\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The next step is to add the following code to method \b processFunctionKey: \b0 in class\line \b\expndtw1 Dispatcher \b0 so that the desired functions occur when Fl and F2 are pressed.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2384\margrsxn1903\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 222    Chapter 14: Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li749\fi-353\ri0\sb320\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 MoveWindowFunction == aCharacter\line \expndtw-1 ifTrue: [}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1109\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 pane topPane hasCursor}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 ifTrue: [Apane topPane dispatcher move]\line \expndtw-1 ifFalse: [ATerminal bell]].\line \expndtw0 FrameWindowFunction == aCharacter\line \expndtw-1 ifTrue: [}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1109\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 pane topPane hasCursor}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1465\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 ifTrue: [Apane topPane dispatcher frame]\line \expndtw-1 ifFalse: [ATerminal bell]].}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb374\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-13\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Collections}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb216\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A collection \b0 is a group of related objects. The Smalltalk collection classes define several\line \expndtw-3 different data structures which serve as containers for arbitrary objects. For example, a\line \i\expndtw-5 String \i0 is a sequence of characters while a \i Set \i0 is an unordered collection of non-duplicated\line \expndtw0 objects of any kind. The collection classes are useful because they provide similar\line protocol for:}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb18\sa0\sl-396\slmult0\tx616 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-23\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  1.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb18\sa0\sl-396\slmult0\tx616 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent220\pnf3{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-23\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Iterating over the elements of a collection.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-396\slmult0\tx616 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-19\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  2.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-396\slmult0\tx616 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent220\pnf3{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-19\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Searching a collection for a particular element.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-396\slmult0\tx616 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-21\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  3.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-396\slmult0\tx616 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent220\pnf3{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-21\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Adding and removing elements.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-396\slmult0\tx616 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-15\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  4.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-396\slmult0\tx616 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent220\pnf3{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-15\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Accessing and changing elements.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-396\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The following is the \b Collection \b0 class hierarchy:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi-396\ri0\sb133\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Collection\line \expndtw-6 Bag\line \expndtw-3 IndexedCollection}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1588\fi-385\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 FixedSizeCollection\line \expndtw-10 Array\line \expndtw-13 Byte Array\line \expndtw-5 Interval\line String}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1192\fi796\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Symbol\line OrderedCollection}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi796\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 SortedCollection\line \expndtw-11 Set}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1192\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Dictionary}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1595\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 IdentityDictionary}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1994\margrsxn2294\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter l4: Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes    223}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb310\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The attributes, conversions, and common protocol among various  collections are\line \expndtw0 discussed next with a description of each kind of collection following.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb360\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Attributes of the Collection Class}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb198\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 In general, each kind of collection can be characterized by four attributes:}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li644\fi-238\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx644 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-21\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  1.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li644\fi-238\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx644 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent238\pnf3{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-21\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Whether the collection has a well defined order associated with its elements.\line \expndtw3 This order can be defined either externally by a key or internally by the\line \expndtw-1 contents of elements.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb140\sa0\tx644 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-19\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  2.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb140\sa0\tx644 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent237\pnf3{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-19\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Whether the collection's size is fixed or expandable.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb133\sa0\tx644 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-19\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  3.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb133\sa0\tx644 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent237\pnf3{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-19\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Whether or not duplicates of the collection's elements are allowed.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li644\fi-238\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-23