238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 ifFalse: \scaps [a \scaps0 nil],\line browseddass := aClass.\line \expndtw1 topPane := TopPane new}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1195\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 label: aClass name, ' I ClassBrowser';\line \expndtw-1 minimumSize: SysFontWidth * 20}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1199\fi403\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 @ (SysFontHeight * 8);\line \expndtw-3 yourself.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 twoIineHeight : = ListFont height * 2 + 4.\line \expndtw-7 topPane addSubpane:\line \expndtw1 (IistPane new\line \expndtw-3 model: self;\line name: # dictionaries;\line \expndtw1 change: #dictionary:;\line \expndtw-3 selection: 2;\line \expndtw-4 framingBlock: [box I\line \expndtw1 box origin extent:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi792\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 box width // 5 @ twoIineHeight]).\line \expndtw-4 selectedDictionary :\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0 \'97\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0  browsedClass.\line \expndtw-7 topPane addSubpane:\line \expndtw1 (IistPane new\line \expndtw-3 model: self;\line \expndtw-2 name: # selectors;\line \expndtw-4 menu: # selector Menu;\line \expndtw2 change: #selector:;\line \expndtw-1 framingBlock: [:boxl}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2383\fi-392\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 box origin + (0 (8) twoIineHeight)\line \expndtw9 extent: box width // 5 @}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi1199\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 (box height - twoIineHeight)]).\line \expndtw-7 topPane addSubpane:\line \expndtw-1 (TextPane new\line \expndtw-3 model: self;\line \expndtw4 name: #text;\line \expndtw-3 change: # accept:from:;\line \expndtw-1 framingBlock: [:boxl}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1987\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw13\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 box origin + ((box width // 5) \i @ \i0 0)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi1580\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 corner: box corner]).\line \expndtw-4 topPane dispatcher open schedule Window}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1879\margrsxn2416\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 14: Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes    255}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb295\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Invoking this method will create a window with three subpanes:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb144\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 dictionaries \i0 (a ListPane)\line \i\expndtw-6 selectors \i0 (a ListPane)\line \i\expndtw-1 text \i0 (a TextPane)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 In order for the window to work properly, the messages \b dictionaries, dictionary:,\line \expndtw-3 selectors, selector:, selectorMenu, text, \b0 and \b accepr.from: \b0 must be defined as instance\line \expndtw1 methods in the model.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb328\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Initialize Contents of Panes}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri4\sb198\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The application model must provide for each subpane a method with the same name as\line \expndtw-3 the pane name which, when invoked, answers the data of the pane. For example, the\line \b\expndtw-2 ClassBrowser \b0 has three methods to initialize its three subpanes:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 dictionaries}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li821\fi382\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 "Answer the array of dictionaries"\line \b0\scaps\expndtw0 a \scaps0\b # ( class instance )}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 selectors}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li824\fi382\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 "Answer \b0 a \b sorted list of selectors for the selected dictionary"\line \expndtw-4 AselectedDictionary selectors asSortedCollection}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb140\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 text}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li821\fi382\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 "Answer the source text for the selected method"\line \expndtw-4 AselectedDictionary sourceCodeAt: selectedMethod}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri4\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Note that the first two methods answer an instance of a subclass of class \b IndexedCol-\line lection \b0 whose elements must be printable like Strings or Symbols. The third one answers\line \expndtw-4 a string (lines within the string are separated by line feeds). In case there is more data than\line \expndtw-2 a string can hold, the method \b filelnFrom: \b0 in \b TextPane \b0 can be used to initialize its data\line \expndtw-3 from an external file (refer to source code of the \b file \b0 method in the \b DiskBrowser \b0 class).}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb328\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Cany Out Communication and Synchronization}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb198\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 When you make a selection or change the contents of pane data, the effect can be either\line \i\expndtw-1 local \i0 or \i global. \i0 Global effects the model or other panes. Anything else is local. For\line \expndtw-4 example, in the Class Browser, when you make a selection in the dictionaries pane, both\line the selectors pane and text pane need to be synchronized. Thus the effect is global. If you\line make editing changes in the Class Browser's text pane, the change is local because it does\line \expndtw-1 not effect other panes or the model. When you save these changes, however, the text\line \expndtw-2 needs to be compiled into the selected class and logged to the \b change log \b0 file. This can\line \expndtw2 only be done by the model, so the effect of saving the text is global.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2421\margrsxn1871\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 236    Chapter 14: Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri0\sb324\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Specifying change messages in the \b open \b0 or \b openOn: \b0 method provides each pane with a\line message to send when these global effects occur. The argument of a change message is\line usually a piece of data passed from the pane to the model. For example, when you select\line \expndtw-4 a method in the selectors pane, the following method in \b ClassBrowser \b0 is invoked by the\line \expndtw-7 pane:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb130\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 selector: aSymbol}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi407\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 "Display the selected method in the text pane"\line \expndtw0 selectedMethod := aSymbol.\line \expndtw5 self changed: #text}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 where the first statement changes the application state by assigning \b aSymbol \b0 to the\line \expndtw-2 instance variable \b selectedMethod, \b0 and the second statement informs the \i text \i0 pane that\line \expndtw2 the state has changed and it needs to update its contents.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 When the global effect calls for one or more updates in another pane, the \b changed: \b0 or\line \b\expndtw-4 changed-.with: \b0 method defined in class \b Object \b0 can be used to broadcast the effect to all\line \expndtw-3 subpanes of the model. In the previous example, selecting a method in the selectors pane\line \expndtw-1 displays the source of the method in the text pane. The \b changed: \b0 message is used to\line \expndtw-2 notify the text pane that the \b selectedMethod \b0 had been changed. The other message,\line \b changed:with:, \b0 in addition to notifying subpanes, also passes an object as the argument\line \expndtw2 of the \b with: \b0 keyword to provide communication from the model to the panes.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 When the subpane receives the update message (sent by method \b changed:) \b0 and its name\line \expndtw-2 matches the argument of the \b changed: \b0 keyword, the pane name is sent as a message to\line \expndtw-3 the model retrieving the new pane contents. To continue the previous example, after the\line \expndtw1 text pane receives the update message, it updates its own data by sending the \b text\line \b0\expndtw-3 message to the \b ClassBrowser \b0 to perform the \b text \b0 method which in turn answers a string\line \expndtw-2 of the new text pane contents. This concludes the update, and the \b Dispatcher \b0 regains\line \expndtw1 control and waits for the next keyboard or mouse event.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb338\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 Define Menus for Panes}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb205\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 If the \b menu: \b0 message is sent during the creation of a pane, a method with the same name\line as the message argument must be defined in the model. This method answers an instance\line \expndtw-1 of class \b Menu \b0 which contains the desired menu items for the pane. In the \b openOn:\line \b0\expndtw-4 method of the \b ClassBrowser, \b0 the message \b menu: #selectorMenu \b0 is sent to the selectors\line \expndtw-1 pane. Thus a corresponding method is defined in the \b ClassBrowser:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 selectorMenu}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li817\fi385\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 "Answer the selector pane menu"\line \b0\scaps\expndtw-13 a \scaps0\b Menu}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1192\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 labels: 'remove\\senders\\implementors' withCrs}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1192\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw12\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 lines: #()}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1188\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 selectors: # (removeSelector senders implementors)}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1919\margrsxn2366\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 14: Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes    23 \i0 7}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb313\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The string argument to \b labels: \b0 contains the items to be shown in the menu. Message\line \b\expndtw-3 withCrs \b0 replaces backslashes (\\) with line feeds in its receiver string. The argument to\line \b selectors: \b0 is an array of messages to send when you select the corresponding item in the\line menu. The methods carrying out these messages can be optionally defined in the model.\line \expndtw-4 If you do not define them, the ones in the \b Dispatcher \b0 class (associated with the pane) are\line \expndtw-5 used as defaults. If they are not defined in either class, an error results. The \b ClassBrowser\line \b0\expndtw0 defines all three methods needed in the menu:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 removeSelector}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi407\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 "Remove the selected method"\line \expndtw0 selectedMethod isNil}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi400\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 ifTrue: \scaps [a \scaps0 nil].\line \expndtw-3 selectedDictionary}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi396\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 removeSelector: selectedMethod.\line Smalltalk logEvaluate:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1195\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 selectedDictionary name,}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1202\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 'removeSelector: #',}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi396\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 selectedMethod.\line \expndtw1 selectedMethod := nil.\line \expndtw2 self}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1199\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 changed: #selectors with: # restore;}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1199\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 changed: #text}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 senders}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi407\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 "Popup a window with the senders of the selectedMethod"\line \expndtw6 selectedMethod == nil}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1195\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 ifFalse: [Smalltalk sendersOf: selectedMethod]}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 implementors}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 "Popup a window with the implementors of the selectedMethod"\line \expndtw7 selectedMethod == nil\line \expndtw-4 ifFalse: [}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1595\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Smalltalk implementorsOf: selectedMethod]}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri14\sb144\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The \b removeSelector \b0 method provides another example of changing the current state and\line \expndtw0 using message \b changed: \b0 to inform the selectors pane to update.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2358\margrsxn1930\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 238    Chapter 14: Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb356\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-15\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 Pane}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri18\sb212\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 An instance of class \b TopPane \b0 is responsible for all the functions pertaining to the whole\line \expndtw-7 window:}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li619\fi-212\ri0\sb158\sa0\sl-241\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li619\fi-212\ri0\sb158\sa0\sl-241\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Display the window frame and invoke each \b SubPane \b0 to display its pane\line \expndtw-2 contents.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Save, display, and highlight the window label.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Activate the window and all subpanes.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer whether the window contains a certain point.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Close the \b TopPane \b0 and invoke each \b SubPane \b0 to close itself.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri14\sb158\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Class \b SubPane \b0 and its three subclasses, \b GraphPane, IistPane \b0 and \b TextPane \b0 are\line responsible for functions that are specific to subpanes:}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Display the pane frame.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Activate itself.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer whether the pane contains a certain point.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Display a portion of its data in the pane.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Scroll data in four directions.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Make a selection on a piece of its data.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Close itself.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri4\sb155\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 In addition, a \b TextPane \b0 provides the capabilities to cut, paste, copy, and execute portions\line \expndtw1 of its data.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb324\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex81\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Dispatcher}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The main function of an instance of class \b Dispatcher \b0 and its subclasses is to interpret the\line \expndtw-3 input from the keyboard or mouse and send an appropriate message to the corresponding\line \expndtw0 pane. It also has the following functions:}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Activate or de-activate the corresponding pane.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Return the cursor to the top-left corner of its pane.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Open or close the window.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Cycle windows or panes in the window.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb137\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A \b TopDispatcher \b0 has the following additional functions:}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb133\sa0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb133\sa0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Provide methods to execute items in the window menu.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-400\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-400\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Set or change the content of the window label bar.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-400\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Other \b Dispatchers \b0 have the following additional functions:}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-400\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-400\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Tell the pane to scroll its data by a specified amount.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Tell the pane to handle selections.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2015\margrsxn2254\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 14: Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes    239}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb295\sa0\tx623 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 \'95{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw1\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0 Provide methods to execute items in the pane menu.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb299\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex82\expndtw-4\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Prompter}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri11\sb209\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Class \b Prompter \b0 gives an application writer a simple mechanism to pose a question and\line \expndtw-2 solicit an answer. A Prompter is a window with its label showing the intended question\line \expndtw-4 and a single text pane for editing the answer. It is a window application itself, but is often\line \expndtw-3 used by other window applications as a building block. For example, when you create \b a\line \b0 file using the Disk Browser, the first thing you see is a Prompter asking you to respond\line \expndtw-1 with the file name.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb144\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To open a Prompter, you can send one of the following two messages to class \b Prompter:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb144\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Prompter prompt: question default: answer\line \expndtw-4 Prompter prompt: question defaultExpression: answer}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri18\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 where both \b question \b0 and \b answer \b0 are strings. After the Prompter window is opened, the\line \b\expndtw-5 answer \b0 string will be shown in its text pane as a default. The first message returns a string\line \expndtw-4 as answered by the application user, while the second message returns an object resulting\line \expndtw-1 from evaluating the answer. For instance,}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi-389\ri0\sb144\sa0\sl-245\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Prompter prompt: 'Give me a string please'\line \expndtw7 default: \b0 '2 \b + \b0 3'}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb144\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 returns '2 \b + \b0 3', and}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi-389\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Prompter prompt: 'Give me an expression please'\line \expndtw0 defaultExpression: \b0 '2 \b + \b0 3*}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri0\sb144\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 returns 5 after the default answer is accepted. If you cancel the Prompter, an answer of\line \expndtw0 nil will be returned by both messages.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri25\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Notice that when a Prompter \i is \i0 accepted or canceled, the program flow control is given\line \expndtw1 back to the caller of the Prompter. When most other kinds of windows are closed,\line \expndtw-3 control is given to the \b Scheduler \b0 (described below) to cause another window to become\line \expndtw-6 active.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb324\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex82\expndtw1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Dispatch Manager}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri22\sb209\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A DispatchManager \b0 schedules all the windows under its control. Normally only one\line \expndtw-2 such instance exists in the system which is contained in the global variable \b Scheduler.\line \expndtw0 The Scheduler \b0 maintains an ordered collection of \b TopDispatchers \b0 and schedules\line \expndtw-1 windows by sending messages to these \b TopDispatchers. \b0 It performs the following\line \expndtw-4 functions:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb140\sa0\tx623 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 \'95{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-1\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0 Add and remove dispatchers (thus windows).}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2361\margrsxn1905\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 240    Chapter 14: Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb320\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb320\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer the \b TopDispatcher \b0 associated with the active window.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Display all the windows.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Cycle the ordering of windows.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Search for the window containing the cursor and make it the active window.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li619\fi-212\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li619\fi-212\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx619 \f3\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent212\pnf3{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Re-initialize the system by removing all windows and then drawing the\line \expndtw-3 System Transcript window.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb356\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Applications with Multiple Windows}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri4\sb212\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 One way to coordinate windows within a multi-windowed application is to have one\line \expndtw0 application model for all the windows in the application. You make each subpane of\line \expndtw-1 these windows a dependent of the model. When a change is made to a subpane which\line \expndtw-3 will have global effects, one of the change methods in the model will be invoked. It will\line \expndtw1 then decide what other subpanes will be affected and updated.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri18\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 In \b Smalltalk, \b0 subpanes in one window can have non-unique names. Subpanes with the\line \expndtw-4 same name are updated simultaneously in one broadcasting of changes. Since this is also\line \expndtw-2 true for the one model multi-window approach, take care in giving the same name to\line subpanes in different windows.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri22\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Another way to coordinate windows is to leave the current scheme of one model per\line window as it is. In this case, one super model is created with all other models as its\line \expndtw0 dependents. In the super model, one change message is defined for each dependent.\line \expndtw-4 When the lower-level model receives a change message, it updates its own panes as in the\line \expndtw0 single window application. In addition, the lower-level model sends an appropriate\line \expndtw-3 change message to the super model which then broadcasts the change to other dependent\line \expndtw-2 models. Each lower-level model should implement an update method to accept the\line \expndtw0 broadcasting from the super model.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A window can also be associated with the super model which can, for example, allow you\line \expndtw-1 to select different functions in the application. Each selection triggers a sequence of\line \expndtw-4 windows being activated. This approach provides more modularity. For instance, subpane\line \expndtw-2 names are related to a particular lower-level model, so you do not have to be concerned\line about name collisions among windows. This gives you an opportunity to use single-\line \expndtw-4 window applications as building blocks. The disadvantage is that more levels of message\line \expndtw-1 sends will be generated.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri22\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 When an application wants to update a subpane which is outside of the current active\line \expndtw-3 window, it should make the subpane's window the active window first. If it does not, the\line \expndtw1 portions of the subpane obscured by other windows will be overwritten.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1979\margrsxn2283\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 14: Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes    241}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb324\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-13\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Graphic Classes}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li14\fi0\ri18\sb220\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Smalltalk/V \b0 graphics are generated by bitmapped operations. In fact, \b Small talk/\b0 V uses\line \expndtw0 bitmapped graphics to generate the entire user interface.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A \i Bitmap \i0 is simply a linear array of bits. Each bit has a value of 1 or 0, with 1 representing\line \expndtw-1 white and 0 black. Since a monochrome display screen is a two dimensional plane of\line \expndtw-5 pixels, instances of class \b Form \b0 provide a two dimensional view of the bitmap to represent\line \expndtw-3 the monochrome screen. A Form has a \b bitmap, \b0 a \b width \b0 and a \b height, \b0 which allows you\line \expndtw-4 to manipulate the bitmap as if it were a two dimensional array of bits. The \b DisplayScreen\line \b0\expndtw-2 represents a monochrome screen which is a special kind of Form, and hence a subclass\line of class \b Form.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A ColorScreen \b0 or a \b ColorForm \b0 (both are subclasses of \b Form) \b0 consists of an array of\line \expndtw0 bitmaps. This additional dimension allows colors other than black and white to be\line \expndtw-2 recorded. All bits at the same location of each bitmap collectively represent the color of\line \expndtw1 the pixel at that location. For example, if the bit at location 0@0 in the first bitmap is\line \expndtw-1 1, and the bits at the same location in the second, third, and fourth bitmap are 1, 0, and\line \expndtw-2 0, then the color code for the top left pixel is the binary number 0011 (the bit in the first\line \expndtw-4 bitmap is least significant) or 3 in decimal. The EGA and VGA graphics controllers allow\line \expndtw-2 a maximum of four bitmaps, thus a maximum of 16 colors are available to be displayed\line \expndtw0 at any one time.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri22\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Almost all bitmapped operations involve moving bits from one place to another.\line \expndtw-1 Naturally, you might think that you would implement this by simply sending messages\line \expndtw-2 to a \b Form. \b0 Due to the complexity of these operations, however, another class, called\line \b\expndtw0 BitBlt, \b0 is created to handle all bitmapped operations.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri22\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Bitmapped operations address a bit or an area of bits in a Form. A \b Point \b0 addresses an\line \expndtw1 individual bit, while a \b Rectangle \b0 refers to a block of bits.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri25\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Bitmapped graphics, then, is centered around four classes and their subclasses: \b Point,\line Rectangle, Form, \b0 and \b BitBlt. \b0 The rest of the chapter describes each of these classes in\line \expndtw-5 detail.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb364\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Point}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri18\sb212\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A Point addresses a bit within the bitmap of a two dimensional Form. It has two instance\line \expndtw-3 variables: x, representing the column (horizontal) coordinate, and y, representing the row\line \expndtw1 (vertical) coordinate. The value of x increases to the right and \b y \b0 to the bottom.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri22\sb151\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The most efficient way to create a Point is by sending the \i @ \i0 message to an Integer. For\line \expndtw2 example, the top left corner of a Form can be addressed by the Point:}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1319\margrsxn1914\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1073\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 242    Chapter 14: Smalltalk/ V 286 Classes}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1458\fi0\ri0\sb324\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 0<S>0}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li1062\fi0\ri4\sb162\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 where the first integer (receiver) is the x coordinate and the second integer (argument) the\line \expndtw-2 y coordinate. The x: and y: messages alter the coordinates of a Point, while the \b x \b0 and y\line \expndtw-3 messages retrieve these coordinates. A Point can also be compared with another Point.\line Following are some examples:}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2784\margrsxn5388\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3409\posnegy115\absw853\absh-2631\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Result}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb191\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3409\posnegy115\absw853\absh-2631\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 1}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3409\posnegy115\absw853\absh-2631\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-20\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 100}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3409\posnegy115\absw853\absh-2631\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 50 @ 100}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3409\posnegy115\absw853\absh-2631\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 1 @ 50}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3409\posnegy115\absw853\absh-2631\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtx