}}}{\sp{\sn pictureGray}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn pWrapPolygonVertices}{\sv 8;9;(0,0);(0,19382);(0,19382);(0,21600);(5660,21600);(5660,19382);(21600,19382);(21600,0);(0,0)}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fIsBullet}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fAllowOverlap}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fEditedWrap}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fBehindDocument}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fPrint}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn dxWrapDistLeft}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn dxWrapDistRight}{\sv 0}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb2912\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 15.1\line \b\expndtw-4 Smalltalk/V \b0 Screen}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi259\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-133\slmult0\tx2329 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex93\expndtw-2\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 "Draw a Mandala."\line Display fill: rectangle{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw0 *}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li266\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-133\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex93\expndtw-1\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 rule: \b Fora \b0 over}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi263\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-133\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex93\expndtw-3\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 mask: (Display coapatibleHask color: 8).\line \expndtw-4 pen \b homo!}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li274\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-133\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex93\expndtw-7\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 north;}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li266\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-133\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 mask:   (Display compatihleHask color:   8);}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li263\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-133\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 \'95\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0 tandala:   24 diameter:   388.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1861\margrsxn2441\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri4\sb248\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Every window in \b Smalltalk/V \b0 has a \i label bar \i0 and is surrounded by a \i border. \i0 The area\line inside the border is divided into one or more \i panes. \i0 In our example, the Workspace and\line \expndtw-2 the System Transcript each have a single pane, and the Class Browser has three panes.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb360\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 The Keypad}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri0\sb216\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The arrow that moves around the screen is the \i cursor. \i0 You move the cursor by pressing\line \expndtw-4 the \b cursor arrow \b0 keys on the keypad, as shown in Figure 15.2. Pressing an \b arrow \b0 key\line \expndtw-3 moves the cursor one space in the direction of the arrow. Pressing the \b arrow \b0 key while\line holding down the shift key makes the cursor jump several spaces in the direction of the\line \expndtw-6 arrow.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li14\fi0\ri4\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 If you have a mouse, the left button serves as the \b select \b0 key and the right button for other\line functions. These keys are described throughout this chapter. You can reassign these keys,\line \expndtw0 and any other keyboard keys if you wish.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1620\margrsxn1545\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex33\expndtw25\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 II.\expndtw0  \expndtw4 I}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1138\fi0\ri0\sb227\sa918 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 264    Chapter 15: Smalltalk/V 286 Environment}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn3096\margrsxn1642\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols3\colno1\colw1994\colsr1066\colno2\colw1116\colsr353\colno3\colw2642 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2916\shptop108\shpright2916\shpbottom2880\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft7250\shptop-497\shpright7250\shpbottom2887\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 8890}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb2455\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 15.2}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Cursor Movement Keys}\par \pard\plain\fs2\sa1901\sl-1\slmult0\column\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-670 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx576 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx1116 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-119\slmult0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 F9\line \expndtw-4 cycle\line windows}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-119\slmult0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 F10\line \expndtw-1 cycle\line \expndtw-3 panes}\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard\pard\plain\fs2\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\column\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-662 \clvmgf\clvertalt\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx533 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx1059 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx1570 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2081 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2643 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi-4\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-140\slmult0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 7\line \expndtw-3 scroll\line \expndtw-2 left}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\super\cf0\charscalex69\expndtw-9\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs32 8\nosupersub T}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-140\slmult0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 9}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi-7\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-140\slmult0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 scroll\line \expndtw-4 up}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi-7\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-140\slmult0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 extend\line \expndtw-1 select}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-634 \clvmrg\clvertalt\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx533 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx1059 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx1570 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2081 \clvmgf\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2643 {\par \cell }\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 4}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 <\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\f2\cchs0 \'97}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 5}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-212\slmult0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 6\line \expndtw49 -\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\f2\cchs0 \'bb}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi-4\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-788\slmult0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 +\line \expndtw-1 select}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-641 \clvmrg\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx533 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx1059 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx1570 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2081 \clvmrg\clvertalt\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2643 {\par \cell }\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi7\ri7\sb0\sa0\sl-140\slmult0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 1\line \expndtw-3 scroll\line \expndtw-2 right}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 2}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex56\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs32 A}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi-4\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-137\slmult0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 3\line \expndtw-3 scroll\line down}\cell {\par \cell }\pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-634 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx1059 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2081 \clvmrg\clvertalt\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2643 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li202\fi0\ri158\sb0\sa0\sl-140\slmult0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 window\line \expndtw-3 menu}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li230\fi0\ri227\sb0\sa0\sl-140\slmult0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 pane\line \expndtw-5 menu}\cell {\par \cell }\pard\intbl\row \pard\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1620\margrsxn1545\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li1127\fi0\ri0\sb248\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 If your mouse has three buttons, pressing the middle button produces a beep. You can,\line \expndtw-4 however, modify the behavior of the mouse, as well as anything else in the environment.\line \expndtw-2 Soon you will feel comfortable enough with \b Smalltalk/V \b0 to customize your system. If\line \expndtw-3 you want to program the third mouse button, start with the method \b initialState \b0 in class\line \b\expndtw-2 TerminalStream. \b0 Or, if you find that the scroll speed is too fast or too slow you may\line \expndtw0 want to modify the method \b scrollDelay: \b0 in the class \b ScrollDispatcher.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1134\fi0\ri0\sb374\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Active Window}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li1130\fi0\ri14\sb227\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To \i select \i0 a window, move the cursor into the window and press the \b select \b0 key, or, if you\line \expndtw-5 have a mouse, position the cursor within the window and click (quickly press and release)\line \expndtw1 the left mouse button.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li1130\fi0\ri22\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The window that you have selected is called the \i active \i0 window. The active window is\line \expndtw-5 always on top of all other windows and its label bar is reversed. A window remains active\line \expndtw-2 regardless of whether or not the cursor is inside it. To deactivate a window, move the\line \expndtw1 cursor outside of the window, and press the select key or the left mouse button.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li1134\fi0\ri25\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The \i screen \i0 is considered the active window if you last pressed the \b select \b0 key when the\line \expndtw-2 cursor was outside of all windows. When no window is active, all of the label bars have\line \expndtw-3 a normal appearance.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2426\margrsxn1854\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 15: Smalltalk/V 286 Environment    265}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb331\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Cycling}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri7\sb223\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Smalltalk/V \b0 provides a fast way to move the cursor about the screen. Pressing the \b cycle\line \expndtw0 windows \b0 key moves the cursor to the next window in a clockwise direction and\line \expndtw-4 automatically activates it. This is called \i window cycling.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li18\fi0\ri7\sb140\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Similarly, pressing the \b cycle panes \b0 key moves the cursor from pane to pane in a clockwise\line \expndtw-3 direction within a window. This is called \i pane cycling.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li25\fi0\ri0\sb378\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Using Menus}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb428\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 System Menu}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri7\sb212\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Menus are the standard way of giving commands to \b Smalltalk/V. \b0 The \i system \i0 menu has\line commands for creating new windows, saving your work, exiting the environment, and\line \expndtw-2 redrawing the screen.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri4\sb148\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To pop up the system menu, move the cursor outside all windows on the screen, and\line \expndtw-4 press either the \b window menu \b0 key or the \b pane menu \b0 key, or, if you have a mouse, click\line \expndtw2 the right button.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri4\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To \i select a menu function, \i0 move the cursor to the desired function and press the \b select \b0 key\line \expndtw2 (the line on which the cursor sits becomes reversed to show that it is selected).\line \b\expndtw0 Smalltalk/V \b0 immediately performs the action, and the menu disappears.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To \i leave a menu \i0 without performing any function, move the cursor outside the menu in\line \expndtw3 any direction. If you have a mouse, then click the left mouse button. The menu\line \expndtw-6 disappears.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb133\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The other functions of the system menu are described in detail in subsequent chapters.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb360\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Window and Pane Menus}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri4\sb209\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Smalltalk/V \b0 includes several menus, some of which are shown in Figure 15.3. You must\line \expndtw-3 leave a menu before you can pop up a different menu. The menu that you get at any time\line \expndtw1 is determined by the cursor location and which \b menu \b0 key you use.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri4\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To pop up a \i window menu, \i0 move the cursor into a window and press the \b window menu\line \b0 key or, if you have a mouse, click the right button. If you have a mouse, the cursor must\line \expndtw-2 be on the label bar, any border line of the window, or any pane border line within the\line \expndtw0 window. The window menu contains functions specific to that window.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1321\margrsxn1948\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1008\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa407 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 266    Chapter 15: Smalltalk/V 286 Environment}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1321\margrsxn7575\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw720\colsr576\colno2\colw1717 \pard \plain \li0\ri0\sb0\sa0\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx3312\posnegy0\absw0\absh3254\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\pict\picw9067\pich5740\picwgoal5140\pichgoal3254\jpegblip
}\par\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-133\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx7506\posnegy2318\absw932\absh-537\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 broMse disk\line \expndtw-7 open workspace\line broMse classes\line \expndtw-6 redraw screen}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-133\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx7510\posnegy2851\absw666\absh-270\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 save inage\line run dean}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb1660\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\super\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 1\nosupersub  u}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb2959\sa0\sl-209\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 15.3\line \b Smalltalk/V \b0 Menus}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1321\margrsxn1948\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-7\shptop1883\shpright-7\shpbottom5980\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-158\shptop4799\shpright-158\shpbottom7125\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 20320}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li997\fi0\ri18\sb349\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To pop up a \i pane menu, \i0 move the cursor into a pane of the window and press the \b pane\line \expndtw0 menu \b0 key or, if you have a mouse, click the right button. The pane menu contains\line functions specific to that pane.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li1001\fi0\ri0\sb140\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 If you press either menu key or the right mouse button when the cursor is outside of\line every window, the system menu is popped up.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1019\fi0\ri0\sb378\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Manipulating Windows}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1004\fi0\ri0\sb425\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-14\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 Opening a Workspace}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li1001\fi0\ri11\sb202\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Windows are usually opened from menus. To \i open a new workspace, \i0 select \b open\line \expndtw-4 workspace \b0 from the system menu. An active \b workspace \b0 window opens up. This window\line can be closed, collapsed or resized using the label bar buttons and manipulated like other\line \expndtw0 windows using the window menu.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1008\fi0\ri0\sb349\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-13\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 Label Bar}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li1004\fi0\ri14\sb202\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The label bar, shown in Figure 15.4, displays the window title along with two or more\line \expndtw-1 small buttons, depending on which \b Smalltalk/V \b0 window is open. The buttons provide\line \expndtw-2 quick access to specific window activities.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li1004\fi0\ri18\sb137\sa0\sl-245\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To select a button, place the cursor on the button and click the left mouse button or use\line \expndtw3 the numeric keypad \b + \b0 key.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1008\fi0\ri0\sb130\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Close Button: \b0 When selected, the window closes and disappears from the screen.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1970\margrsxn2313\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4230\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa356 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 15: Smalltalk/V 286 Environment    267}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1970\margrsxn2313\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720 \pard \plain \li0\ri0\sb0\sa0\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx295\posnegy0\absw0\absh3305\nowrap\dfrmtxtx10080\dfrmtxty0 {\pict\picw11874\pich5829\picwgoal6732\pichgoal3304\jpegblip
}\par\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx2938\posnegy1112\absw0\absh-144\nowrap\dfrmtxtx10080\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 This window is in the process of being}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-281\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx288\posnegy1174\absw717\absh-565\nowrap\dfrmtxtx10080\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 collapse\line \expndtw-2 resize}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx292\posnegy2455\absw1112\absh-882\nowrap\dfrmtxtx10080\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 15.4\line \expndtw-7 Label Bar\line \expndtw-5 and Window\line \expndtw-8 Resizing}\par {\pard\plain \sb0\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1970\margrsxn2313\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri4\sb425\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Zoom Button: \b0 When selected, \b Smalltalk/V \b0 zooms in on the text pane so that it fills the\line \expndtw-1 whole screen. To unzoom the text pane, click on the label bar and the window redraws\line to its original configuration. You can also use the F8 function key to zoom a text pane.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri4\sb144\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Collapse Button: \b0 When selected, the window collapses to show only the label bar. If the\line window is already collapsed, selecting this button expands the window to its original size\line \expndtw1 and position on the screen.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri4\sb158\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Resize Button: \b0 Select this button and the system responds with a rectangle outline for\line \expndtw-2 resizing the window, shown in Figure 15.4.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li410\fi0\ri403\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 With a mouse. \i0 With the cursor on the resize button, press and hold down the left\line \expndtw-1 mouse button while you move the mouse to drag the cursor and resize the\line \expndtw0 rectangle outline. Release the mouse button to redraw the window.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li410\fi0\ri403\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 With the keypad. \i0 Select the \b resize button \b0 with the numeric keypad + key; then\line \expndtw-5 use the keyboard cursor keys to move the cursor and resize the rectangle outline.\line \expndtw1 Press and release the numeric keypad + key to redraw the window.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb356\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Common Window Menu Functions}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The window menu of every window has functions that apply to the window as a whole.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri7\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To \i move a window, \i0 select move from the window menu of the window you want to move\line \expndtw-2 or move the cursor over the window label and hold down the left mouse button. You'll\line \expndtw-3 then see a rectangle outline that is the size of the window being moved. Move the cursor\line \expndtw-4 until the rectangle outline is in the desired location and press the \b select \b0 key or release the\line \expndtw1 left mouse button. \b Smalltalk/V \b0 moves the window to its new location.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2363\margrsxn1907\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li97\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 268     \i Chapter 15: Smalltalk/ V 286 Environment}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li76\fi0\ri0\sb324\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To \i frame or resize a window, \i0 pop up the window menu and select the frame function.\line \b\expndtw-1 Smalltalk/V \b0 responds with a rectangle outline, as shown in Figure 15.4. Move the\line \expndtw-4 rectangle until the lower right corner is in the location you want, and press the \b select \b0 key\line \expndtw1 or click the left mouse button. \b Smalltalk/V \b0 and changes the window's size.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li65\fi0\ri4\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To change the color of a window, pop up the window menu and select the \b color \b0 option.\line A second menu comes up from which you can choose \b\i text \i0 color \b0 or \b background color.\line \b0\expndtw-2 Selecting either one causes a third menu containing a palette of 16 colors to appear.\line Choosing a color makes either the text or background color of the window change\line \expndtw-5 accordingly.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li61\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Collapse \b0 causes the window \i to \i0 be collapsed so that only the label bar is visible. The\line \expndtw-1 contents of the window remain intact; you just can't see them. To make the contents\line \expndtw-3 visible again, select frame from the menu and reframe the window or select \b collapse \b0 a\line \expndtw0 second time and the window will open to its previous size and position.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li54\fi0\ri11\sb144\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Cycle causes a window underneath other windows to pop up on top and become the\line active window. This is the same as pressing the \b window cycle (F9) \b0 key.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li43\fi0\ri11\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Label \b0 lets you type in a new label for the window. When \b label \b0 is selected, \b Smalltalk/V\line \b0\expndtw-4 pops up a prompter window where you can type a new label. Just type the new label, and\line \expndtw-2 press the \b return \b0 key when finished.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li43\fi0\ri0\sb133\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Close \b0 causes the window and its contents to disappear.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li54\fi0\ri0\sb367\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-18\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Panes}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li40\fi0\ri14\sb220\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Windows are composed of one or more panes. There are three kinds of panes: \i text \i0 panes,\line \i list \i0 panes, and \i graph \i0 panes.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li18\fi0\ri14\sb151\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Many of the windows in the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 environment have panes that allow you to\line \expndtw-4 modify or edit text. These are called \i text \i0 panes. The System Transcript is a window with\line \expndtw-3 only a single text pane, as is any Workspace. These and all other text panes use the same\line \expndtw-1 text editor.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri14\sb166\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Other windows in the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 environment have panes that allow you to select from\line \expndtw0 a list of items. These are called \i list \i0 panes. Windows that have list panes are usually\line \expndtw-5 referred to as \i browsers. \i0 The Class Browser is an example of a window with two list panes\line \expndtw1 and one text pane.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri18\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The third kind of pane, \i graph \i0 pane, allows you to draw pictures. Since graph panes are\line not used by any of the standard windows in the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 environment, they are not\line \expndtw-1 explained in this chapter. Refer to the graphics and windows tutorials and reference\line sections for more information.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1982\margrsxn2274\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4241\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa709 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 15: Smalltalk/V 286 Environment    269}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1982\margrsxn2274\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720 \pard \plain \li0\ri0\sb0\sa0\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx2315\posnegy0\absw0\absh561\nowrap\dfrmtxtx10080\dfrmtxty0 {\pict\picw8940\pich990\picwgoal5068\pichgoal561\jpegblip
}\par{\pard\plain \sb0\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1982\margrsxn2274\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3236\fi0\ri0\sb112\sa0\sl-137\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 This is sample text.  It will scroll upward and out\line \expndtw-5 of sight as you click and drag the mouse downward\line \expndtw-7 ' within this pane.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li349\fi0\ri0\sb29\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 scroll bar}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li353\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa598 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 scroll cursor}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2338\margrsxn2969\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw957\colsr1908\colno2\colw3736 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft1958\shptop-2228\shpright1958\shpbottom990\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 13970}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2556\shptop-1919\shpright2556\shpbottom385\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft1901\shptop-306\shpright1901\shpbottom313\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft6898\shptop-1933\shpright6898\shpbottom385\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 52705}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb173\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 15.5\line \expndtw-1 Pane with\line \expndtw-7 Scroll Bar\line \expndtw-3 and Cursor}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li140\fi-140\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-133\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 Scrolling will cause this text to nove upward in this\line \expndtw-6 pane, revealing the text which is below and currently}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li144\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx3737 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex139\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs10 not   ,,1,11,1.{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1982\margrsxn2274\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb137\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Scrolling}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri7\sb216\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 There are many instances when the contents of a pane are larger than the pane itself. You\line \expndtw1 can think of a pane as a screen which lets you see only a portion of a pane's contents,\line \expndtw-2 as shown in Figure 15.5. \i Scrolling \i0 lets you move this screen around the text so that you\line \expndtw1 can see a different portion of it.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri14\sb144\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 You can scroll through a file using either the mouse or keypad keys. However, when you\line \expndtw1 use the mouse, you have access to the \b scroll bar.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri14\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The scroll bar displays the relative location of the visible contents of the file to the file\line \expndtw-4 as a whole. By positioning the scroll cursor on the scroll bar and releasing the right mouse\line \expndtw0 button, you \i quick jump \i0 around the file.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri14\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Experiment with this often missed feature. It is particularly useful for use with large files\line \expndtw0 where scrolling would be time consuming.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb335\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 Scrolling With the Keyboard}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri14\sb202\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To scroll \i vertically, \i0 use the \b PgUp \b0 and \b PgDn \b0 keys. Pressing \b PgUp \b0 moves the pane\line \expndtw2 contents up one line, while pressing \b PgDn \b0 moves the pane contents down one line.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri11\sb144\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To scroll \i horizontally, \i0 use the \b Home \b0 and \b End \b0 keys. Pressing Home moves the pane\line \expndtw2 contents four characters to the right. Pressing \b End \b0 moves the pane contents four\line \expndtw1 characters to the left.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2345\margrsxn1925\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li32\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 270    Chapter 15: Smalltalk/ V 286 Environment}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li18\fi0\ri7\sb324\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Holding down the shift key when pressing any of the four scrolling keys causes the pane\line \expndtw-1 contents to move a larger amount in the indicated direction. For vertical scrolling, the\line pane contents move almost the entire height of the pane. For horizontal scrolling, the\line \expndtw1 pane contents move one-half of the pane width.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb295\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex80\expndtw1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Scrolling With \i0 a \i Mouse}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li14\fi0\ri7\sb191\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 There are two ways to scroll a pane using a mouse. One way is to grab a character and\line \expndtw-5 pull it to the position in the pane where you want it. Continuous scrolling is also available.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li14\fi0\ri4\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 In the \i grab and pull \i0 technique, the grab location is the position of the cursor when you\line \expndtw-1 press the right mouse button. Position the cursor at a character in the last line of a text\line \expndtw1 pane in the active window. Press the right mouse button. Keeping the button down,\line \expndtw-3 move the cursor to the first line of the pane and a few characters over to the left. Release\line \expndtw2 the button. If you did not move the cursor out of the pane before you released the\line \expndtw-1 button, you will see that the text has been pulled to the location of the cursor when the\line button was released.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri0\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 For a \i horizontal continuous scroll, \i0 press the right button while the cursor is in the pane you\line \expndtw-1 want to scroll. Holding the button down, move the cursor to the right of the pane, then\line \expndtw-3 back inside the pane, then move it outside to the left of the pane. Do not allow the cursor\line \expndtw-2 to go above or below the pane. Now release the button. While the cursor is back inside\line the pane, scrolling pauses. When the cursor is moved back out of the pane, scrolling is\line \expndtw0 resumed. When the button is released, scrolling ends.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri4\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 For a \i vertical continuous scroll, \i0 press the right button down while the cursor is in the pane\line \expndtw-2 you want to scroll. Holding the button down, move the cursor above the pane or on the\line \expndtw-1 top border of the pane. Notice that the pane scrolls down. Similarly, if you move the\line \expndtw2 cursor below the pane or on the bottom border, the pane scrolls up.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri7\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Vertical scrolling speed \i is \i0 controlled by the horizontal position of the cursor in relation\line \expndtw-2 to the width of the pane. As you move the cursor to the left, the speed slowly decreases\line \expndtw-1 until you move the cursor past the left border of the pane. At this point, scrolling speed\line \expndtw-3 is at its slowest. As you move the cursor to the right, the speed gradually increases until\line \expndtw0 you move past the right border of the pane. Now scrolling is at its maximum speed,\line \expndtw1 almost a page at a time.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri7\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To \i pause \i0 during the scroll, move the cursor back into the pane. To \i resume \i0 scrolling, move\line \expndtw-3 the cursor out of the pane as you did to start the scroll. To \i terminate \i0 scrolling, release the\line \expndtw-1 button.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri4\sb162\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To \i quick jump \i0 through large chunks of text without scrolling, position the scroll cursor\line on the scroll bar to locate the section of the file you want to see, and release the right\line \expndtw-2 mouse button. The pane will now show the area of the file you located on the scroll bar.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2046\margrsxn2249\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri11\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 1\}: Smalltalk/ V 286 Environment    271}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb328\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Text Editor}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb396\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex82\expndtw-3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Inserting Text}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri4\sb209\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Whenever you press the \b select \b0 key, an I-beam is drawn between two characters to mark\line \expndtw-4 the \i text insertion point. \i0 As you type characters, they appear in front of the text insertion\line \expndtw-3 point, which moves to the right with each keystroke. If you press the backspace key, the\line characters in front of the insertion point is deleted, and the insertion point moves a space\line \expndtw2 to the left.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri4\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To \i move the insertion point, \i0 place the cursor at the new position and press the \b select \b0 key.\line \expndtw1 The insertion point jumps to the cursor position.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri0\sb140\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Whenever the cursor is outside the text editing pane, if you try to type a character, your\line system beeps, and the character does not appear. You can only edit the contents of a text\line \expndtw1 pane if the cursor is inside the pane.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb313\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex82\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Return, Tab, and Backspace Keys}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Pressing the \b return \b0 key moves the insertion point to the beginning of a new line. If the\line \expndtw-2 insertion point was in the middle of a line, the line is split into two lines at the insertion\line point.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri4\sb144\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 If you press the \b tab \b0 key, blanks will be inserted at the insertion point to make it move\line \expndtw2 to the next tab stop. In this editor, tab stops occur every four spaces.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri4\sb144\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 If you press the \b backspace \b0 key, the character in front of the insertion point is deleted.\line \expndtw-1 Notice that if the insertion point is at the beginning of a line and backspace is pressed,\line \expndtw1 the line is joined to the line above.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb320\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex82\expndtw-2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Selecting, Replacing, and Deleting}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb205\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To \i select text, \i0 move the cursor to either the beginning or end of the text to be selected.\line This position can be at any character, even in the middle of a word. Press the \b select \b0 key\line \expndtw-1 to bring the insertion point to the cursor. Now move the cursor to the other end of the\line \expndtw-2 text to be selected (again, at any character position) and press the \b extend selection \b0 key\line \expndtw-5 The entire selected area is reversed. Notice what happens if you move the cursor and press\line \expndtw-3 the \b extend selection \b0 key again. The selected (reversed) area of text now ends at the new\line \expndtw-1 cursor position. You can continue to move the cursor and adjust the selected text by\line \expndtw-2 pressing the \b extend selection \b0 key until you've selected the text you want as shown in\line \expndtw-6 Figure 15.6.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1950\margrsxn2259\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 212     Chapter 15: Smalltalk/ V 286 Environment}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3244\fi0\ri0\sb1447\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 This text is not selected.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4622\fi0\ri0\sb263\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 D, but this is not.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li378\fi0\ri0\sb1368\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 15.6\line \expndtw-6 Selected Text}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri14\sb346\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 If you press the \b select \b0 key, the selected text is deselected (no longer reversed) and the\line \expndtw0 insertion point appears at the cursor.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb133\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Selecting text with a mouse works in a similar fashion.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri11\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To \i insert text \i0 in a \i text \i0 pane of the active window, position the cursor where you want the\line \expndtw-2 insertion point to be, then click the left mouse button. Now the I-beam appears and you\line \expndtw-3 can type.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri4\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To \i select text \i0 in the active window, you can use a method similar to using the \b extend\line \expndtw-2 selection \b0 key. First move the cursor to the point where you want to begin or end your\line \expndtw-1 selection, and click the left button. To extend the selection, move the cursor to the other\line end of the text then hold down the \b shift \b0 key, and press the left mouse button. The text\line \expndtw1 selection will now extend to the current cursor location.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri4\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 You can also select text using the \i draw through \i0 method. Position the cursor at one end\line \expndtw1 of the text you want selected. Now press the left mouse button. Hold the button down\line \expndtw0 as you move the cursor to the other end of the selection. Notice that as you move the\line \expndtw-2 cursor, the selection (the reversed text) follows and includes the current cursor location.\line Draw through terminates when you release the button. Note that if you move the cursor\line \expndtw-1 outside the pane while holding the left mouse button down, the pane will scroll while\line extending the selection.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri0\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To \i select a single character, \i0 position the cursor at the character you want to select. Then\line \expndtw-2 press down the left button and hold it until the character is reversed. This takes only a\line \expndtw0 fraction of a second.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To \i select a whole word, \i0 position the cursor anywhere on the word to be selected and\line double click the left mouse button. The word is reversed.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1624\margrsxn2603\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri14\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 15: Smalltalk/ V 286 Environment    273}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri47\sb302\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To \i select a line, \i0 place the cursor just inside the window border to the left of the line you\line \expndtw2 wish to select and click the left mouse button twice.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri43\sb151\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To \i replace \i0 text, select the text to replace and then type the new text. As you type,\line \b\expndtw1 Smalltalk/V \b0 replaces the selected text with the new text.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri40\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To \i deletefotge \i0 amounts of text, select the text and press the backspace key. To delete text\line \expndtw-2 one character at a time, place the insertion point at the end of the text to be deleted and\line \expndtw-1 press the backspace key.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb342\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Saving and Restoring}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri22\sb212\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The text editor in \b Smalltalk/V \b0 is always working with a text copy of some underlying\line object in the system. Among other things, this can be a file, a string, or some Smalltalk\line \expndtw-3 code. For example, the System Transcript and any Workspace edit strings of characters,\line \expndtw-1 and the text pane in the Class Hierarchy Browser edits Smalltalk code. Because a copy\line \expndtw0 is being edited, you must tell the environment when editing is complete. \b Smalltalk/V\line \b0\expndtw-1 can then store the edited text back in the original place. You can also restore the text in\line \expndtw0 the pane to its previous state, if you wish.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb130\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Every pane that allows text editing has editing functions on its pane menu.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li14\fi0\ri18\sb140\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The \i restore \i0 function replaces the text in the pane with the text representation of the\line \expndtw-3 underlying object being edited. If you are editing a string, then the string replaces the text\line in the pane. If you are editing a file, the text in the file is reread into the pane. If you are\line \expndtw0 editing Smalltalk code, then the source code currently being used by the system is put\line in the pane.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li14\fi0\ri14\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The \i save \i0 function in the pane menu tells \b Smalltalk/V \b0 that editing is complete.\line \b\expndtw0 Smalltalk/V \b0 responds by updating the underlying object being edited with the text\line \expndtw-3 currently in the pane. For example, if a file is being edited, then the file is rewritten with\line \expndtw2 the text in the pane.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb353\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Cutting, Copying, and Pasting}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li18\fi0\ri4\sb209\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The text editor has a buffer that can be used to transfer text from place to place. Text\line \expndtw-3 is placed in this buffer by either \i cutting \i0 or \i copying \i0 it from the pane. After text has been\line \expndtw-1 placed in the edit buffer, it can be \i pasted \i0 anywhere inside of a text pane. This is shown\line \expndtw-5 in Figure 15.7.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li22\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To place text in the edit buffer you must first select the text. Then, pop up the pane menu\line \expndtw-1 and select either \b cut \b0 or copy. If the \i cut \i0 function is selected, \b Smalltalk/V \b0 responds by\line \expndtw0 replacing the contents of the edit buffer with the selected text, and then deleting the\line \expndtw-4 selected text from the pane. If the \i copy \i0 function is selected, the selected text is not deleted\line \expndtw2 from the pane. Instead a copy of the text replaces the contents of the edit buffer.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1502\margrsxn1802\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-36\shptop623\shpright-36\shpbottom1451\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li983\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 274    \i Chapter 15: Smalltalk/V 286 Environment}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft3629\shptop306\shpright4011\shpbottom306\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 2540}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft3226\shptop342\shpright5746\shpbottom342\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri3542\sb356\sa162 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 Smalltalk^ Transcript}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn4771\margrsxn1997\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw2199\colsr738\colno2\colw2203 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-36\shptop-151\shpright2498\shpbottom-151\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-29\shptop-310\shpright-29\shpbottom489\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2455\shptop-310\shpright2455\shpbottom496\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 15875}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft5141\shptop-252\shpright5141\shpbottom2671\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\pard\plain \sb0\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\pard \plain \li0\ri0\sb0\sa0\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx29\posnegy619\absw0\absh835\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\pict\picw4648\pich1473\picwgoal2635\pichgoal835\jpegblip
}\par\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx1253\posnegy569\absw0\absh-140\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 Workspace}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-133\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 This text has been cut and pasted\line into several places in three\line \expndtw-8 windows.}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb324\sa0\sl-133\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 This text has been cut and pasted\line into several places in three\line \expndtw-9 windows.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb529\sa0\sl-133\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 This text has been cut and pasted\line into several places in three\line \expndtw-9 windows.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1502\margrsxn1802\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-43\shptop-25\shpright-43\shpbottom148\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3618\fi0\ri0\sb40\sa76\sl-137\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 This text has been cut and pasted\line into several places in three\line \expndtw-9 windows.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2802\margrsxn1993\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols3\colno1\colw1666\colsr655\colno2\colw2239\colsr353\colno3\colw2199 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2020\shptop-806\shpright2020\shpbottom728\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft4604\shptop-806\shpright4604\shpbottom483\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 13970}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb407\sa0\sl-212\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 15.7\line \expndtw-5 Cutting and Pasting}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li22\fi0\ri0\sb461\sa0\sl-126\slmult0\tlul\tx2239 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 This text has been cut and pasted\line \ul\expndtw-7 into several places in three{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-137\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 This text has been cut and pasted\line into several places in three\line \expndtw0 windowsT}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1502\margrsxn1802\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-101\shptop241\shpright-101\shpbottom1400\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 29845}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-29\shptop241\shpright-29\shpbottom4316\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 8890}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li983\fi0\ri11\sb454\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Text in the edit buffer can be pasted into the pane by either inserting it into a new place\line \expndtw1 or replacing some existing text. To insert the contents of the edit buffer, place the\line \expndtw-2 insertion point at the desired position and then select the \b paste \b0 function from the pane\line \expndtw0 menu. To replace some text with the contents of the edit buffer, first select the text to\line \expndtw1 be replaced and then select the \b paste \b0 function from the pane menu.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li983\fi0\ri11\sb140\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The paste function leaves the contents of the edit buffer unchanged. This means that the\line \expndtw0 same text can be pasted several times and in different places.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li983\fi0\ri7\sb151\sa360\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Since the same edit buffer is shared by all of the text panes, you can easily transfer text\line \expndtw-3 between windows. First select the text to be transferred. Next, place this text into the edit\line \expndtw-2 buffer by using the pane menu to either cut it or copy it. Then move the cursor into the\line \expndtw-3 new window and either place the insertion point where the text is to be inserted or select\line \expndtw0 some existing text that is to be replaced. Now, use the \b paste \b0 function from the pane\line menu. The text appears in the new window.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1502\margrsxn1802\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw720\colsr263\colno2\colw7621\linebetcol \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 .!}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Saving the Image}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri4\sb220\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The \i image \i0 is all of the Smalltalk objects, both code and data, that make up the\line \b\expndtw-3 Smalltalk/V \b0 environment. The image is read from the image file when the system starts\line up. In this way, the objects are loaded into memory. These objects include the windows\line \expndtw1 that appear on the screen.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Since \b Smalltalk/V \b0 is an interactive and modifiable environment, the image is constantly\line \expndtw-3 being changed as you use and modify \b Smalltalk/V. \b0 These modifications are not written\line \expndtw0 on the disk until you ask them to be written. This can be done at any time by selecting}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2122\margrsxn2159\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 15: Smalltalk/V 286 Environment    275}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li22\fi0\ri0\sb299\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 the \i save image \i0 function from the system menu. You can also save the image while exiting\line \expndtw-3 as described below. The next time you start up the system, it resumes exactly as it was\line \expndtw-1 when the \b image \b0 Hie was last written.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li18\fi0\ri4\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The \b image \b0 file on the disk represents the last saved version; therefore it also becomes the\line \expndtw-3 starting point in the event of a system crash or a major mistake. For these reasons, you\line \expndtw-1 should maintain a recent backup of the image file along with the \b source \b0 file and the\line \b\expndtw-2 change log \b0 that is associated with these files. \b Maintaining Smalltalk/V, \b0 later in this\line \expndtw2 chapter, explains the relationships between these files in more detail, and gives\line \expndtw-3 instructions on maintaining them. It also gives advice on how to recover from a system\line \expndtw0 crash or other problem.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li29\fi0\ri0\sb374\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Exiting Smalltalk/V}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri7\sb227\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To exit \b Smalltalk/V, \b0 select \b exit Smalltalk \b0 from the system menu. You'll then see\line \expndtw-3 another menu, asking whether to remember or throw away the changes made since the\line \expndtw-2 environment was started.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri7\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Selecting the \i save image \i0 function causes the state of the system, including the location and\line \expndtw-2 contents of all the windows, to be saved. When you start \b Smalltalk/V \b0 the next time, it\line \expndtw1 will be restored to the saved state.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri7\sb158\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Selecting the \i forget image \i0 function causes all of the changes made since \b Smalltalk/V \b0 was\line \expndtw-2 started to be forgotten. When \b Smalltalk/V \b0 is started the next time, it will be restored to\line \expndtw0 the previous saved state (the way it was when it was started this time).}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri11\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Selecting the \i continue \i0 function returns you back to the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 environment. This\line \expndtw0 has the same effect as leaving the menu without selecting anything.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li22\fi0\ri0\sb374\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Evaluating Smalltalk Expressions}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri14\sb227\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The Smalltalk language includes expressions which are similar to expressions in other\line \expndtw-2 programming languages. In the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 environment, you can enter the text for an\line \expndtw-5 expression in any text pane, evaluate it, and display the result. You specify what you want\line \expndtw4 to do in the environment by using pop-up menus and by evaluating Smalltalk\line \expndtw-1 expressions, which serve as the \b Smalltalk/V \b0 command language.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1318\margrsxn1926\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw720\colsr328\colno2\colw7617\linebetcol \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li32\fi0\ri0\sb2074\sa0\sl-720\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-310\dn12\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs102 1.}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 216     Chapter 15: Smalltalk/ V 286 Environment}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb364\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Doing and Showing}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb216\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 All text panes in the system support immediate expression evaluation via their pane\line \expndtw-5 menus. To \i evaluate an expression, \i0 you must first select it, then pop up the pane menu and\line \expndtw-3 select either the \i do it \i0 or the \i show it \i0 function. If you choose \i show it, \i0 the expression is\line \expndtw-2 evaluated and a character representation of the expression value is inserted in the pane\line \expndtw-4 after the evaluated text. If you choose \i do it, \i0 the expression is evaluated and the expression\line value is thrown away. Notice that only the selected text is evaluated; the other text in the\line pane is ignored. Extra blanks at the beginning or the end of the selected text are similarly\line ignored.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri11\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Any legal Smalltalk expression or expression series can be selected in a text pane and\line \expndtw-1 evaluated. Temporary variables can be declared as needed.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb349\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Compilation Errors}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri7\sb212\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 When you select and evaluate an expression, \b Smalltalk/V \b0 compiles and then evaluates\line \expndtw-2 it. If it detects a compilation error, \b Smalltalk/V \b0 inserts an error message in the source\line \expndtw1 code at the point of error. To fix the error, simply edit the text in the window, and\line \expndtw-2 evaluate the expression again.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb353\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Making Command Templates}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri7\sb216\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 You do not need to type the expression that you want to evaluate. You can edit some\line \expndtw-3 existing text in the pane and then select and evaluate it. This feature makes it possible to\line \expndtw0 build a window or even a file of useful expressions that you can edit as command\line \expndtw-3 templates to construct new expressions for evaluation. File sample.sml contains several\line \expndtw-4 useful expressions. You can use the Disk Browser to look at and evaluate the expressions\line \expndtw-1 contained in this file. These expressions all have comments explaining them.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri4\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 You can add to the expressions in this file (or make files of expressions of your own)\line \expndtw-4 using the Disk Browser. You can include comments with your expressions by merely\line \expndtw1 enclosing the comment in double quotes like this: "this is \b a comment".}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1318\margrsxn1926\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-18\shptop-1364\shpright-18\shpbottom1977\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-112\shptop284\shpright-112\shpbottom896\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1051\fi0\ri0\sb356\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Prompters}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li1040\fi0\ri11\sb216\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Prompters \b0 are a special kind of text editing window that appear on the screen when you\line \expndtw-1 request something that requires additional information. The label of a Prompter is a\line \expndtw-3 message called a prompt, which tells you what information \b Smalltalk/V \b0 needs to finish\line \expndtw-2 the operation. You enter your response into a single text pane of the Prompter. Often a\line \expndtw0 default response appears in the text pane as shown in Figure 15.8.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1951\margrsxn2300\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx4277\posnegy0\absw0\absh-205\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 13: Smalltalk/ V 286 Environment    277}\par \pard \plain \li2380\ri317\sb389\sa0{\pict\picw8750\pich4648\picwgoal4960\pichgoal2635\jpegblip
}\par\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li436\fi0\ri0\sb292\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 15.8\line \expndtw-3 Prompter}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li32\fi0\ri0\sb374\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The text editor used by a Prompter is the same as the text editor described under \b Text\line \expndtw-1 Editor \b0 above, except for the following differences:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li25\fi0\ri4\sb155\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Smalltalk/V \b0 uses Prompters to request a single piece of information from you. You\line \expndtw-2 must answer the request or tell \b Smalltalk/V \b0 that you want to cancel whatever operation\line is requesting the information. Since you must respond to the request, \b Smalltalk/V \b0 will\line \expndtw0 not deactivate the prompter window until you do so. In addition, a Prompter has no\line \expndtw1 window menu. \b Smalltalk/V \b0 will beep if you press the \b window menu \b0 key.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li18\fi0\ri11\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The pane menu of a Prompter (which you pop up by pressing the \b pane menu \b0 key) gives\line \expndtw-5 you two choices which are specific to Prompters. When you select the \i accept \i0 function, the\line \expndtw-3 Prompter sends the text in the pane to the requestor of the information. When you select\line \expndtw-4 the \i cancel \i0 function, the Prompter sends nil to the requestor. The requestor will cancel the\line \expndtw-3 operation. Pressing the \b return \b0 key is the same as selecting the \i accept \i0 function from the\line \expndtw-4 pane menu. After the request is answered, either by accepting or canceling, the prompter\line window disappears.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb378\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 The System Dictionary}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri22\sb234\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 There is a class in \b Smalltalk/V \b0 known as SystemDictionary. There is only one instance\line \expndtw-3 of this class, the \b System Dictionary. \b0 The System Dictionary defines methods for\line \expndtw-4 system-oriented functions such as compressing the \b change log \b0 and determining available\line memory. It also contains all of the names known globally in the system. This includes the\line \expndtw-3 names of the classes, global variables, and pool dictionaries. The System Dictionary is\line \expndtw-4 referred to in Smalltalk code with the name \b Smalltalk \b0 which identifies a global variable.\line \expndtw-2 All global variable names must begin with a capital letter. An example of a message to\line \expndtw-1 the System Dictionary is the following expression:}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2401\margrsxn1883\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li22\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 278    Chapter 15: Smalltalk/ V 286 Environment}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb302\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Smalltalk unusedMemory}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb144\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 This computes the number of bytes of available memory in your system.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri11\sb144\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 This chapter describes the System Dictionary and some of the system commands\line \expndtw0 (messages) that are sent to it.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb356\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 System Dictionary Contents}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li14\fi0\ri4\sb212\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The System Dictionary contains all of the names of the classes, global variables and pool\line \expndtw-3 dictionaries in the system. In addition, as you define classes, global variables, and pool\line \expndtw0 dictionaries, their names are added to the System Dictionary.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri0\sb158\sa29\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 For the classes present in the dictionary, the key is the class name and the value is the class\line \expndtw-3 itself. For the global variables present in the dictionary, the key is the variable name and\line \expndtw-4 the value is an object. If the variable has been defined but not initialized, its value is nil.\line Some of the more important global variables present in the system are listed below, along\line \expndtw-1 with their values and a brief description. The pool dictionaries are explained in more\line \expndtw2 detail at the end of this chapter.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2807\margrsxn1901\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1735\colsr943\colno2\colw4521 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Variable\line \expndtw-4 Aspect}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb378\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 CharacterConstants}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb662\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 CurrentEvent}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb270\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 CurrentProcess\line \expndtw-9 Cursor}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb47\sa0\sl-673\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Disk}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-673\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Display}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-673\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 FunctionKeys}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb144\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Description}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb184\sa0\sl-245\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A Fraction \b0 which contains the aspect ratio of your\line \expndtw-8 display.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb187\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A pool dictionary. \b CharacterConstants \b0 associate\line \expndtw-2 names with special character values such as:\line carriage return, line feed, escape, form feed, etc.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb187\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 An \b InputEvent \b0 used by the environment for\line reading all keyboard and mouse events.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb176\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The \b Process \b0 that is currently running.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri256\sb194\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A \b CursorManager \b0 used to store the location of\line \expndtw-1 the cursor.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb194\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A \b Directory. \b0 The current directory when the\line system is booted.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb191\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A DisplayScreen \b0 which is used to access the video\line screen as a form.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri248\sb198\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A pool dictionary. This dictionary defines names\line \expndtw-4 for keyboard function key values and for mouse\line \expndtw-1 input codes.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2005\margrsxn2290\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4212\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa540 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 15: Smalltalk/ V 286 Environment    279}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2394\margrsxn2337\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1890\colsr788\colno2\colw4500 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-436\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Variable\line \expndtw-9 KeyboardSemaphore}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb472\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Processor\line \expndtw-7 Scheduler}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb709\sa0\sl-443\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Smalltalk\line Sources}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb515\sa0\sl-680\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 SysFont}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-680\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Terminal}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-680\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Transcript}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb155\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Description}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb187\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A Semaphore \b0 that is signaled every time there is a\line \expndtw-3 keyboard or mouse interrupt. \b CurrentEvent \b0 waits\line \expndtw-2 on this Semaphore.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb169\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The \b ProcessScheduler \b0 of the system.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb194\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A \b DispatchManager \b0 which manages the\line \expndtw-1 scheduling of windows. \b Scheduler \b0 should be the\line only instance of class \b DispatchManager \b0 in the\line \expndtw-7 system.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb180\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The \b SystemDictionary.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb194\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 An Array \b0 containing two file streams for accessing\line \expndtw1 the source code of \b Smalltalk/V. \b0 The first entry is\line \expndtw0 the \b source \b0 file. The second entry is the \b change\line \expndtw1 log \b0 file.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb191\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The default \b Font \b0 used for the current graphics\line \expndtw-4 resolution.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A TerminalStream \b0 which is used for reading the\line \expndtw-1 keyboard and mouse, if any.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb198\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A TextEditor \b0 which is the System Transcript.\line \b\expndtw-3 Transcript \b0\i is \i0 used primarily for system messages.\line \expndtw0 The user can also send his messages to it (e.g., for\line \expndtw-3 debugging traces).}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2005\margrsxn2290\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb356\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 System Dictionary Methods}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb209\sa169\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 There are many useful functions or methods which operate on the System Dictionary.\line \expndtw-3 They include:}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2404\margrsxn2539\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1760\colsr911\colno2\colw4294 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb11\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Method}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb176\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 at: \i key \i0 put: \i anObject}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Description}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri0\sb194\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Creates a new global variable, \i key, \i0 with the value\line \i anObject. \i0 If the global variable exists, changes its\line \expndtw-7 value to \i anObject.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2407\margrsxn1863\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa364 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 280    Chapter 15: Smalltalk/V 286 Environment}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2803\margrsxn1903\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1746\colsr940\colno2\colw4518 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-436\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Method\line \ul0\expndtw-8 compressChanges}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb382\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 compressSources}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb652\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 implementorsOf:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li425\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 aSymbol}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb554\sa0\sl-677\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 keys}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-677\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 removeKey: \b0\i key\line \i0\b\expndtw-7 sendorsOf: \b0\i aSymbol}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb1296\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 unusedMemory}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Description}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb191\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Compresses the \b change log \b0 file, removing all but\line \expndtw1 the latest version of the methods.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb194\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Compresses the \b source \b0 file after updating it with\line \expndtw2 the latest version of the methods in the \b change\line \expndtw0 log \b0 file.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb198\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Returns a Method Browser containing all of the\line classes which define a method with the name\line \i\expndtw-2 aSymbol. \i0 This is equivalent to choosing the\line \b\expndtw0 implementors \b0 function on the method list pane\line \expndtw-1 menu \i of \i0 the Class Hierarchy Browser.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb191\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Returns all of the keys currently defined in the\line \expndtw-3 System Dictionary.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb194\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Removes the specified key from the System\line \expndtw-4 Dictionary.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb198\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Returns a Method Browser containing all of the\line \expndtw0 methods, and their corresponding class names,\line \expndtw-2 which send a message with name \i aSymbol. \i0 This is\line \expndtw0 equivalent to choosing the \b senders \b0 function on the\line method list pane menu of the Class Hierarchy\line \expndtw-8 Browser.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb184\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Returns the number of bytes free in the system.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2407\margrsxn1863\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb328\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex82\expndtw-2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Pool Dictionaries}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb187\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A dictionary contained in a global variable can be used as a pool dictionary.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb338\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 CharacterConstants}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa32\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 CharacterConstants \b0 is a pool dictionary associating names to special ASCII character\line values such as line feed and escape. The keys of this dictionary are descriptive strings and\line \expndtw-1 the values are the associated ASCII characters as shown below:}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2806\margrsxn3177\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1011\colsr1663\colno2\colw3250 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Key String}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Bell}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-12\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Bs}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb7\sa0\sl-436\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 ASCII Character}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-436\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Bell character (ASCII value 7)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-436\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Back space character (ASCII value 8)}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2050\margrsxn2220\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 15: Smalltalk/V 286 Environment    281}\par \pard\plain\fs2\sa544\sl-1\slmult0\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-230 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2023 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx6725 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Key String}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li544\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 ASCII Character}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-518 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2023 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx6725 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\f