rr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx180 \clvertalt\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx842 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx1123 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx1613 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2275 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx3045 \clvertalt\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx3326 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 chaoter.3}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 5193}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 86-87-16}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex111\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 18:27:12    \i i}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2329\margrsxn1922\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri22\sb346\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The \i directory order \i0 pane contains a statement telling you how the information in a\line \expndtw-3 directory is ordered when it is displayed in the contents pane. The pane menu associated\line \expndtw0 with the directory order pane gives you the choice of ordering the directory by date,\line \expndtw-3 name, or size.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri0\sb166\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The label bar of the Disk Browser displays other useful information. If the disk being\line \expndtw-1 browsed \i is \i0 labeled, the label \i is \i0 displayed between the brackets, [ and ]. The full path\line \expndtw-3 name of the currently selected directory in the browser is displayed. If no directory is\line \expndtw-1 selected, then only the device drive character appears. The numbers at the right side of\line \expndtw-2 the label represent the amount of free space on the disk. This number is automatically\line \expndtw1 updated as you use the browser.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb324\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex81\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Browsing Directories}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri25\sb209\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To \i select a directory \i0 to browse, move the cursor into the directory list pane and press the\line \expndtw0 select key when the cursor is on top of the directory you wish to browse. Smalltalk/V\line \expndtw-5 displays a list of file names in the file list pane (the right-hand pane) and a complete \i listing\line \i0\expndtw-1 of the directory information in the contents pane (the bottom pane). You can move the\line \expndtw-3 cursor or scroll the directory list pane and select a different directory any time you wish.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb133\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The directory hierarchy list pane menu has four selections:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri29\sb155\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Remove \i0 eliminates a subdirectory from the disk. You will get an error if there are files in\line \expndtw-1 the subdirectory}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri32\sb166\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Update \i0 allows you to browse another disk in the same drive. Selecting this function tells\line the window to update itself by rereading the directory structure on the disk. You should\line \expndtw0 select this function only after you have inserted the second disk.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2095\margrsxn2172\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Chapter 16: Smalltalk/ V 286 Standard Windows    293}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri25\sb310\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Hide/ Show \i0 expands the subdirectory hierarchy if the selected directory has an ellipsis (...)\line \expndtw-3 at the end, or hides the subdirectories if they are displayed. Note that the same effect can\line \expndtw-1 be achieved by merely clicking on a selected directory name.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri32\sb144\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Create \i0 makes a new directory as a subdirectory of the selected directory. When you select\line \expndtw0 this function, a prompter appears, asking for the path (directory) name.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb317\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex81\expndtw-2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Browsing Files}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri32\sb205\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To \i select a file \i0 to browse, move the cursor on top of the file name in the \i file list \i0 pane and\line press the \b select \b0 key. \b Smalltalk/V \b0 responds by displaying the file contents in the contents\line \expndtw1 pane. You can select another file to browse by selecting it in the file list pane.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri36\sb144\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The menu for the file list pane displays a variety of functions for files. The file list pane\line \expndtw1 is the top-right pane of the Disk Browser.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li32\fi0\ri0\sb22\sa0\sl-400\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Remove \i0 eliminates the selected file and its contents.\line \i\expndtw0 Print \i0 causes the selected file to be printed.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li14\fi0\ri22\sb126\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Mode \i0 permits you to change the system file mode bits (see your PC or MS-DOS manual)\line \expndtw-1 of the selected file.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li43\fi0\ri0\sb29\sa0\sl-400\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Rename \i0 lets you change a selected file's name.\line \i\expndtw-4 Copy \i0 duplicates a selected file in another location.\line \i Create \i0 generates an empty new file.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb274\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex79\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Editing Contents}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri11\sb194\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 16.2 shows the three menus for the file contents pane, the pane at the bottom of\line \expndtw-3 the window. Which menu appears is dependent upon what you select in the other panes.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri22\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 If you are looking at a directory, you can pop up the menu shown at center. The menu\line \expndtw-3 at left can be brought up only if part of a large file has been read into the pane. You can\line pop up the menu on the right if you have selected a smaller file. All of these menus are\line \expndtw-4 popped up by pressing the \b pane menu \b0 key \b (Smalltalk/V \b0 knows which one to use) or the\line \expndtw1 right mouse button.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li14\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 As you can see, the three menus share some common functions. The \i copy, cut, \i0 and \i paste\line \i0\expndtw-3 functions are the same as those used in normal text editing (described in Chapter 15). In\line addition, the \i do it \i0 and \i show it \i0 functions are identical to those previously described for\line \expndtw-4 Smalltalk expression evaluation. \i Save \i0 and \i restore \i0 have been explained under text editing\line \expndtw-5 as well.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2284\margrsxn2007\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li29\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 296    Chapter 16: Smalltalk/ V 286 Standard Windows}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2300\shptop504\shpright4813\shpbottom504\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri3488\sb518\sa176 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f17\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 SmalltalK/V Transcript}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2626\margrsxn2234\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1112\colsr1012\colno2\colw4924 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft1958\shptop-166\shpright4471\shpbottom-166\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft1958\shptop-324\shpright1958\shpbottom475\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 13970}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb2351\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure 16.2\line File Contents\line \expndtw-4 Pane Menus}\par \pard\plain\fs2\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\column\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-173 \clvertalc\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx1606 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\