0\sl-392\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-30\dn7\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs52 Part 4}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li511\fi-511\ri0\sb803\sa0\sl-864\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex88\expndtw-8\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs82 Encyclopedia\line \expndtw-6 of Classes}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2216\margrsxn2065\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri36\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Animation      311}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb342\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 Animation}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri14\sb209\sa29\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 An Animation contains a collection of pens representing objects being animated. Each pen\line \expndtw2 is moved by erasing its image from the old location and then displaying the image in a new\line location. The message interface is similar to class Pen except that a name must be given to\line \expndtw4 identify the object to move. Each pen in the collection behaves differently than a non-\line \expndtw1 animation pen, for example, the instance variable sourceForm of each pen contains an Array\line of Forms representing pictures in successive stages of a motion. These pictures are displayed\line \expndtw2 in a cyclical fashion for each BitBlt copy. The overlapped objects are displayed in the order\line \expndtw4 as they are entered into the Animation object. Thus an object entered first will appear to\line \expndtw5 always move behind the object entered later.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2223\margrsxn5561\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw2253\colsr367\colno2\colw1504 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb11\sa0\sl-436\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri