\li11\fi0\ri0\sb299\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 Association}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri11\sb198\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Association provides the means of associating two objects known as the key/value pair,\line \expndtw4 and defines the protocol to manipulate them. Association objects are often used as the\line \expndtw3 elements of class Dictionary.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2309\margrsxn1990\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx2621\posnegy22\absw1494\absh-882\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Magnitude Object\line \expndtw-2 (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb29\sa0\sl-436\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:\line \expndtw3 Inherited By:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-436\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Named Instance Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb50\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw19\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 key}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains the first object of the key/value pair. It is primarily used as a key to\line \expndtw1 retrieve the second object (the value) of the association when dealing with instances\line \expndtw2 of class Dictionary.\line \b\expndtw4\fs22 value}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains the second object of the key/value pair.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi-410\ri0\sb126\sa0\sl-320\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Variables:\line \expndtw-2 (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb191\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Pool Dictionaries:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2635\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb212\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb83\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 key: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer an instance of class Association whose key is initialized to anObject.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 key: \b0 aKey \b value: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer an instance of class Association whose key is initialized to aKey and whose\line \expndtw4 value is initialized to anObject.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb205\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Instance Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li414\fi0\ri0\sb83\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 <C anAssociation}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the receiver key is less than anAssociation key, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li414\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 ^ \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0 \'99\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0  anAssociation}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the receiver key is less than or equal to anAssociation key, else\line \expndtw1 answer false.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2036\margrsxn2241\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Bag      315}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li454\fi0\ri0\sb317\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 \'97\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0  \i0 anAssociation}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li817\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the receiver key is equal to anAssociation key, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li436\fi0\ri0\sb68\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 ^ anAssociation}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li814\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the receiver key is greater than anAssociation key, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li439\fi0\ri0\sb79\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 > \dbch\af3\loch\af1\hich\f1\cchs0 \u9632\'3f\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0 \'ab\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0  anAssociation}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li814\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the receiver key is greater than or equal to anAssociation key, eke\line \expndtw1 answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li418\fi0\ri0\sb68\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 hash}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li814\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the integer hash value for the key of the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li421\fi0\ri0\sb76\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw19\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 key}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li814\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the key of the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li421\fi0\ri0\sb83\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 key: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li814\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Set the key of the receiver to be anObject. Answer the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li414\fi0\ri0\sb50\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 print On: \b0 aStream}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li814\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Append the ASCII representation of the receiver to aStream.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li418\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 storeOn: \b0 aStream}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li810\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Append the ASCII representation of the receiver to aStream from which the\line \expndtw5 receiver can be reinstantiated.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb72\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 value}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li810\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the value of the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 value: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li810\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Set the value of the receiver to be anObject. Answer the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri14\sb767\sa29\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 A Bag is a collection of unordered elements in which duplicates are allowed. It cannot be\line \expndtw3 accessed through external keys. Bags are useful for containing arbitrary objects and for\line \expndtw4 counting occurrences of equal objects. Bags are hashed for rapid searching.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2047\margrsxn5809\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1224\colsr1390\colno2\colw1440 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb169\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb209\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherited By:}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Collection Object\line \expndtw-3 (None)}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2036\margrsxn2241\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb166\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Named Instance Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 elements}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li799\fi0\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains a Dictionary. For each key /value pair, the key contains an element of\line the bag and the associated value represents the number of occurrences of the\line \expndtw6 element in the bag.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li418\fi-418\ri0\sb130\sa0\sl-320\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Variables:\line \expndtw-3 (None)}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2401\margrsxn1890\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 316     Bag}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb313\sa0\tx2642 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Pool Dictionaries:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-2 (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb205\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw15\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 new}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer an empty Bag.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Instance Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 add: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer anObject. Add anObject to the elements of the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 add: \b0 anObject \b withOccurrences: \b0 aninteger}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer anObject. Add anObject to the elements of the receiver aninteger number\line \expndtw2 of times.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 at: \b0 aninteger}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the element of the receiver at index position aninteger. Report an error\line \expndtw4 since bags are not indexable.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 at: \b0 aninteger \b put: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Replace the element of the receiver at index position aninteger with anObject.\line \expndtw5 Report an error, since bags are not indexable.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 do: \b0 aBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 For each element in the receiver, evaluate aBlock with that element as the\line \expndtw3 argument.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 includes: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the receiver contains an element equal to anObject, else answer\line \expndtw-1 false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb65\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 occurrencesOf: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the number of elements of the receiver equal to anObject.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw12\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 remove: anObject \b ifAbsent: \b0 aBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer anObject. Remove one occurrence of anObject from the receiver collection.\line \expndtw1 If anObject is not an element of the receiver, evaluate aBlock (with no arguments).}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb76\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 size}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the number of elements in the receiver collection.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb292\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 Behavior}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri4\sb205\sa32\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Behavior is the abstract class that defines and implements the common protocol for\line \expndtw2 all the classes and metaclasses in Smalltalk. Behavior provides methods that support source\line \expndtw4 code access, compilation, object creation, and class hierarchy access.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2405\margrsxn5580\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1220\colsr1393\colno2\colw1310 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:\line Inherited By:}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb166\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Object}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb198\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class MetaClass}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2036\margrsxn2252\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 Behavior      317}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb302\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Named Instance Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 comment}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi392\ri0\sb11\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 This is reserved for future use.\line \b\expndtw-2 dictionary Array}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi396\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Contains an Array of method dictionaries, in message lookup order.\line \b\expndtw5 instances}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Contains an Array of instance variable names defined by this class. The names are}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi392\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 stored as strings.\line \b\expndtw4 name}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi389\ri0\sb7\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Contains the Symbol that is the name of this class.\line \b\expndtw2 structure}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Contains a Smalllnteger that describes the physical structure of instances of this}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi392\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 class. See the class variables of Behavior for the definition of the encoding.\line \b\expndtw5 subclasses}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi389\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Contains an Array of all the subclasses of this class.\line \b\expndtw7 superclass}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Contains the superclass of this class.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb184\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Class Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 InstlndexedBit}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li796\fi0\ri14\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Contains a Smalllnteger which, when logically ANDed with the instance variable\line \expndtw-5 structure, determines whether or not an instance of the class can have indexed\line \expndtw-3 instance variables. The value contained is 8192.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Ins tNumber Mask}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li796\fi0\ri11\sb4\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Contains a Smalllnteger which, when logically ANDed with the instance variable\line \expndtw-3 structure, determines the number of named instance variables for each instance\line of the class. The value contained is 127.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 InstPointerBit}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li785\fi0\ri14\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Contains a Smalllnteger which, when logically ANDed with the instance variable\line \expndtw-2 structure, determines whether or not an instance of the class contains object\line pointers in their instance variables. The value contained is 16384.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb40\sa0\sl-436\slmult0\tx2632 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Pool Dictionaries:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-11 (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-436\slmult0\tx2632 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Class Methods:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-6 (All private)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-436\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Instance Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb50\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 addSelector: \b0 aSymbol \b withMethod: \b0 aCompiledMethod}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li792\fi0\ri14\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Add aCompiledMethod to the receiver messageDictionary using aSymbol as the\line \expndtw-2 key. If aSymbol is not a Symbol report an error.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 addSubclass: \b0 aClass}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li792\fi0\ri14\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Add aClass to the subclasses of the receiver. Make the the receiver the superclass\line \expndtw-9 of aClass.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb72\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 allClasses}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer a Set of all of the classes contained in Smalltalk.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2362\margrsxn1941\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 318      Behavior}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb338\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 allClassVarNames}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a Set of strings of all of the class variable names defined in the receiver\line and its superclasses.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 alllnstances}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer an Array of all of the instances of the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 alllnstVarNames}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li792\fi0\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer an Array of strings of all of the instance variable names defined in the\line receiver and its superclasses.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb83\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 allSubclasses}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer an OrderedCollection of all the subclasses of the receiver in hierarchical\line \expndtw4 order. Classes at the same hierarchical level are sorted alphabetically.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 allSuperclasses}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer an OrderedCollection of all the superclasses of the receiver. The\line \expndtw4 superclasses are in inverse hierarchical order, i.e class Object is last.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 canUnderstand: \b0 aSymbol}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li792\fi0\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the receiver or any of the receiver superclasses implement the\line \expndtw4 method named aSymbol, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb79\sa0\sl-223\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 classVariableString}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li788\fi0\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-223\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a String of all the class variable names defined by the receiver. The names\line \expndtw4 are separated with blanks.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 compile: \b0 codeString}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Compile the Smalltalk method contained in codeString. The class to use for\line \expndtw3 resolving variables is the receiver. If there are no errors, add the method to the\line \expndtw2 receiver messageDictionary and answer the Association with the message selector\line \expndtw4 as the key and the compiled method as the value. If there is an error, answer nil.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 compile: \b0 codeString \b notifying: \b0 requestor}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li785\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Compile the Smalltalk method contained in codeString. The class to use for\line \expndtw3 resolving variables is the receiver. If there are no errors, add the method to the\line \expndtw2 recevier messageDictionary and answer the Association with the message selector\line \expndtw3 as the key and the compiled method as the value. If there is an error the requestor\line is sent a message by the compiler identitfying the error and this method answers\line \expndtw0 nil.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb76\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 compiledMethodAt: \b0 aSymbol}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li785\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the compiled code of the method named aSymbol defined in the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li389\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 compile Logic: \b0 codeString}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li781\fi0\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Compile the Prolog method contained in codeString. The class to use for resolving\line \expndtw3 variables is the receiver. If there are no errors, add the method to the receiver\line \expndtw0 messageDictionary and answer the Association with the message selector as the key\line \expndtw6 and the compiled method as the value. If there is an error, answer nil.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li389\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 compile Logic: \b0 codeString \b notifying: \b0 requestor}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li778\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Compile the Prolog method contained in codeString.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2458\margrsxn2240\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 Behavior      319}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb331\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 deepCopy}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li396\fi0\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a copy of the receiver with shallow copies of each instance variable. Because\line \expndtw4 classes are unique (cannot be copied), answer the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb76\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 implementorsOf: \b0 aSymbol}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li396\fi0\ri7\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a collection of methods of myself and my subclasses that implement\line \expndtw1 aSymbol.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb83\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 includesSelector: \b0 aSymbol}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li396\fi0\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the message dictionary of the receiver includes a method of name\line \expndtw3 aSymbol, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb54\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 inheritsFrom: \b0 aClass}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if receiver can inherit methods from aClass, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 instance VariableString}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li396\fi0\ri18\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a String containing all the instance variable names defined by the receiver.\line \expndtw4 The names are separated with spaces.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 instSize}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi0\ri7\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the number of named instance variables contained in instances of the\line \expndtw0 receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb65\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 instVarNames}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the array of instance variable names defined by the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 isBits}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li389\fi0\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if instances of the receiver contain 8 bit values instead of object\line \expndtw3 pointers, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 isBytes}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if instances of the receiver contain 8 bit byte values, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 isFixed}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li396\fi0\ri14\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if instances of the receiver do not contain indexed instance variables,\line \expndtw2 else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 isPointers}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li396\fi0\ri11\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if instances of the receiver contain object pointers instead of 8 bit\line \expndtw2 values, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb101\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 isVariable}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li396\fi0\ri7\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if instances of the receiver contain indexed instance variables, else\line \expndtw1 answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb65\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 methodDictionary}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the dictionary of methods defined in the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 methods}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer an instance of ClassReader initialized for the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb101\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw14\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 new}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li396\fi0\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer an instance of the receiver. If the receiver is indexable, then allocate zero\line indexed instance variables. This method is frequently reimplemented as a class\line \expndtw4 message in classes that need special initialization of their instances.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1400\margrsxn1811\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-72\shptop8377\shpright-72\shpbottom9781\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-158\shptop9126\shpright-158\shpbottom10955\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1087\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 320      Behavior}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1483\fi0\ri0\sb335\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 new: \b0 anlnteger}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li1872\fi0\ri25\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer an instance of the receiver. Allocate anlnteger number of indexed instance\line \expndtw4 variables. If the receiver does not have indexed instance variables an error is\line \expndtw3 reported. This method is frequently reimplemented as a class message in classes\line \expndtw4 that need special initialization of their instances.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1480\fi0\ri0\sb72\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 print On: \b0 aStream}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1879\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Print the name of the receiver on aStream.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1483\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 removeSelector: \b0 aSymbol}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1883\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Remove the method named aSymbol from the methods defined in the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1490\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex116\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 selectors}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1883\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a Set of symbols of the names of the methods defined by the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1494\fi0\ri0\sb83\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 sendersOf: \b0 aSymbol}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1883\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a collection of methods of myself and my subclasses that send aSymbol.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1494\fi0\ri0\sb101\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 shallowCopy}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li1883\fi0\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a copy of the receiver which shares the receiver instance variables. Because\line \expndtw4 classes are unique (cannot be copied), answer the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1494\fi0\ri0\sb83\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 sourceCodeAt: \b0 aSymbol}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1883\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a String of the source code for the method named aSymbol in the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1490\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex116\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 structure}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li1883\fi0\ri7\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the integer that describes the structure of instances of the receiver. Refer\line \expndtw4 to the class variables of Behavior for a definition of this integer.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1490\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex116\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 subclasses}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1886\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer an Array of subclasses of the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1494\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex116\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 superclass}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1886\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the superclass of the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1490\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 withAUSubclasses}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li1886\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer an OrderedCollection of the receiver and all of its subclasses in hierarchical\line \expndtw2 order.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1105\fi0\ri0\sb292\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 BiColorForm}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li1087\fi0\ri0\sb205\sa25\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 A BiColorForm is like a Form except that it contains two additional instance variables,\line \expndtw0 foreColor and backColor. This enables the BiColorForm to take on two arbitrary colors rather\line \expndtw5 than just black and white. The foreColor is associated with 1 bits and the backColor with\line \expndtw7 0 bits in the bitmap.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2494\margrsxn3122\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1224\colsr1393\colno2\colw3675 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb180\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb209\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherited By:}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-443\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Form DisplayMedium DisplayObject Object\line \expndtw-3 (None)}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1400\margrsxn1811\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb1472\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex53\expndtw14\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 I !}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2172\margrsxn2116\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 BiColorForm      321}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb338\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Named Instance Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 backColor}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi389\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains an integer representing the background color (for 0 bits in bitmap).\line \b\expndtw3\fs22 bits}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi407\ri5260\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (From class Form)\line \b\expndtw-3\fs22 byte Width}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li403\fi407\ri5263\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (From class Form)\line \b\expndtw5\fs22 deviceType}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi407\ri5263\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (From class Form)\line \b\expndtw0\fs22 foreColor}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi392\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains an integer representing the foreground color (for 1 bits in bitmap).\line \b\expndtw5\fs22 height}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi410\ri5260\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (From class Form)\line \b\expndtw6\fs22 offset}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li403\fi407\ri5260\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (From class Form)\line \b\expndtw0\fs22 width}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li810\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (From 