 Append the ASCII representation of the receiver to aStream in the form: mmm\line \expndtw-4 dd, yyyy. (The form yyyy is satisfied only for positive year numbers of 4 digits).}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb54\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 subtractDate: \b0 aDate}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer the number of days between the receiver and aDate.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li414\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 subtractDays: \b0 anlnteger}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer the date that is anlnteger number of days before the receiver Date.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb54\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 year}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li806\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer the year number of receiver Date.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li22\fi0\ri0\sb284\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 Debugger}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri4\sb202\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A Debugger is a window application which allows debugging a Process in two different\line \expndtw-8 windows: a single pane walkback window and a six pane debugger window. The Debugger\line \expndtw-3 initially creates a walkback window. If requested via the \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0 \'97\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0 debug'*' menu choice, the\line \expndtw-10 walkback window is replaced with the debug window. The debug window allows the debugged\line \expndtw-5 process to be resumed from the point of interruption or restarted by resending a selected\line \expndtw-6 message. Traced execution can be controlled by hop, skip, and jump buttons in the window\line \expndtw-8 label.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb40\sa0\sl-439\slmult0\tx2628 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Inherits From:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-5 Inspector Object}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0\tx2642 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Inherited By:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-11 (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Named Instance Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb43\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 breakpointArray}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Contains an Array of pairs of classes and selectors for methods which have}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi396\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 breakpoints set.\line \b\expndtw4 breakpoints}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi392\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Contains a SortedCollection of methods which have breakpoints set.\line \b\expndtw0 browse Walkback}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi396\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Contains true if browsing the walkback and false if browsing breakpoints.\line \b\expndtw9 instlndex}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi407\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 (From class Inspector)\line \b\expndtw2 instList}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi410\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\ex