0 \u9632\'3f\u9632\'3f\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0  aDirectory}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li785\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if aDirectory represents the same directory as the receiver, else answer\line \expndtw-1 false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb65\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 create}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li785\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Create a DOS directory on disk for the receiver directory.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 drive}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the disk drive letter of the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 drive: \b0 aCharacter}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Initialize the drive for the receiver to aCharacter.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2111\margrsxn2191\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 DiskBrowser      361}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb349\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 file: \b0 aString}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a FileStream for the file named aString in the current directory. If the file\line \expndtw4 does not exist, it wiD be created.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 formatted}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a collection of arrays of file information for the receiver directory. Each\line \expndtw6 array has four entries: file name, size, date/time and attributes.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 freeDiskSpace}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the free space in bytes on the disk containing the current directory.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 hasSubdirectory}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the receiver has a subdirectory.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb54\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 makeCurrent}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Make the receiver the current DOS directory.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 newFile: \b0 aString}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a FileStream for the file named aString in the current directory. If the file\line \expndtw5 exists, it will be removed and a new file will be created.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 pathName}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a String representing the path name of the receiver directory (drive letter\line not included).}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb65\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 pathName: \b0 aString}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Set the receiver directory path name to aString.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 remove}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Remove the directory described by the receiver from the disk.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 subdirectories}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li785\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer an OrderedCollection of arrays, where each Array contains the complete\line \expndtw6 path name and the file name of a subdirectory of the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 volumeLabel}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the volume label of the disk containing the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb284\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 DiskBrowser}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri4\sb202\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class DiskBrowser implements a window on the complete directory hierarchy on a disk. It\line \expndtw3 replaces most DOS file commands. Directories can be created, deleted and browsed. Files\line can be created, deleted, copied, renamed, browsed, printed, edited and their attributes may\line \expndtw2 be modified.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb32\sa0\sl-439\slmult0\tx2617 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw1 Object}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0\tx2624 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherited By:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-2 (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Named Instance Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb18\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 allFileMenu}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains the contents pane menu when the entire file has been read.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2370\margrsxn1921\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 362     DiskBrowser}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb342\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 contentsPane}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi392\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains the TextPane used to display file contents.\line \b\expndtw5\fs22 device}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi392\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains the disk drive character.\line \b\expndtw0\fs22 directory Index}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi389\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains the index of the selected directory.\line \b\expndtw-2\fs22 directory List}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi392\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains an OrderedCollection of strings describing the directory hierarchy.\line \b\expndtw4\fs22 hiddenDirectories}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi392\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains a set of directories currently being hidden.\line \b\expndtw3\fs22 noFileMenu}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi392\ri0\sb7\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains the contents pane menu when no file has been read.\line \b\expndtw3\fs22 partFileMenu}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi396\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains the contents pane menu when part of the file has been read.\line \b\expndtw2\fs22 pathNameArray}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains an Array that parallels directoryList. Each entry contains the complete}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi378\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 path name of a directory.\line \b\fs22 selectedDirectory}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains a Directory for the selected DOS directory, or nil if no directory is}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi385\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 selected.\line \b\expndtw5\fs22 selectedFile}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi389\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains a String representing the selected file name, or nil if no file is selected.\line \b\expndtw0\fs22 sortCriteria}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains a block which describes how to sort the files in a directory: by name, size}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi392\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 or creation date/time.\line \b\expndtw0\fs22 sortedFileLJst}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains an OrderedCollection of arrays describing the files in the selected}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 directory. Each Array entry has four elements: the file name, size, creation date/}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi389\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 time and attributes (mode).\line \b\expndtw5\fs22 sortPane}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi396\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains a ListPane which describes the sort criteria.\line \b\fs22 volumeLabel}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi392\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains a String representation of the volume label.\line \b\expndtw5\fs22 wholeFileRequest}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains true if the entire file is to be displayed in the text pane, false if only the}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 head and tail are to be displayed.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li414\fi-414\ri0\sb133\sa0\sl-317\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Variables:\line \expndtw-2 (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb191\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Pool Dictionaries:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 CharacterConstants}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb7\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Defines variables for some of the most frequently used characters (e.g., Space for\line \expndtw5 the space character, Lf for the line-feed character, etc.).\line \b\expndtw4\fs22 FunctionKeys}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Defines variables for the function key codes (of class Character) input from the\line \expndtw3 keyboard or mouse.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2030\margrsxn2254\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li6502\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa144 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Dispatcher     363}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2037\margrsxn6516\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1522\colsr1112\colno2\colw720 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Methods:\line \expndtw2 Instance Methods:}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb173\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (None)}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2030\margrsxn2254\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb47\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 openOn: \b0 driveCharacter}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li806\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Open a disk browser window on the device identified by driveCharacter. Define\line \expndtw5 the type, behavior and relative size of each pane and schedule the window.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb281\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 Dispatcher}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri7\sb202\sa29\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Dispatcher is an abstract class which provides the common protocol for its subclasses.\line \expndtw2 Its main function is to provide default methods for processing input from both the keyboard\line \expndtw4 and mouse. It communicates with its associated pane to keep the pane contents up to date.\line It also provides the protocol for opening, closing, activating, and deactivating a window.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2037\margrsxn3132\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw2250\colsr360\colno2\colw4129 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:\line Inherited By:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb605\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Named Instance Variables:}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb166\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Object}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb205\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 GraphDispatcher ListSelector PointDispatcher\line PromptEditor ScreenDispatcher ScrollDispatcher\line \expndtw2 TextEditor TopDispatcher}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2030\margrsxn2254\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 active}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains true when the pane associated with this dispatcher is active and false when\line \expndtw4 it is not active.\line \b\fs22 pane}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains the pane associated with this dispatcher.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 WindowActivateKey}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains the first character to process when the window is activated and the\line \expndtw5 character is not nil.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb205\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Pool Dictionaries:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 CharacterConstants}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Defines variables for some of the most frequently used characters (e.g., Space for\line \expndtw5 the space character, Lf for the line-feed character, etc.).\line \b\expndtw4\fs22 FunctionKeys}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Defines variables for the function key codes (of class Character) input from the\line \expndtw3 keyboard or mouse.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw15\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 new}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a new initialized Dispatcher.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2417\margrsxn1893\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 364     Dispatcher}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb317\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Instance Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb119\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex131\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 activate}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Make the receiver active. Most subclasses supplement this method.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb79\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 activate Window}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Make the receiver window active by displaying it and then giving control to the\line \expndtw3 main processing loop for the active window.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb115\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex131\expndtw-3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 active}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the receiver is the active dispatcher, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb79\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw14\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 boxOfSize: aPoint}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a Rectangle with extent of aPoint and centered at cursor position.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex111\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 closelt}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li785\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Close the receiver window and resume the Scheduler main processing loop.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 close Window}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li785\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Close the receiver window and remove the receiver from the Scheduler dispatchers.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 cycle}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li785\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Deactivate the receiver window and cause the windows to rotate.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li389\fi0\ri0\sb68\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 cyclePane}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Move to the next pane in the receiver window.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 deactivate}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Make the receiver inactive.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb65\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 deactivate Window}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Mark the receiver to be inactive and change the pane visual cues to reflect it.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li389\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 display}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li785\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Display the receiver window.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li389\fi0\ri0\sb83\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 displayln: \b0 visibleRegions}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li785\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Display the portion of the pane of the receiver within visibleRegions.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 doesNotHandle}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Ring the bell for input not handled by the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li389\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 homeCursor}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li785\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Move the cursor to the receiver home position.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li385\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 isControlActive}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li781\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the receiver is active and contains the cursor. Some subclasses will\line \expndtw6 override and/or supplement this test.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li382\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 isControlWanted}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li781\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the pane contains the cursor, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li385\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 modified}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li778\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Indicate whether or not the contents of the receiver pane have been modified.\line \expndtw5 Answer fake as default.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2119\margrsxn2173\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 DispatchManager     365}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb292\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 open}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Open and activate the receiver window of default size.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb76\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 openln: \b0 aRectangle}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Open the receiver window as the active one in aRectangle.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb54\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 open Window}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Open the receiver window.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 pane}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the pane of the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb83\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw13\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 pane: \b0 aPane}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Set the receiver pane to be aPane and initialize the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb50\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 schedule Window}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Activate the receiver window.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 searchForActivePane}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li792\fi0\ri7\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Give control to the pane that contains the cursor. This is the main processing loop\line \expndtw3 for the active window.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb68\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 select}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Ring the bell since this function should be implemented by subclasses of this class.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 topDispatcher}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the top dispatcher for the receiver window.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb281\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 DispatchManager}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb205\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 A DispatchManager schedules windows by providing messages for adding and removing\line \expndtw4 windows, displaying all the windows, or making a specific window be the top one and\line \expndtw3 activating it. A global variable, Scheduler, contains an instance of class DispatchManager\line \expndtw6 and this should be the only instance in the system.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb40\sa0\sl-436\slmult0\tx2624 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw1 Object}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-436\slmult0\tx2635 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherited By:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-1 (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-436\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Named Instance Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb54\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 dispatchers}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains an OrderedCollection of dispatchers used to control windows. Windows\line \expndtw3 can be overlaid and the first one in the collection is always the top one displayed\line \expndtw4 on the screen. A top window may not be active, but an active window is always\line \expndtw5 the top one.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb68\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 None}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains a ScreenDispatcher which has control when no window is active.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1247\margrsxn1856\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw720\colsr468\colno2\colw7617 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb11207\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\