gin: \b0 aPoint}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Set the origin of the icon to aPoint.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2395\margrsxn1863\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 396     Icon}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li414\fi0\ri0\sb292\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 show}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li810\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Mark the icon as visible.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li414\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 width}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li806\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the width of the icon.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li22\fi0\ri0\sb284\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 IdentityDictionary}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri0\sb216\sa32\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 An IdentityDictionary is a collection of key/value pairs of objects. The keys in an\line IdentityDictionary are unique, whereas the values may be duplicated. It can be searched\line \expndtw1 either by key or by value. Key searches use hashing for efficiency. Elements may be entered\line \expndtw3 into and extracted from an IdentityDictionary either as a pair of objects (e.g., at:put:) or as\line an Association (e.g., add:). Internally, an IdentityDictionary stores the key/value pairs in\line \expndtw5 successive elements of the contents array whereas a Dictionary stores the key/value pairs\line \expndtw2 as a set of associations. For this class, two keys are equal when they are actually the same\line \expndtw0 object.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2395\margrsxn4110\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw2260\colsr367\colno2\colw2775 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx0\posnegy4198\absw7650\absh-2733\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a new IdentityDictionary.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx0\posnegy4198\absw7650\absh-2733\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 new: \b0 aninteger}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx0\posnegy4198\absw7650\absh-2733\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Create a new instance with an initial capacity of aninteger elements. This method\line \expndtw6 reports an error since the size of an idendity dictionary must be a power of 2.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx0\posnegy4198\absw7650\absh-2733\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Instance Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb83\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx0\posnegy4198\absw7650\absh-2733\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 add: \b0 anAssociation}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx0\posnegy4198\absw7650\absh-2733\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer anAssociation. Add anAssociation to the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx0\posnegy4198\absw7650\absh-2733\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 associationAt: \b0 aKey if Absent: aBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx0\posnegy4198\absw7650\absh-2733\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer an Association, with aKey and its corresponding value if aKey exists in the\line \expndtw5 receiver, else evaluate aBlock (with no arguments).}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:\line Inherited By:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Named Instance Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb50\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 contents}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi403\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (From class Set)\line \b\fs22 elementCount}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li814\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (From class Set)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li414\fi-407\ri0\sb133\sa0\sl-320\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Variables:\line (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb191\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Pool Dictionaries:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi-396\ri0\sb137\sa0\sl-313\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Methods:\line \b\expndtw15 new}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Dictionary Set Collection Object\line \expndtw2 MethodDictionary}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb2340\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (None)}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2014\margrsxn2274\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 IndexedCoUection      397}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb342\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 associationsDo: \b0 aBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the receiver. For each key/value pair in the receiver, evaluate aBlock with\line \expndtw6 that pair as the argument.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 at: \b0 aKey}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the value of the key/value pair whose key equals aKey from the receiver.\line \expndtw6 If not found, report an error.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 at: \b0 aKey \b ifAbsent: \b0 aBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the value of the key/value pair whose key equals aKey from the receiver.\line \expndtw4 If not found, evaluate aBlock (with no arguments).}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 at: \b0 aKey \b put: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer anObject. If aKey exists in the receiver, replace the corresponding value\line \expndtw6 with anObject, else add the aKey/anObject pair to the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 do: \b0 aBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the receiver. For each value in the receiver, evaluate aBlock with that value\line \expndtw4 as the argument.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 includesKey: \b0 aKey}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the receiver contains aKey, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 key At Value: \b0 anObject \b ifAbsent: \b0 aBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the key in the receiver whose paired value equals anObject. If not found,\line evaluate aBlock (with no arguments).}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb65\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 keys}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a Set containing all the keys in the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 removeKey: \b0 aKey \b ifAbsent: \b0 aBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer aKey. Remove the key/value pair whose key is aKey from the receiver.\line If aKey is not in the receiver, evaluate aBlock (with no arguments).}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 values}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a Bag containing all the values of the key/value pairs in the receiver\line \expndtw2 dictionary.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb295\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 IndexedCoUection}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri7\sb209\sa194\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class IndexedCoUection is an abstract class providing the common protocol for all the\line \expndtw4 indexable collection subclasses. It includes methods to concatenate elements between\line \expndtw2 collections, to replace elements of one collection with another, to iterate over the collection\line \expndtw0 and perform some block of code on each element. Indexable collections can be accessed using\line \expndtw3 integer indices.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2021\margrsxn5838\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1220\colsr1386\colno2\colw1443 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb7\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Collection Object}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2484\margrsxn1801\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa313 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 398     IndexedCollection}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2487\margrsxn2175\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1112\colsr1508\colno2\colw4626 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherited By:}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb7\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Array Bitmap ByteArray CompiledMethod FileHandle\line \expndtw0 FixedSizeCoUection Interval OrderedCollection Process\line \expndtw4 SortedCollection String Symbol}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2484\margrsxn1801\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb194\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Named Instance Variables: (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li414\fi-414\ri0\sb137\sa22\sl-317\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Variables:\line (None)}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2484\margrsxn6070\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1486\colsr1148\colno2\colw720 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb169\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Pool Dictionaries:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb209\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Methods:}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (None)\line (None)}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2484\margrsxn1801\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb169\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Instance Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb79\sa0\sl-223\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 , aCollection}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li796\fi0\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-223\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a new collection containing the elements of the receiver followed by the\line the elements of aCollection.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li439\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 = aCollection}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li796\fi0\ri14\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the elements contained by the receiver are equal to the elements\line \expndtw4 contained by the argument aCollection.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 atAU: \b0 aCollection \b put: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li796\fi0\ri14\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the receiver after replacing those elements, indexed by the indices\line \expndtw4 contained in aCollection, with anObject.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb79\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 atAHPut: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the receiver after each element has been replaced with anObject.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 copyFrom: \b0 start \b to: \b0 stop}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li796\fi0\ri14\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a new collection containing the elements of the receiver indexed from start\line \expndtw2 through stop.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 copyReplaceFrom: \b0 start \b to: \b0 stop \b with: \b0 aCollection}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li799\fi0\ri18\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a new collection containing a copy of the receiver with the elements at\line \expndtw2 index positions from start through stop replaced with the elements of aCollection.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 copyWith: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a copy of the receiver with anObject added to it as an element.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 copy Without: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a copy of the receiver excluding the first element that equals anObject, if\line \expndtw0 any.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 do: aBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li796\fi0\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the receiver. For each element in the receiver, evaluate aBlock with that\line \expndtw5 element as the argument.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw14\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 findFirst: aBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li792\fi0\ri14\sb4\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the index of the first element of the receiver that causes aBlock to evaluate\line \expndtw6 to true (with that element as the argument). If no such element is found, report\line an error.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2424\margrsxn2260\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 IndexedCollection      399}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb346\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 findLast: \b0 aBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi0\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the index of the last element of the receiver that causes aBlock to evaluate\line \expndtw6 to true (with that element as the argument). If no such element is found, report\line \expndtw5 an error.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 first}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi0\ri7\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the first element of the receiver. Report an error if the receiver has no\line \expndtw2 elements.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 grow}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the receiver expanded in size to accomodate more elements.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 includes: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi0\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the receiver contains an element equal to anObject, else answer\line \expndtw-2 false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 indexOf: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li403\fi0\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the index position of the element equal to anObject in the receiver. If no\line \expndtw4 such element is found, answer zero.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb101\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 indexOf: \b0 anObject \b ifAbsent: \b0 aBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi0\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the index position of the element equal to anObject in the receiver. If no\line \expndtw4 such element is found, evaluate aBlock (without any arguments).}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 last}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi0\ri7\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the last element of the receiver. Report an error if the receiver has no\line \expndtw2 elements.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 replaceFrom: \b0 start \b to: \b0 stop \b with: \b0 aCollection}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi0\ri7\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the receiver. Replace the elements of the receiver at index positions start\line \expndtw3 through stop, with the elements of aCollection. The number of elements being\line \expndtw4 replaced must be the same as the number of elements in aCollection, else report\line \expndtw5 an error.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 replaceFrom: \b0 start}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li205\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 to: \b0 stop \b with: \b0 aCollection \b startingAt: \b0 repStart}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li403\fi0\ri7\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Replace the elements of the receiver at index positions start through stop with\line consecutive elements of aCollection beginning at index position repStart. Answer\line \expndtw3 the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 replaceFrom: \b0 start \b to: \b0 stop \b withObject: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi0\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Replace each of the elements of the receiver at index positions start through stop\line \expndtw4 with anObject. Answer anObject.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb65\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 reversed}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a new object containing the elements of the receiver in reverse order.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 reverseDo: \b0 aBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li396\fi0\ri14\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 For each element in the receiver, starting with the last element, evaluate aBlock\line \expndtw6 with that element as the argument.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb72\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 shallowCopy}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a copy of the receiver which shares the receiver elements.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2462\margrsxn1844\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 400      IndexedColleetion}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb288\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 size}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the number of elements of the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 with: \b0 aCollection do: aBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 For each pair of elements (the first from the receiver and the second from\line \expndtw2 aCollection), evaluate aBlock with those elements as the arguments. The receiver\line \expndtw4 and aCollection must contain the same number of elements, else report an error.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb281\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 InputEvent}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb209\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 An InputEvent reads all keyboard and mouse events. The global variable CurrentEvent\line \expndtw2 contains the instance of InputEvent used by the environment. Events are requested by using\line \expndtw19 the message getNextEvent which waits on the Keyboards emaphore. The\line \expndtw4 Keyboards emaphore is signaled by keyboard and mouse interrupts.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb29\sa0\sl-439\slmult0\tx2624 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw1 Object}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0\tx2635 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherited By:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-3 (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Named Instance Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 button}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains a Smalllnteger corresponding to the mouse button currently depressed.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0\tx943 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 0{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw4 = no button, l = left button, 2 = right button, 3 = middle button. Shift key state\line \expndtw5 at time of button press is indicated by adding 4 if shift key was depressed.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 type}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains a Symbol describing the event type last read by the primitive. This\line \expndtw4 corresponds to the symbol returned by the getNextEvent message.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 typeArray}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains an Array of 5 symbols used by the get next event primitive to set the type\line \expndtw10 of the event. The 5 primitive events and the corresponding event types are:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0\tx943 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 1{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw2 = characterlnput,      2 = functionlnput,      3 = mouseMove,      4 = mouseButton,\line 5 = nullEvent.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 value}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains an object which is the value of the event. For mouse events it is the button\line \expndtw1 involved. For keyboard events it is the character or scan code of the key depressed.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 x}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb7\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains the x-coordinate of the mouse at the time of the event as a Smalllnteger.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb36\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 y}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains the y-coordinate of the mouse at the time of the event as a Smalllnteger.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi-410\ri0\sb130\sa194\sl-317\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Variables:\line \expndtw-2 (None)}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2462\margrsxn6095\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1483\colsr1148\colno2\colw720 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Pool Dictionaries:}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (None)}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2061\margrsxn2230\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri7\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 Inspector      401}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb310\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Methods:}\par \pard \plain \