 true if the receiver is greater than or equal to aMagnitude, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 between: \b0 min \b and: \b0 max}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the receiver is greater than or equal to min and less than or equal\line \expndtw3 to max, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb72\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 hash}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the positive integer hash value for the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb79\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 max: aMagnitude}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the receiver if it is greater than aMagnitude, else answer aMagnitude.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb79\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 min: \b0 aMagnitude}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the receiver if it is less than aMagnitude, else answer aMagnitude.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb288\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-12\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 Menu}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri4\sb202\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Menu defines the protocol for an application to present a menu of items to the user,\line allow the selection of an item, and then take some action based on the selection. Therefore,\line to define a menu, two ingredients must be supplied -- a String of menu items (separated by\line \expndtw2 line-feeds) to be shown to the user and an Array of action selectors to be invoked when its\line \expndtw3 corresponding item gets selected. A Menu is usually created by the class message\line \expndtw2 labels:lines:selectors:. It can be activated by either the popUpAt: or popUpAt:for: instance\line \expndtw-2 message.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb36\sa0\sl-439\slmult0\tx2621 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw1 Object}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0\tx2632 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherited By:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-3 (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Named Instance Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 currentLJne}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains an integer representing the index of the line in the menu where the cursor\line \expndtw1 is positioned.\line \b\expndtw4\fs22 frame}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains the rectangle that the menu occupies on the screen.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2592\margrsxn1721\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 412     Menu}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb328\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 hiddenArea}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\