00\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer aMethod. Enter aSymbol and aMethod as a key/value pair in the receiver.\line \expndtw5 Flush the method cache in case an old method has changed.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 remove \b0 Key: aSymbol \b ifAbsent: \b0 aBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer aSymbol. Remove entry with key aSymbol from the receiver. If aSymbol\line \expndtw0 is not a key of the receiver, evaluate aBlock (with no arguments). Flush the method\line \expndtw-1 cache.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2155\margrsxn2115\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 NoMouseCursor     417}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li25\fi0\ri0\sb284\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 NoMouseCursor}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri11\sb212\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 An instance of NoMouseCursor contains the bit pattern needed to display a cursor shape.\line \expndtw2 In addition, it contains the methods for managing the moving, hiding, and displaying of the\line \expndtw5 cursor. This class is used when there is no mouse driver loaded in memory. Thus the\line displaying and hiding of the cursor is done with Smalltalk code.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb40\sa0\sl-436\slmult0\tx2628 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw2 CursorManager Object}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-436\slmult0\tx2642 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherited By:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\