t0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Set the paneMenuSelector to the message selector contained in aSymbol which is\line \expndtw-3 used to generate the pane menu.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 model}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer the model for the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 model: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Set the model of the receiver to anObject and add the receiver as a dependent of\line \expndtw-5 the model.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 paneScanner}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Answer the Characters canner associated with the pane.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 popUp: \b0 aMenu}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Display aMenu at the cursor and perform the menu selection.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 popUp: \b0 aMenu \b at: \b0 aPoint}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li403\fi0\ri14\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Display aMenu at aPoint. If the user choice is nil, do nothing. If the model can\line \expndtw-3 respond to the choice, let it perform the choice. Else, let the dispatcher perform\line \expndtw-6 it.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb65\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 release}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Remove model dependency and disconnect the model from the pane.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 superpane: \b0 aPane}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Set the receiver superpane to aPane.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 unzoom}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Return zoomed pane to normal.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2342\margrsxn1953\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 432      Pattern}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb274\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 Pattern}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri4\sb212\sa198\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 An instance of Pattern contains a finite state pattern to be used to match against another\line \expndtw3 object. The pattern itself and the object to be matched against can be any subclass of\line \expndtw4 IndexedCollection. In addition, the Pattern class contains methods needed for performing\line \expndtw3 the match. There are two ways to invoke the pattern matching. One is to pass the entire\line \expndtw1 matching collection to the pattern. Another is to setup a loop and pass one element at a time\line \expndtw3 from the matching collection to the Pattern and a prebuilt block will be executed each time\line \expndtw2 a match occurs. The first way is more efficient when there is only one matching collection.\line \expndtw4 The second way is normally used when there are several matching collections.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2349\margrsxn6219\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1220\colsr1400\colno2\colw720 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb7\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Object}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2349\margrsxn5928\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\pard\plain \sb198\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2349\margrsxn5928\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1108\colsr1512\colno2\colw1011 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb7\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherited By:}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 WildPattern}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2342\margrsxn1953\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb198\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Named Instance Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex128\expndtw-5\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 fail}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains an Array of integers corresponding to elements in the pattern collection.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Each integer denotes the next element to go to when the current pattern element}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi389\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 fails to match the element in the matching collection.\line \b\charscalex115\expndtw-2 first}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains the first element in the pattern collection. This is used to increase}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi400\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 matching speed.\line \b\charscalex115\expndtw-3 input}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi389\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains the collection to be used as the pattern.\line \b\charscalex115\expndtw-2 matchBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains a block of code to be executed when a match occurs using the second way}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi392\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 of invoking the pattern match.\line \b\charscalex115\expndtw-1 state}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains an Integer denoting the current state of the pattern collection which is}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 the index of the current pattern element being matched.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb79\sa0\sl-223\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex109\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 WildcardChar}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa205\sl-223\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains a Character which when appears in the pattern collection will match zero\line \expndtw5 or more elements in the matching collection.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2353\margrsxn6208\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1476\colsr1152\colno2\colw720 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Pool Dictionaries:}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (None)}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2342\margrsxn1953\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb205\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 new: \b0 aString}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a new pattern with aString as the pattern to match.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb72\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex109\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 wildcardChar}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the wild card character.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2178\margrsxn2110\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Pen     433}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb320\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Instance Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 match: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li788\fi0\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Compare anObject against the pattern. If anObject completes the matching of the\line \expndtw5 pattern, evaluate the match block.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 match: \b0 aCollection \b index: \b0 anlnteger}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li796\fi0\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a Point representing the start and stop of the subcollection within\line \expndtw2 aCollection that matches the receiver starting at index position anlnteger. Answer\line \expndtw6 nil if no match.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 matchBlock: \b0 aBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li796\fi0\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Set the match block of the receiver to aBlock. This block will be evaluated when\line \expndtw5 the pattern is fully matched.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 reset}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Reset the receiver to start matching at the beginning of the pattern.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li22\fi0\ri0\sb259\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 Pen}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri4\sb205\sa32\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 This class extends the functions of BitBlt to provide a turtle graphics type of drawing\line \expndtw3 interface. The source form serves as the nib of the pen, the mask form the color of the pen,\line \expndtw2 and the destination form the canvas for drawing. It draws by repeatedly copying the masked\line \expndtw1 bits from the source form to the destination form. For each copy made, the destination origin\line \expndtw5 is moved according to the specified drawing pattern, e.g. a line or a circle.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2178\margrsxn5137\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw2250\colsr367\colno2\colw1976 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherited By:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Named Instance Variables:}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 BitBlt Object\line \expndtw2 Animation Commander}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2178\margrsxn2110\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb40\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 clipHeight}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi410\ri5224\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (From class BitBlt)\line \b\expndtw-4\fs22 clip Width}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi407\ri5227\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (From class BitBlt)\line \b\expndtw1\fs22 clipX}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li396\fi414\ri5224\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (F