\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 place: \b0 aPoint}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Position the pen at aPoint.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb79\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 polygon: \b0 llnteger \b sides: \b0 slnteger}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Draw a polygon with slnteger number of sides where each is of length llnteger.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb83\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex112\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 solidEllipse: \b0 aninteger \b aspect: \b0 aFraction}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Draw an ellipse with aninteger as half the width and aFraction as the aspect ratio\line with the pen position as the center, and fill its insides with the color of the mask\line \expndtw1 form.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 spiral: \b0 aninteger \b angle: \b0 dlnteger}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li799\fi0\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Draw a spiral with aninteger number of lines where dlnteger is the angle between\line \expndtw1 two successive lines.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb101\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 turn: \b0 aninteger}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li796\fi0\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Change the direction of the pen aninteger number of degrees, aninteger can be\line \expndtw3 either positive or negative.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 up}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Lift the pen up.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb83\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex112\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 white}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Change the color of the pen to white.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb288\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 Point}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 A Point represents a position in two dimensions (e.g., a character's position in a form). It\line \expndtw0 consists of a pair of numbers, x and y. By convention, x increases to the right and y increases\line \expndtw-1 downward.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb36\sa0\sl-439\slmult0\tx2624 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw0 Object}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0\tx2632 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherited By:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-3 (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Named Instance Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains a number representing the x-coordinate (column) of the point.\line \expndtw5 Contains a number representing the y-coordinate (row) of the point.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2144\margrsxn2140\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Point      437}\par \pard\plain\fs2\sa353\sl-1\slmult0\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-223 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2030 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3189 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Variables:}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-403 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2030 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3189 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li299\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (None)}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-432 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2030 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3189 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Pool Dictionaries:}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li486\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (None)}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-324 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2030 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3189 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Methods:}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li490\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (None)}\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb216\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Instance Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 * scale}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li792\fi0\ri11\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a new Point which is the product of the receiver and scale. Scale can be\line \expndtw3 a number or a Point. If scale is a Point, the x-coordinates are multiplied and the\line y-coordinates are multiplied.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li443\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw13\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 + delta}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li792\fi0\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a new Point which is the sum of the receiver and delta. Delta can be a\line \expndtw6 number or a Point. If delta is a Point, the x-coordinates are added and the\line \expndtw3 y-coordinates are added.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 - delta}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li792\fi0\ri14\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a new Point which is the difference of the receiver and delta, delta can be\line a number or a Point. If delta is a Point, the x-coordinates are subtracted and the\line y-coordinates are subtracted.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw14\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 // scale}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li792\fi0\ri14\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a new Point which is the receiver Point divided by scale. Scale can be a\line \expndtw4 number or a Point. If scale is a Point, the x-coordinates are divided and the\line \expndtw2 y-coordinates are divided.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw13\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 < aPoint}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li788\fi0\ri18\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the x and y coordinates of the receiver are less than the x and y\line \expndtw3 coordinates of aPoint, respectively, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li414\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw13\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 <\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0 \'99\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0  aPoint}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li785\fi0\ri22\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the x and y coordinates of the receiver are less than or equal to the\line \expndtw4 x and y coordinates of aPoint, respectively, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li428\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw13\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 = aPoint}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li785\fi0\ri18\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the x and y coordinates of the receiver are equal to the x and y\line \expndtw3 coordinates of aPoint, respectively, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw12\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 > aPoint}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li785\fi0\ri18\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the x and y coordinates of the receiver are greater than the x and\line \expndtw4 y coordinates of aPoint, respectively, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb79\sa0\sl-223\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw24\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 >\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0 \'ab\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0  aPoint}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li785\fi0\ri18\sb0\sa0\sl-223\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the x and y coordinates of the receiver are greater than or equal to\line \expndtw4 the x and y coordinates of aPoint, respectively, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw16\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 \\\\ scale}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li785\fi0\ri22\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a new Point which is the integer remainder of the receiver Point divided\line by scale. Scale can be a number or a Point. If scale is a Point, the x-coordinates\line are divided and the y-coordinates are divided.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2302\margrsxn1982\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 438      Point}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb320\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 aba}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a Point with coordinates that are the absolute value of the x and y\line \expndtw4 coordinates of the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw13\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 between: \b0 aPoint \b and: \b0 bPoint}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the receiver is greater than or equal to aPoint and less than or equal\line \expndtw4 to aPoint, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb65\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 corner: \b0 aPoint}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a Rectangle with origin equal to the receiver and corner equal to aPoint.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 dot Product: \b0 aPoint}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a number which is the sum of the product of the x-coordinates and the\line \expndtw5 product of the y-coordinates of the receiver and aPoint.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb65\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 extent: \b0 aPoint}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a Rectangle with origin equal to the receiver and extent equal to aPoint.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb54\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 hash}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the integer hash value of the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 isBefore: \b0 aPoint}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if receiver is text-wise earlier than aPoint, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw12\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 max: \b0 aPoint}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a Point with the maximum of the x-coordinates and the maximum of the\line y-coordinates of the receiver and aPoint.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 min: \b0 aPoint}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a Point with the minimum of the x-coordinates and the minimum of the\line \expndtw4 y-coordinates of the receiver and aPoint.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 moveBy: \b0 aPoint}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li806\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the receiver with its x-coordinate incremented by aPoint x and y-coordinate\line \expndtw6 incremented by aPoint y.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 negated}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a Point with the x and y coordinates of the receiver negated.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 printOn: \b0 aStream}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li806\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Append the ASCII representation of the receiver to aStream.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb54\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 rounded}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a Point which has the receiver coordinates rounded to integers.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 transpose}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer  a  Point  with  x-coordinate  equal  to  the  receiver's  y-coordinate  and\line \expndtw3 y-coordinate equal to receiver's x-coordinate.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb65\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 truncated}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a Point which has the receiver coordinates truncated to integers.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 x}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li806\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the receiver's x-coordinate.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2090\margrsxn2205\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 PoinlDispatcher     439}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb310\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw12\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 x: aNumber}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the receiver. Set the receiver's x-coordinate to aNumber.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 y}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the receiver's y-coordinate.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb76\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 y: aNumber}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the receiver. Set the receiver's y-coordinate to aNumber.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb277\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 PointDispatcher}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb209\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 A PointDispatcher is used to interactively define or modify a rectangle on the screen. The\line rectangle can be moved about the screen, be expanded or shrunk in size. A PointDispatcher\line \expndtw-1 answers a Point if only move is allowed and a Rectangle if resizing is also allowed. It is largely\line \expndtw4 used for moving or framing a window.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb29\sa0\sl-439\slmult0\tx2617 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw3 Dispatcher Object}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0\tx2632 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherited By:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-2 (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Named Instance Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb54\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 active}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi410\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (From class Dispatcher)\line \b\expndtw6\fs22 aPen}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi396\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains a Pen to draw the outline of the rectangle.\line \b\expndtw3\fs22 cursorOffset}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains a Point representing the offset between the display box origin and the}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi389\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 cursor.\line \b\expndtw2\fs22 displayBox}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi392\ri0\sb0\sa