b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the next object accessible by the receiver and advance the stream position.\line \expndtw6 Report an error if the receiver stream is positioned at end.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2201\margrsxn2094\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 ReadWriteStream      447}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb284\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 ReadWriteStream}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri14\sb212\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 A ReadWriteStream allows streaming over an indexed collection of objects for read and write\line \expndtw2 access. A stream has an internal record of its current position. It has access messages to get\line \expndtw1 and put the object (s) at the current position and cause the position to be advanced. Messages\line \expndtw5 are defined for changing the stream position, so that random access is possible.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb25\sa0\sl-439\slmult0\tx2617 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw6 WriteStream Stream Object}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0\tx2624 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherited By:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw6 FileStream Terminalstream}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Named Instance Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 collection}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi410\ri5105\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charsc