e most frequently used characters (e.g., Space for\line \expndtw5 the space character, Lf for the line-feed character, etc.).\line \b\expndtw4\fs22 FunctionKeys}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Defines variables for the function key codes (of class Character) input from the\line \expndtw3 keyboard or mouse.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb68\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 systemMenu}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the system menu.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb205\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Instance Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 activate Window}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Make the screen background active. Begin the loop to process input.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 execute: \b0 pathName \b parameters: \b0 aString}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Execute a Dos program whose file name is pathName and parameter is aString.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb54\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 executeCommands: \b0 aString Array}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Create the batch file to execute aStringArray as DOS commands.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 executeProgram: \b0 pathName \b parameters: \b0 aString}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Close files in use and temporarily exit to DOS. Reopen files upon return from DOS.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb79\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw-2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 exit}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Pop-up the exit menu.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb83\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 select}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Select outside all windows. Do nothing.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2316\margrsxn1972\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 452     ScrollDispatcher}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb281\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 ScrollDispatcher}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb209\sa40\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class ScrollDispatcher is an abstract class which processes scrolling related inputs from either\line \expndtw9 the keyboard or mouse. The scrolling commands issued from the keyboard are\line \expndtw2 straightforward. The scrolling caused by the mouse right-button are of two types: a move if\line \expndtw1 the cursor never goes out of the current pane while the button remains down; or a continuous\line \expndtw0 scroll if the cursor goes out of the pane while the button is down. A move slides the text from\line \expndtw2 the point where the mouse button is pressed to the point where the button is released. A\line continuous scroll moves the text by some amount continuously as long as the mouse button\line \expndtw1 remains pressed down and outside the pane. In this case, the scrolling direction is determined\line by the cursor position relative to the active pane (e.g., text goes up when the cursor is below\line \expndtw4 the active pane).}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2324\margrsxn3808\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw2250\colsr367\colno2\colw3160 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-436\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-436\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherited By:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-436\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Named Instance Variables:}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb162\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Dispatcher Object}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb194\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 ListS elector PromptEditor TextEditor}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2316\margrsxn1972\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb43\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex130\expndtw-3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 active}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi410\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (From class Dispatcher)\line \b\expndtw5\fs22 pane}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li810\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (From class Dispatcher)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 PageScroll}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains true if the scrolling amount is the pane height for vertical scrolling or a\line \expndtw1 half of the pane width for horizontal scrolling. Contains false if the scrolling amount\line \expndtw4 is one line vertically or four characters horizontally.\line \b\expndtw2\fs22 WindowActivateKey}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li810\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (From class Dispatcher)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Pool Dictionaries:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 CharacterConstants}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Defines variables for some of the most frequently used characters (e.g., Space for\line \expndtw5 the space character, Lf for the line-feed character, etc.).\line \b\expndtw4\fs22 FunctionKeys}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa205\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Defines variables for the function key codes (of class Character) input from the\line \expndtw3 keyboard or mouse.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2316\margrsxn6238\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1234\colsr1400\colno2\colw720 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Methods:}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\