ult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Add newObject after the element oldObject in the receiver. This method reports\line \expndtw5 an error since the sortBlock determines element order.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 add: \b0 newObject \b before: \b0 oldObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Add newObject before the element oldObject in the receiver. This method reports\line \expndtw6 an error since the sortBlock determines element order.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 addAU: \b0 aCollection}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer aCollection. Add all the elements in aCollection to the receiver in sorted\line \expndtw2 order.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb101\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 addAUFirst: \b0 aCollection}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Add all the elements of aCollection to the receiver before its first element. This\line method reports an error since the sortBlock determines element order.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb83\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 addAULast: \b0 aCollection}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Add all the elements of aCollection to the receiver after its last element. This\line \expndtw6 method reports an error since the sortBlock determines element order.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 addFirst: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Add anObject before the first element of the receiver. This method reports an error\line \expndtw5 since the sortBlock determines element order.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 addLast: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Add anObject after the last element of the receiver. This method reports an error\line \expndtw5 since the sortBlock determines element order.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2009\margrsxn2272\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 Stream      457}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb338\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 at: \b0 anlnteger \b put: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li799\fi0\ri7\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Replace the element at index position anlnteger in the receiver collection with\line \expndtw4 anObject. This method reports an error since the sortBlock determines element\line \expndtw1 order.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb101\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 copyFrom: \b0 beginning \b to: \b0 end}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li796\fi0\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a SortedCollection containing the elements of the receiver from index\line \expndtw4 position beginning through index position end.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 sortBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the block that determines sort ordering for the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 sortBlock: \b0 aBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li806\fi0\ri11\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the receiver. Set the sort block for the receiver to aBlock and resort the\line \expndtw0 receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb292\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 Stream}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri11\sb205\sa32\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Stream and its subclasses are used for accessing files, devices and internal objects as\line \expndtw4 a sequence of characters or other objects. A stream has an internal record of its current\line \expndtw3 position. It has access messages to get or put the object(s) at the current position and cause\line \expndtw2 the position to be advanced. Messages are defined for changing the stream position, so that\line \expndtw3 random access is possible.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2023\margrsxn3650\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1220\colsr1386\colno2\colw3628 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:\line Inherited By:}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb173\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Object}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa0\sl-223\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 FileStream ReadStream ReadWriteStream\line Terminals tream WriteStream}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2009\margrsxn2272\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb212\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Named Instance Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 collection}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains the indexed collection being streamed over. For FileStreams, it contains}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi400\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 the file page buffer string.\line \b\fs22 position}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li410\fi392\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains an integer representing the current stream position.\line \b\expndtw1\fs22 readLimit}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains an integer representing the current number of elements in the stream.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li421\fi-410\ri0\sb126\sa0\sl-320\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Variables:\line \expndtw-2 (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb187\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Pool Dictionaries:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li414\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 CharacterConstants}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li806\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Defines variables for some of the most frequently used characters (e.g., Space for\line \expndtw5 the space character, Lf for the line-feed character, etc.).}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2268\margrsxn2041\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 458      Stream}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb324\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 on: \b0 anlndexedCollection}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a new instance of the receiver on anlndexedCollection.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb198\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Instance Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 atEnd}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li788\fi0\ri0\sb18\sa0\sl-209\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the receiver is positioned at the end (beyond the last object), else\line \expndtw1 answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb65\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 close}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li785\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Close the stream. Do nothing for non-file streams.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb54\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 contents}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li788\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the collection over which the receiver is streaming.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb72\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 copyFrom: \b0 firstlndex \b to: \b0 lastlndex}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li778\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the subcollection of the collection over which the receiver is streaming,\line \expndtw5 from firstlndex to lastlndex.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li389\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 countBlanks}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li778\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Skip over blank and tab characters. Answer the number of character positions\line \expndtw6 skipped, counting 1 for blanks and 4 for tabs.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li385\fi0\ri0\sb76\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 do: \b0 aBlock}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li778\fi0\ri0\sb18\sa0\sl-209\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Evaluate aBlock once for each element in the receiver, from the current position\line \expndtw6 to the end.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li382\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-223\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex114\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 fileln}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li774\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-223\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Read and execute the Smalltalk source code chunks from the receiver. If a chunk\line \expndtw5 starts with ! send it the message filelnFrom: self}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li378\fi0\ri0\sb54\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 isEmpty}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li774\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the receiver stream contains no elements, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li378\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 lineDelimiter}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li770\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the default line delimiter, line-feed.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li374\fi0\ri0\sb54\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 lineDelimiter: \b0 aCharacter}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li767\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Change the line delimiter character to aCharacter. Ignore for non-file streams.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li371\fi0\ri0\sb76\sa0\sl-223\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw12\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 next: \b0 anlnteger}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li763\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-223\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the next anlnteger number of items from the receiver, returned in a\line \expndtw4 collection of the same species as the collection being streamed over.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li364\fi0\ri0\sb72\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 next: \b0 anlnteger \b put: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li760\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer anObject. Put anObject to the receiver stream anlnteger number of times.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li360\fi0\ri0\sb68\sa0\sl-223\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 nextChunk}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li752\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-223\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a String up to '!', undoubling embedded !'s. Trailing white space is skipped.\line \expndtw5 The methods in sources.sml and change.log are in chunk format.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2365\margrsxn2315\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 Stream      459}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb331\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex116\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 nextChunkPut: \b0 aString}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Output aString terminated with '!', doubling embedded !'s and replacing groups of\line leading blanks with tabs. Destination is receiver stream. The methods in sources,\line \expndtw5 sml and change.log are in chunk format.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex116\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 nextLine}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li403\fi0\ri14\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a String consisting of the characters of the receiver up to the next line\line delimiter.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex116\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 nextMatchFor: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi0\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Access the next object in the receiver. Answer true if it equals anObject, else answer\line \expndtw-2 false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex116\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 nextPiece}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li403\fi0\ri14\sb11\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 File sources.sml consists of compressed sequences of characters called pieces.\line \expndtw5 Answer a String containing the next piece of text to be compressed from the\line \expndtw3 receiver stream.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb104\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex116\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 nextWord}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi0\ri18\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a String containing the next word in the receiver stream. A word starts\line \expndtw5 with a letter, followed by a sequence of letters and digits.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex116\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 peek}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li396\fi0\ri18\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the next object in the receiver stream without advancing the stream\line position. If the stream is positioned at the end, answer nil.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 peekFor: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi0\ri22\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the next object to be accessed in the receiver stream equals anObject,\line \expndtw5 else answer false. Only advance the stream position if the answer is true.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb83\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex116\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 position}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the current receiver stream position.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 position: \b0 aninteger}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi0\ri18\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Set the receiver stream position to aninteger. Report an error if aninteger is outside\line \expndtw4 the bounds of the receiver collection.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex116\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 reset}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Position the receiver stream to the beginning.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex116\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 reverseContents}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li403\fi0\ri22\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a collection of the same species as the receiver collection, with the contents\line \expndtw4 in reverse order.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex116\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 setToEnd}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Set the position of the receiver stream to the end.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb83\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 show: \b0 aCollection}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li396\fi0\ri18\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Equivalent to nextPutAll: for streams. For text editor windows, causes immediate\line \expndtw3 display on screen.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb83\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex116\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 size}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the size of (number of objects in) the receiver stream.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2406\margrsxn1893\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\