ex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Show the gap selection if the pane has one.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 topPane}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li806\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the top pane of the receiver pane.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 update}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Update the contents of the receiver pane. Default is do nothing.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 update: \b0 aSymbol}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 If aSymbol is equal to the name of the receiver pane then update the contents of\line \expndtw4 the pane.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 update: \b0 nameSymbol \b with: \b0 aSymbol}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 If nameSymbol is equal to the name of the receiver pane then perform the selector\line \expndtw0 aSymbol.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 update: \b0 nameSymbol \b with: \b0 aSymbol \b with: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 If nameSymbol is equal to the name of the receiver pane then perform aSymbol\line with anObject as its argument.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb292\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 Symbol}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri25\sb202\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 A Symbol is a fixed size sequence of characters guaranteed to be unique throughout the\line \expndtw0 system. Hence, no copies can be made of the instances of this class and the existing instances\line \expndtw5 cannot be modified. Symbols are removed from the system through the cloning process.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2502\margrsxn2146\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1206\colsr1393\colno2\colw4662 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-544\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 468     Symbol\line \i0\expndtw3\fs20 Inherits From:}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb810\sa0\sl-212\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 String FixedSizeCollection IndexedCollection Collection\line \expndtw1 Object}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2491\margrsxn1837\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb198\sa0\tx2621 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherited By:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-1 (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 This class contains indexed byte values.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi-396\ri0\sb130\sa0\sl-317\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Variables:\line (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb187\sa0\tx2621 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Pool Dictionaries:{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-3 (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb205\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb72\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 mustBeSymbol: \b0 aSymbol}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li785\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Report an error if aSymbol is not a Symbol.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li389\fi0\ri0\sb79\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 new: \b0 ignoreArgument}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li781\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer an instance of the receiver. This method reports an error.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li382\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 purge UnusedSymbols}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li785\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Purge unused symbols from symbol table.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb198\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Instance Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li425\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 = aSymbol}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li778\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the receiver object is the the argument aSymbol, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li382\fi0\ri0\sb54\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 asString}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li778\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a String of the characters contained by the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li389\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 as Symbol}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li781\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a Symbol for the receiver. The receiver itself is answered since it is a\line \expndtw0 Symbol.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li385\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 at: \b0 aninteger \b put: \b0 aCharacter}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li774\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Replace the character in the receiver indexed by aninteger with the argument\line \expndtw1 aCharacter. This message is not valid for symbols, since they are not allowed to\line \expndtw-1 change.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li385\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 deepCopy}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li774\fi0\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a copy of the receiver with shallow copies of each instance variable. Because\line \expndtw5 symbols are unique (cannot be copied), answer the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li378\fi0\ri0\sb54\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 hash}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li770\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the integer hash of the receiver.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li371\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 print On: \b0 aStream}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li767\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Append the ASCII representation of the receiver to aStream.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li382\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 shallowCopv}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li763\fi0\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a shallow copy of the receiver. Because symbols are unique (cannot be\line \expndtw4 copied), answer the receiver.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2091\margrsxn2186\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 SystemDictionary     469}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li414\fi0\ri0\sb295\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 species}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li806\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer class String as the species of symbols.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li418\fi0\ri0\sb68\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 storeOn: \b0 aStream}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li806\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Append the ASCII representation of the receiver to aStream from which the\line \expndtw4 receiver can be reconstructed.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb288\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 SymbolSet}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri7\sb209\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 A SymbolSet is a set used to record all the Symbol instances. There is only one instance\line \expndtw2 of SymbolSet which is answered by the message Symbol symbolTable. The symbol set is\line \expndtw7 special in that entries are hashed and compared as strings rather than as symbols,\line \expndtw5 guaranteeing that all symbols are unique.}\par \pard\plain\fs2\sa238\sl-1\slmult0\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-302 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2412 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4414 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:}\cell \pard \plain \cbp