acters (e.g., Space for\line \expndtw5 the space character, Lf for the line-feed character, etc.).\line \b\expndtw4\fs22 FunctionKeys}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Defines variables for the function key codes (of class Character) input from the\line \expndtw3 keyboard or mouse.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb104\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex122\expndtw-2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 initialize}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li803\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Set up the standard window menu.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb83\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw23\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 menu}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer the standard window menu.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb212\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Instance Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li407\fi0\ri0\sb58\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 highlightLabel}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inform the top pane to highlight the window label signaling the active window.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2376\margrsxn1927\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 482      TopDispatcher}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb299\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 homeCursor}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li799\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Move the cursor to home position of the first subpane.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 isControlActive}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer true if the receiver is the topDispatcher and its window has the cursor and\line \expndtw5 the cursor is not in any subpanes, else answer false.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb86\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 label}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Prompt the user for a new label of the window and answer the label.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb284\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 TopPane}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri7\sb209\sa25\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 A TopPane is responsible for all the operations related to its entire window (as opposed to\line \expndtw1 operations related to the panes). For some operations (e.g., display window), it also invokes\line \expndtw5 subpanes in sequence to complete the work.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2379\margrsxn5883\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1227\colsr1390\colno2\colw1029 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-439\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:\line \expndtw4 Inherited By:}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-443\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Pane Object\line \expndtw-2 (None)}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2376\margrsxn1927\margtsxn1440\marg