pndtw2 to put the object (s) at the current position and cause the position to be advanced. Messages\line \expndtw5 are defined for changing the stream position, so that random access is possible.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2419\margrsxn2916\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1220\colsr1397\colno2\colw3956 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherits From:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb209\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Inherited By:}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Stream Object}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb202\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 FileStream Read WriteStream Terminals tream}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2412\margrsxn1883\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb205\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Named Instance Variables:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 collection}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li400\fi410\ri5105\sb4\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (From class Stream)\line \b\expndtw3\fs22 position}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li403\fi407\ri5101\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (From class Stream)\line \b\expndtw1\fs22 readLimit}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li403\fi407\ri5101\sb7\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (From class Stream)\line \b\expndtw-5\fs22 write Limit}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb11\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Contains the integer position of the highest position written in the collection being}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 streamed over.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li414\fi-414\ri0\sb137\sa0\sl-320\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Variables:\line \expndtw-2 (None)}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb187\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Pool Dictionaries:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb97\sa0\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 CharacterConstants}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa202\sl-220\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Defines variables for some of the most frequently used characters (e.g., Space for\line \expndtw5 the space character, Lf for the line-feed character, etc.).}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2412\margrsxn6145\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1231\colsr1400\colno2\colw720 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class Methods :}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (None)}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2375\margrsxn1926\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 WriteStream      489}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb328\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Instance Methods:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb65\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 contents}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Answer a collection representing the contents of the stream.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb72\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 cr}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Write the line terminating character (line-feed) to the receiver stream.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li389\fi0\ri0\sb90\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 nextBytePut: \b0 aByte}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Write the character whose ASCII value is aByte to the receiver stream. Answer\line \expndtw-1 aByte.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 nextFourBytesPut: \b0 anlnteger}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Write anlnteger as the next four bytes of the receiver stream.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb83\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw12\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 nextPut: \b0 anObject}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Write anObject to the receiver stream. Answer anObject.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb76\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 nextPutAU: \b0 aCollection}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Write each of the objects in aCollection to the receiver stream. Answer aCollection.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 nextTwoBytesPut: \b0 anlnteger}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Write anlnteger as the next two bytes of the receiver stream.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb94\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 position: \b0 anlnteger}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-216\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Set the receiver stream position to anlnteger. Report an error if anlnteger is outside\line \expndtw4 the bounds of the receiver collection.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb72\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 setToEnd}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li796\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Set the position of the receiver stream to the end.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li403\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 space}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Write a space character to the receiver stream.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li400\fi0\ri0\sb79\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw13\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 tab}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li792\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Write a tab character to the receiver stream.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn4561\margrsxn3241\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-734\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-48\dn1\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs80 Appendices}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2423\margrsxn1854\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs30 Appendix 1: SMALLTALK SYNTAX SUMMARY}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb680\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs26 How Syntax is Specified}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri11\sb227\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The formal syntax specification is presented using the Extended Backus Naur Formalism\line \expndtw-3 (EBNF) used in \i Programming in Modula-2 \i0 by Niklaus Wirth, Springer-Verlag, 1982.\line \expndtw0 EBNF is used here in order to precisely and concisely specify the syntax.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb133\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 What follows is a specification of EBNF syntax in EBNF. The syntax rules are:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li425\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 <rule> syntax = \{rule\}}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li425\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 <rule> rule = "<rule>" identifier "=" expression ".".}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li428\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 <rule!> expression = term \{"I" term\}.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li425\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw24\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 ^^ term = factor \{factor\}.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2203\fi-943\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1031\fs22  \lang1033 factor = identifier I string I "(" expression ")" I "[" expression\line \expndtw7 "]" \b0 I \b "\{"expression \b0 "\}".}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri14\sb148\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 An EBNF specification is a sequence of syntax rules. The right-hand side of each rule\line \expndtw-2 defines syntax in terms of other rule names and terminal symbols of the language.\line Parentheses, ( and ), group alternative terms. The vertical bar, I , separates alternative\line \expndtw2 terms. Brackets, \b [ \b0 and ], identify optional expressions. Braces, \{ and \}, identify\line \expndtw-4 expressions which may occur zero or more times. Character sequences in paired quotes,\line \expndtw-3 either double-quote " or apostrophe ', identify terminal symbols of the defined language.\line \expndtw-1 An \i identifier \i0 is a sequence of letters and digits beginning with a letter. A string is a\line sequence of characters from the defined language.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi0\ri0\sb148\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The following is an example in which possible meals are defined with a sequence of\line \expndtw-4 EBNF rules.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li414\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 <Crule> appetizer = "artichoke" I "oysters".\line \expndtw4 <rule> dessert = "ice cream" I fruit.\line <rule> fruit = "apple" I "orange" I "pear".\line <rule> meat = "beef" I "lamb" I "fish".\line \expndtw3 <rule> vegetable = "broccoli" I "carrots" I "peas".\line <rule> meal = [appetizer] meat ("potatoes" I "rice")\line \b0\expndtw-7 \{\b vegetable\b0 \} \b [dessert ]\b0 .}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb140\sa0 \f3\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Examples of meals defined by these rules are the following:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb151\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 beef potatoes}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li392\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f3\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 artichoke fish rice peas broccoli ice cream}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\